window.FWN_MESMERIZING_GHOST_DOCTOR_CHAPTERS=(window.FWN_MESMERIZING_GHOST_DOCTOR_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":4901,"title":"Chapter 4901: Hiding","paragraphs":["Yue'er didn't take Xiao Junheng's suspicions here entirely to heart. So by now, she had already returned to the very cave entrance where she had first hidden and was lying low.","The divine beast-level lion crouched beside her. Both human and beast peered out through the trees covering the cave entrance.","\"Master, will they find us here?\" The lion sounded uneasy. After all, the Xiao family had already dispatched search parties. Even if the younger generation hadn't located them, their elders would surely come hunting for it.","\"I don't know. If they come, we'll hide.\" Yue'er replied, then paused before calling out, \"Little Fox.\"","At her call, a small white fox appeared before her. It glanced at the lion before turning its gaze to Yue'er and responding, \"Master.\"","\"How's your spirit energy recovering? How much longer until you're back to normal?\" Yue'er felt a flicker of anxiety. After all, she too feared being captured by the Xiao family.","\"Master, it'll likely take at least ten days to half a month,\" the little fox replied.","\"Would the medicinal pills I gave you help? The ones Mother gave me—should I give you one?\" she asked.","The little fox shook its head, replying helplessly, \"Those medicinal pills are incredibly potent, but they're not quite suited to my current condition. If this place didn't have protective barriers and formations, perhaps drinking some spiritual elixir could help me recover. However, this is a floating immortal island, protected by barriers and formations set up by the Great Emperor. If I can't guarantee we'll get out safely, we'll inevitably be captured, so...\"","It dared not take that risk. Heaven knew it already regretted bringing its young master out of Yunxiao Mountain. If anything truly happened to her, it would be guilty of a crime deserving death.","Ten days? Half a month?","Yue'er gritted her teeth. \"Fine. I'll endure ten days or half a month. Remember to tell me the moment you're recovered.\" After instructing the little fox, she stored it back in her spatial pouch and took out another fruit to munch on.","Meanwhile, at the Phoenix Sovereign's floating immortal island, numerous Immortal Lords and Immortal Elders had gathered.","Ever since learning that the Great Emperor Northern Flame had been slain by this Empress, who had simultaneously seized his domain, they'd steeled themselves to pay their respects. Yet, despite multiple attempts, they'd been denied entry each time, never even catching a glimpse of the Empress herself.","After yet another rejection, groups of immortals retreated, murmuring sighs. One remarked, \"No one came to congratulate her when she ascended. Now we seek an audience, yet even after three attempts, we remain unseen.\"","\"Indeed, how we regret our earlier indifference!\" sighed another, his face equally resigned.<az4a0e> The latest_epɪ_sodes are on_the novel_fіre.net</az4a0e>","Meanwhile, Feng Jiu was not on the Immortal Isle either. After settling the three people she had brought back—Song Mi'er, Tie Song, and Yueniang—she departed alone, intending to visit the immortal isles of the other great emperors to assess the situation.","Though she suspected the other three Emperors wouldn't dare remain on their islands after the incident involving the Great Emperor Northern Flame, she still intended to make the journey. Even if she didn't encounter them, she would unleash a thunderous strike upon their islands to demonstrate her might.","It would also make them understand that she was always plotting to take their lives!","What she hadn't anticipated, however, was that they too had become vigilant. When she arrived outside one of the Great Emperors' immortal islands, she found its protective barrier array exceptionally powerful. Moreover, within the barrier, an ancient counterattack formation had been set up."]},{"number":4902,"title":"Chapter 4902: Approach","paragraphs":["\"Tsk, they really aren’t afraid to spend. This ancient formation may enhance defenses and grant counterattack power, but it also drains immense energy and spirit energy from its caster.\" She stood with her hands behind her back, suspended amidst the clouds, observing the rippling layers of air currents enveloping the immortal island ahead.","\"Very well, I’ll wait a little longer! You won’t escape anyway.\" She murmured softly, her icy gaze fixed on the immortal island ahead, a resolute, cold smile curling her lips.","Upon seeing the ancient formation here, she abandoned plans to visit the other two Great Emperors. Instead, she drew the flying feather from her waist and soared through the clouds. After a long flight, she spotted a town below and descended.","As she walked toward the city, she overheard passing cultivators murmuring about Yunxiao Mountain and the Azure Emperor. Keeping her wits about her, she slowed her pace to listen for a moment before heading toward an inn ahead.","\"Waiter, a superior room.\" Feng Jiu stepped inside, her gaze sweeping indifferently over the first floor patrons before glancing up at the second floor. She headed to the counter.","\"Honored guest, we only have one standard room left today. Perhaps...\" The proprietor, noticing her refined bearing and striking beauty, approached personally.","Feng Jiu noticed the crowd inside and how every pair of eyes had fixed on her since she entered. She frowned slightly and said, \"Never mind.\"","She would find another, quieter place. Just as she turned to leave, a cultivator stepped before her.","\"Fair maiden, how about this—I’ll give up my superior room for you!\" The male cultivator adopted a polite and courteous demeanor, bowing respectfully to Feng Jiu. Yet his gaze lingered on her, filled with astonishment and admiration.","\"No need,\" Feng Jiu replied coolly, stepping forward.","\"Ah, Fair...\" The cultivator took a stride to block her path again. Before he could finish, however, the stunningly beautiful woman shot him a cold glance.","That single glance froze him solid. A bone-chilling aura surged from his soles straight to his heart. Cold sweat beaded on his forehead. His outstretched hand involuntarily retracted. Uttering not a word, he merely stepped back, allowing her to pass.","Only after watching her disappear did the cultivator seem to come back to life, gasping for breath. Yet his eyes still held shock and fear as he pressed a hand to his chest. There, his heart pounded wildly, as if it might leap from his ribcage.","Terrifying... Who... who was that person?","Feng Jiu inquired on the street about the better inns in the city. She learned that a little further ahead, at a three-way intersection, there was a higher-end inn. It was rarely occupied, but its environment and views were excellent.","So she made her way to that inn. As soon as she entered, a waiter greeted her warmly.","\"Please come in, honored guest.\" The waiter led Feng Jiu inside, wiping down a table that gleamed with polish before saying cheerfully, \"Please take a seat and have some tea.\"","After Feng Jiu sat down, the attendant smiled. \"This is your first time here, isn’t it? Our inn is quite renowned in the city. We have several excellent guest rooms upstairs. Shall I show you around?\""]},{"number":4903,"title":"Chapter 4903: Prepares","paragraphs":["\"Just pick me a quieter room,\" Feng Jiu said, then asked, \"Waiter, I heard there’s a place called Yunxiao Mountain not far from this city?\"","\"Yes, it’s a place known far and wide. But you see, it’s quite mysterious—because it belongs to the Azure Emperor.\"","The waiter chuckled as he poured Feng Jiu some tea, then continued, \"The Azure Emperor is a carefree sovereign who pays no heed to worldly affairs. Though Yunxiao Mountain is said to be near the city, no one knows its exact location. Many who sought to visit it never found their way there.\"","\"Oh? Is that so?\" Feng Jiu exclaimed in surprise.","\"But there are those who know—only the powerful immortals or great lords who are close to the Azure Emperor. Ordinary folk simply cannot find Mount Yunxiao.\" The waiter spoke while accepting a tray of peanuts and pastries from another attendant. \"Guests, these are complimentary from the house. Please try them first. Should you require anything else, just call me. I’ll go upstairs now to check the room status for you.\"","With that, he bowed and withdrew.","Feng Jiu silently nodded in approval. The inn’s attendants were clearly well-trained, excelling in both hospitality and etiquette. Moreover, the guests here were unmistakably cultivators clad in brocades and jade robes. Though curious about her, they didn’t stare excessively. They merely stole a glance or two before withdrawing their gaze, showing no disrespect.","She sat in the inn for a while, drank two cups of tea, and ate a pastry before following the attendant downstairs to view the rooms. He had selected the innermost room for her, quieter and more secluded. Opening the rear window revealed distant scenery and street views. The room’s layout was tasteful—indeed, a rather fine inn.","After inspecting the room, she left the inn and wandered through the city. She bought some pastries and other snacks, and at a tailor shop in town, she purchased some necessities and clothing for each of the three children.","She thought to herself that since she was passing through here and so close to the children, she ought to visit them at least once. After all, since her ascension, she hadn’t deliberately sought news of them.","With the intention of visiting them, she bought items the children would enjoy and find useful. For their master, the Azure Emperor, she prepared two jars of her own brewed spirit wine as a gift. After dining outside, she headed back to the inn.","On the first floor of the inn, the proprietor, who had been waiting by the entrance, spotted the figure in crimson approaching. He hurried inside and approached a table, bowing respectfully. \"Young Master,\" he said, \"the lady in red has returned.\"","The white-robed man sipping tea paused, setting down his cup. He spoke softly to an elderly man beside him, \"Uncle Yuan, go see if it’s her.\"","The old man hurried to the doorway. His gaze naturally fell upon the stunningly beautiful woman in red. After just one glance, he swiftly withdrew his eyes, returning to the white-robed man’s side. He whispered, \"Young Master, it’s her. No mistake.\"","Hearing this, the white-clad man let out a faint smile. He stood up, stepped around the table, and waited by the door.","As Feng Jiu approached from afar, she saw two figures darting in and out of the inn entrance. She recognized the innkeeper, but the other elder was unfamiliar. As she drew nearer, she saw the elder she had glimpsed earlier standing beside a white-clad man.","She gave them a fleeting glance before striding past them, heading straight for the private rooms upstairs."]},{"number":4904,"title":"Chapter 4904: Seeking Treatment","paragraphs":["\"Ghost Doctor, please wait.\" The man in white spoke, his voice gentle yet enigmatic.","Feng Jiu, who had just passed by, heard his words. Her eyebrows arched, her steps halted, and she turned slightly to face the man in white. \"Do you know who I am?\"","Since ascending to the throne, few had actually seen her. Those who had knew her only as the newly enthroned Empress Phoenix Sovereign, rarely referring to her by the title Ghost Doctor.","\"I wonder if we may speak privately?\" The man’s gaze shifted toward Feng Jiu’s voice. His eyes were strikingly beautiful, yet they seemed too clear and pure, like glass, lacking any focal point.","Feng Jiu glanced at his eyes and knew immediately that he suffered from an ailment.","\"Yes.\"","Hearing her calm reply, the man smiled faintly, a hint of joy flickering in his expression. He gestured toward Feng Jiu and said, \"A private room upstairs has been prepared. Please.\"","Thus, guided by the innkeeper, Feng Jiu ascended to a private room on the third floor. The innkeeper personally delivered tea and pastries before waiting outside the door, awaiting instructions from within.","After taking a seat, the man spoke slowly, \"I am Yuan Jing. This inn is owned by my Yuan family. Due to an unexpected encounter not long ago, I had the honor of meeting the Holy Emperor. From him, I learned of the Ghost Doctor’s name. Since birth, Yuan Jing has suffered from an eye ailment, never having seen the world’s vibrant colors. His Majesty once mentioned to me that...\"that the Ghost Doctor possessed miraculous medical skills. If the Ghost Doctor were to treat him, perhaps Yuan Jing could see the colors of this world in his lifetime. Therefore, upon learning that the Ghost Doctor had appeared at an inn in the city, Yuan Jing took the liberty of coming to disturb you.\"","Hearing this, Feng Jiu glanced at him and asked, \"The Holy Emperor? Who are you referring to?\" She toyed with the teacup before her, thinking to herself that the Holy Emperor Yuan Jing spoke of was likely Mo Chen. Thus, she sought to confirm it.","\"The Holy Emperor’s full name is Nalan Mo Chen,\" Yuan Jing replied.","Hearing this, Feng Jiu tapped the tabletop lightly. She curved her lips, gazing at the man before her, her voice gentle yet tinged with nonchalance. So you’ve come seeking medical treatment? Did he not inform you that securing my assistance is no simple matter?\"","Yuan Jing paused briefly before replying, \"Yuan Jing is aware. I originally intended to pay a personal visit to request treatment, but I hadn’t anticipated the Phoenix Sovereign appearing here, so...\"","He paused again before continuing, \"I know the Phoenix Sovereign is a peerless Ghost Doctor, a great Sovereign of this realm. The Ghost Doctor lacks nothing. Yet, if it is possible, Yuan Jing still wishes to request the Ghost Doctor examine whether there is any chance of healing his eyes. If the Ghost Doctor can restore Yuan Jing’s sight, whatever conditions the Ghost Doctor demands, Yuan Jing is willing to fulfill them.\"","Hearing this, Feng Jiu smiled. \"Don’t speak so definitively.\"","\"Every word Yuan Jing speaks is true,\" he declared earnestly.","Seeing this, Feng Jiu smiled again, saying nothing but staring intently into his eyes, lost in thought. After a long moment, she finally said, \"Extend your hand.\"","Yuan Jing’s face lit up with joy, while the elderly man beside him grew even more excited, urgently prompting, \"Young Master, your hand! \"He swiftly lifted his young master’s hand onto the table, rolled up his sleeve, and watched Feng Jiu intently, too nervous to speak.","Feng Jiu placed her hand on his wrist and began her diagnosis in silence. After a moment, she examined his eyes.","Yuan Jing felt a pair of hands probing his eyes. Instantly, his heart leapt into his throat..."]},{"number":4905,"title":"Chapter 4905: There is a guest","paragraphs":["Chapter 4905: There is a guest","Feng Jiu withdrew her hand and asked, “A condition you’ve had since birth?”","“Yes.” He answered, his heart pounding.","“You’ve taken quite a few medicines over the years, haven’t you?” Feng Jiu asked calmly.","“Yes. I’ve sought out many physicians and medicinal pill masters, but all said there was no possibility of recovery. Ghost Doctor, I wonder if my eyes...” Hope blossomed in his heart, yet he feared it might shatter. At this moment, his mood was fraught with anxiety.","Feng Jiu tapped her fingers lightly on the tabletop, her gaze fixed on him as she pondered. After a long moment, she spoke: “In the deep sea dwells a creature called the Crimson-Eyed Spirit Fish. Extract its eye, preserve it in an ice box, and bring it to my immortal island. Remember—it must be an adult. Once you find the eye, I’ll attempt to treat your eyes then.”","Hearing this, Yuan Jing’s heart surged with excitement. “So the Ghost Doctor means there’s a possibility my eyes can be cured?”","“You could say that,” Feng Jiu glanced at him. “Provided you find that fish eye.”","“Yes, yes! I’ll definitely send people to search for it. Thank you, Ghost Doctor! Thank you!” His face flushed with emotion as he stood up and bowed to her.","“That’s all for now.” Feng Jiu rose and walked out, returning to her private room on the second floor to rest. She intended to question Mo Chen later about this Yuan Jing.","After seeing Feng Jiu downstairs, Yuan Jing turned to the old man beside him: “Uncle Yuan, did you hear that? My eyes can still be cured!”","The old man’s eyes glistened as he nodded. “I heard you, Young Master. Rest assured, I will have someone retrieve the eyes of that Crimson-Eyed Demon for you!”","“Home. We must return immediately. Have Father dispatch men to search for that Crimson-Eyed Demon at once.” He clasped his hand, his jade-like face radiating excitement and anticipation.","Seeing his excitement and joy, the old man couldn’t bring himself to tell him that the crimson-eyed demon beast was the most ferocious fish-beast in the deep sea. Especially the mature crimson-eyed fierce beasts were extremely rare, for each one took a thousand years to reach adulthood and hid deep within the ocean. The chances of finding one were truly slim.","But even if slim, it was still a hope, a lifeline. They couldn’t give up!","The next morning, Feng Jiu left the inn early, passed through the city gates, and set off toward Yunxiao Mountain.","The townspeople had only given a general direction, for no one truly knew the precise location of Yunxiao Mountain. The exact spot remained unknown, so she had no choice but to search for it herself.","It took her the entire morning to finally locate the mountain.","The entire mountain, indeed the entire area, was concealed by protective barriers and intricate formations. For ordinary cultivators, discovering this place would be exceedingly difficult.","Just as she was searching for the entrance to Mount Yunxiao, the Azure Emperor, seated cross-legged beneath a tree in meditation with Hao’er and Muchen, felt a flicker in his brow and opened his eyes.","“Guests have arrived at the foot of the mountain,” he spoke in a measured tone, gazing toward the mist ahead.","Hearing the voice, Hao’er and Muchen opened their eyes, exchanging a look of surprise. Having been by their Master’s side for so long, they rarely saw visitors come to Yunxiao Mountain.","“Are they friends of the Master? Should we go to greet them?” Hao’er asked, looking at his master.","The Azure Emperor gave them an inexplicable look and said, “Both of you go together!” With that, he handed them a token."]},{"number":4906,"title":"Chapter 4906: Missing","paragraphs":["Chapter 4906: Missing","“Yes.” Both stood up and responded respectfully. After receiving the token that could unlock the barrier and formation, they turned and headed down the mountain.","At this moment, they still didn’t know that the person their master had sent them to fetch was the Mother they had always longed for and thought of.","Feng Jiu wandered around the mountain base until she finally located the entrance. She paused, pondering whether she should greet the Azure Emperor first—after all, she was a guest. Entering someone’s domain unannounced seemed rather impolite.","As she pondered this, two small figures appeared amidst the clouds, flying on swords. The moment she saw them, her eyes softened, and a smile spread across her face.","It seemed the Azure Emperor knew she had arrived. Look, he had even sent her two sons down to greet her.","Seeing her sons after so long filled her heart with both joy and a pang of sadness. It was her fault—because she had too many enemies, she had sent them away to study under the Azure Emperor.","Still, it seemed the Azure Emperor had treated them well. Both had grown significantly taller, and their faces had been altered—no longer the familiar features she knew. Yet, they were her children, and she recognized their essence instantly.","The two children, riding their swords, spotted the familiar red figure from afar. They froze, their eyes widening in surprise.","“I-Is that... Mother? Am I seeing things?” Muchen’s usually expressionless face was now filled with astonishment and bewilderment, his eyes sparkling with a light called delight. Yet, fearing it might be a hallucination born from his longing for his mother, he dared not believe it.","“It is Mother! Mother has come!” Hao’er, a few years older, saw their mother. After the initial shock, his stern little face lit up with delight and excitement. He accelerated his sword flight, soaring toward the mountain gate ahead.","“Mother!”","“Mother!”","The two leapt down from their flying swords, one after the other, and dashed toward the crimson figure. As their forms touched the array and barrier, the protective enchantments automatically opened a path for them, recognizing the tokens they carried.","“Hao’er! Chen’er!”","Feng Jiu spread her arms wide, catching the two as they threw themselves into her embrace. She held them tightly as their small bodies collided into her chest. Bending down, she kissed each of their cheeks, her gaze tender and doting. “Mother missed you so much. Have you been eating properly? Why are you only growing taller and not putting on weight?”","“Mother, Hao’er missed you so much too.”","“Mother, Chen’er missed you so, so much.”","The two little boys, their cheeks kissed by their mother, were both delighted and shy. Their eyes gazed at her, sparkling with joy and happiness.","“Mother, we ate well!” Chen’er beamed as he replied her earnestly.","“Mother, our Master treats us very well. We’re doing fine here, but we miss you terribly and want to see you,” Hao’er said, clutching her hand tightly.","“Good children. Mother misses you too and longs to see you.” She ruffled both boys’ hair. “Where’s Yue’er? Why didn’t she come down with you?”","After all, if her two sons had come down to greet her, their sister surely would have accompanied them. Unconsciously, her brow furrowed slightly as she watched the two boys shift their lips, looking as if they wanted to say something but didn’t quite know how.","“Mother, our sister isn’t on the mountain.....” Chen’er said."]},{"number":4907,"title":"Chapter 4907: Friend","paragraphs":["Chapter 4907: Friend","“Mother, Yue’er secretly asked her contracted beast to take her away from the mountain the other day, saying that she wanted to go see Mother, and has been gone for some days now, and we don’t know any news of her.” Hao’er explained with a wry smile.","Hearing this, Feng Jiu’s heart stirred and asked, “Does your master know about this?”","“Master knows, master said that Yue’er is naughty but good natured. Since she wants to go out, let her go, however, Mother there’s no need to worry! Master did also say that he has left a wisp of divine soul in her body, so if she encounters danger, he will show up to save her.”","Hearing these words, Feng Jiu nodded and said, “Well, Mother knows, let’s go! Take Mother to meet your master.”","“Mm hmm!”","The two men responded, and only then did they take her towards the mountain, and along the way, the two men held her hand one by one, and told her about their cultivation here, as well as the trivialities of their usual life.","Came to the mountain, Feng Jiu will see, that under the tree of a stone table, an immortal style of the man there drinking tea, looking at the appearance of that face, not at the beginning of the face she recognized, however, she also remembered, at the beginning of he said that it was just borrowed a body to act just.","“You here is quite quiet.”Feng Jiu walked over and came to sit across from him.","Azure Emperor held a teapot in one hand and poured her a cup of tea, saying, “Alpine Snow Spirit Tea, taste it.”","Feng Jiu picked it up and took a sip before putting it down, saying, “You know, I didn’t come to see you for tea.”","“You are also not here to see this emperor.”Azure Emperor smiled and glanced at her with a cloudy look, “You came to see how your children are doing? Has this Emperor raised them well?”","“Growing and not growing, it must be because you’re eating too little here.”She said, pinching the arms of her two sons, as she justified in her mind ‘shouldn’t she take them back to live for a while and raise their meat properly?’","“People who cultivate Immortals shouldn’t be too heavy on their appetites in the first place, otherwise, how can they go far on the Great Dao?”Azure Emperor was unimpressed. These three disciples of his were probably also taught bad by Feng Jiu, Fasting Pill was not eaten, they only wanted to eat grains and cereals.","“What’s the use of cultivating immortality if you can’t even eat delicacies, what’s the use of cultivating the way to longevity?” She smiled, took a sip of spirit tea, and said, “This tea is not bad, send me two pounds.”","“You are not polite.” He looked at her, dumbfounded.","“At least we are friends, between friends, naturally we don’t have to be polite, what’s more, I also brought you a meet and greet gift this time I came.” As she spoke, she took out two altars of spirit wine from her space and placed them on one side of the stone table, smiling, “This is my personally brewed spirit wine, there is a market without a price, so it wouldn’t be right for you not to return some gifts, would it?”","At those words, he glanced at her, opened it and took a sniff, saying, “Good wine.”","As soon as his voice fell, he flicked his sleeve and put away the two jars of wine, saying, “Spirit wine personally brewed by the Phoenix Sovereign is naturally priceless in the market.”","As he spoke, with another flick of his sleeve, two exquisite tea pots were placed in front of him, saying, “I also obtained a total of three pounds, these two pounds will be given to you!” Before that, he added, “Just right as a return gift.”","Feng Jiu naturally would not be polite with him, and after saying thank you, she put it away.","Watching her put away the spirit tea, Azure Emperor then said, “I haven’t congratulated you for taking over the Great Emperor Northern Flame’s territory and becoming the Lord of the two lands.” With that, he smiled and said, “I didn’t expect you to be really quite capable.”"]},{"number":4908,"title":"Chapter 4908: Agree","paragraphs":["Chapter 4908: Agree","“You know, it’s not just Great Emperor Northern Flame that I want to kill.” Feng Jiu refilled his teacup and poured her own before asking, “What’s going on with Yue’er? Where is she now?”","Azure Emperor sipped his tea unhurriedly and put down his teacup before saying, “That girl’s heart is not stable, even though there are two of her elder brothers in this mountain, she still misses you and wants to see you. Even though I did not allow them to go down the mountain to see you and that they can only cultivate in the mountain, that girl couldn’t stay any still longer and slipped away quietly on her own.”","He said slowly, poured another cup of tea, said, “As for where she is now, this is something you don’t have to worry about, my Azure Emperor’s disciple won’t be in danger even if she’s out there, however, in a short period of time, I guess she won’t be able to go to your place.”","“You can really make sure that she will not be fine when she is alone outside?”Feng Jiu frowned, it was impossible to say that she was not worried.","“That girl is very resourceful, as long as she doesn’t say she is your daughter, naturally no one will touch her.”Azure Emperor said indifferently.","Hearing this, the corner of Feng Jiu’s mouth twitched as she said, “Although what you said is true, but saying it like this, as if being born as my child is an unlucky matter.”","“Mother, we are most fortunate because you are our mother.”Hao’er said in a hurry.","In his heart, he had always been proud of having such a Mother. To be her child was the luckiest thing in his life.","“Mother, we are happiest being Mother’s children.”Muchen also opened his mouth and spoke, looking at her with a gaze full of admiration.","“Good boys!”","Feng Jiu smiled and rubbed the two’s heads.","“I want to bring the children back to stay for a while.” She looked at Azure Emperor and spoke, thinking that when she said that she would let the children follow him, she wouldn’t come to disturb them, much less come to see them, but she didn’t want to see them now and think of bringing them back for a period of time.","On the one hand is thinking, now she ascended, and killed the Great Emperor Northern Flame, the other three great emperors in this period of time to shut down to heal their wounds, and a short period of time will not dare to lay hands on her, on the other hand is that her territory is almost dealt with, this period of time there is no other things need to be busy, therefore, thinking of the children will be brought back to the side to stay for a period of time.","Azure Emperor listened to her words, there was not a trace of surprise on his face, as if he had expected it, he did not refuse, but looked at the two disciples, then nodded: “Yes, it so happens that I am going to go out to do some things, the two of them, you will take them back first! For now, your place should be safe as well.”","“Thank you, Master!” The two of them immediately thanked their Master joyfully upon hearing this.","“Follow your Mother back, don’t focus on playing, remember to cultivate, when you come back I will have to check.” The Azure Emperor reminded in a deep voice.","“Yes!” The two of them grinned, the look on their little faces a rare joyful happiness.","“Thank you.”Feng Jiu also gave a thank you.","Azure Emperor looked at her and said, “You don’t need to worry about that girl, I will take care of it myself.”","Listening to these words, although Feng Jiu did not know what he meant, however, she also knew that he was very attached to Yue’er and doted on her, so naturally he would not watch her meet with danger and have an accident. Now that he had said this, naturally there was nothing to be uneasy about.","At that moment, she nodded and said, “Mm, thank you.”"]},{"number":4909,"title":"Chapter 4909: Bewildered","paragraphs":["She stayed in this Yunxiao Mountain for two days, then she bid farewell to Azure Emperor and left in an airship with her two children, heading for the Immortal Island ...","Azure Emperor also left the door shortly after they left, not knowing where ....","Meanwhile, in the middle of that forest, Xiao Junyan was looking around with a sullen face, searching for that little brat who had slipped out from under his eyes. Compared to searching for Sacred Beasts and whatnot, he felt it was better to find that little thing first, after all, the level of danger in here was far greater than what she had imagined. If there was an accident, he was afraid that there would be no bones left in the body.","As for the Sacred Beast, it was in their territory and could not run away. This entire place belonged to his Xiao family, even if this time he came out did not find it, the elders in the family will also personally come over a trip the next time.","However, what he didn't expect was that he had been searching in this forest for the past few days, but there had been no sign of that little doll.","On the other hand, Xiao Junheng returned to the mansion and went directly to his father, asking him to quickly have the people in the various rooms underneath him check to see if there were any little girls who were around five years old who had left home.","After he himself went back to the courtyard to change his clothes and have a meal, he didn't have a moment before he saw a guard come up and report, \"Young Master, the Patriarch has asked you to come over.\"","\"Got it.\" Xiao Junheng responded and followed the guard forward.","Arriving in the hall, he saw that, not only was his father seated at the main seat, even the other clan elders were present, seeing this, he stepped forward and bowed, \"Greetings father, all clan elders.\"","\"Jun Heng, the people in the clan reported back after checking themselves that there was no young girls around five or six year old girl who left home. Tell us more, give us the full details.\" Patriarch Xiao spoke in a deep voice, his gaze falling on his son standing in the center.","Hearing these words, Xiao Junheng said in his heart that it was true.","He had long suspected that that child was not a child of their Xiao family, and he did not expect that it really wasn't, only, if it was not a child of their Xiao family, then whose child was it? How could it quietly appear in the middle of the forest on their island?<az25c0> Googlᴇ search novelfire.net</az25c0>","\"Father, all clan elders, that girl is five or six years old, there is no adult accompanying her, I was being beseiged by the lions when that girl suddenly appeared, just that, there is one thing that is strange is that since she appeared, the lions that attacked me fled in panic, at that time, I did not think much about it, but at this time I think it may be related to this girl.\"","His voice was gentle and clear, like flowing water as he gently told them about the situation at that time.","\"I thought at that time, our immortal island has its own boundaries and formations, that is, our Xiao family's children can not go out without a token in their possession, therefore, I thought that she was a child of our clan, who sneaked out to play, but then I saw that she did not have a teleportation jade token or something like that on her body, and then I asked her about it, and she said that it was ...\"","Speaking here, he hesitated.","\"What is it?\"A clan elder asked with a solemn face.People of unknown origin had been mixed in amongst the Immortal Islands, and this matter could be big or small.","\"She said that she followed Junyan into the forest.\" He said, looking at the people sitting in the hall, and added: \"I was worried that she would be in danger alone in the forest, so I forcibly detained her by my side and brought her with me, and then when we encountered an attack by the wolves, Junyan just happened to show up and saved us, and also seemed to be very familiar and close to that girl.\"","\"Close?\"","The people in the hall were stunned, as if they had heard something extraordinary.They looked at each other, bewildered."]},{"number":4910,"title":"Chapter 4910: Found","paragraphs":["Chapter 4910: Found","Patriarch Xiao who was seated in the main seat asked in surprise, “You said that Junyan was very close to that child?”","“Yes, he has been holding that child since he saw her.” Xiao Junheng explained, and when he saw the dismay and surprise on each of their faces, the corners of his lips could not help but raise slightly.","At that time, when he saw Junyan being so close to that child, he probably had the same expression.","Everyone here knew that Xiao Junyan was the most outstanding genius of their Xiao family over the centuries, and was also the son of the Patriarch’s older brother, except that in that main lineage, there was only Xiao Junyan left.","Because he lost his parents when he was young, he only knew how to cultivate since he was young, and he was not close to anyone, therefore, those who heard Jun Heng’s words, were all surprised.","Under the surprised gazes, Xiao Junheng continued to tell them about the matter.","After hearing his words, one of the clan elders wrinkled his brows slightly and said, ”You mean to say that that child ran away after drugging the few of you? Even Junyan was affected?”","“Yes.” Xiao Junheng replied honestly and remained silent thereafter.","There was silence in the hall for a moment, and only after a while did one of the clan elders look at the others and asked, “What do the rest of you think of this matter? Who do you think would have placed such a child in our territory? And in such a quiet manner?”","“It seems that the child has to be found first.” Patriarch Xiao said, and immediately said to Xiao Junheng, “Bring some people to search in the forest, don’t hurt that child when you find her, first bring her back for us to question her personally.” As he spoke, he tossed a token for mobilizing people to him.","“Yes.” Xiao Junheng answered as he caught the token and saluted before retreating.","Yue’er did not know about what was going on here, however, she knew that she had to hide well, lest she be captured by the Xiao Family’s people, after all, she had drugged them, and they naturally knew that she wasn’t a son or daughter of the Xiao Family.","At this time, she was roasting the prey which the lion had brought back, and did not know that the smoke emitted was rising outside.","Xiao Junyan has been searching for a few days, there has been no news, at this time he stood on the sword above the forest looking down, when he saw that a wisp of smoke was rising from a certain place, a glint fleeted across his eyes.","Whenever their Xiao family enters this forest, there is not much time to roast meat to eat, most of them were on the Fasting Pill, only that little doll would think of roasting meat.","Thinking of this, the corner of his lips slightly hooked, knowing that that little brat was very clever, at that moment, he convereged his breath as he swept towards that location in great speed.","As Yue’er smelled the fragrant meat, a happy smile appeared on her small face as she cut off a large piece for the lion, and then she herself cut off a piece of meat and ate it.","“Mmmm, it smells so good, my craftsmanship is really getting better and better.” She smelled the aroma of the meat and gulped, as she tore off a small piece and ate it.","The lion was lying beside her and was also eating the roasted meat at this moment. Ever since it followed this little master, it seemed to have become less fond of eating raw meat.","At this time, the one person and one beast in the cave did not know that on a tree not far from the cave entrance, Xiao Junyan was pressing down the leaves that blocked his vision with one hand, looking at the one person and one beast in the cave, a hint of surprise crossing his eyes.","It turned out that the Sacred Beast was following this little doll around, no wonder there had been no trace of the Sacred Beast, however, how did this little doll take in that Sacred Beast?"]},{"number":4911,"title":"Chapter 4911: Stalling","paragraphs":["Chapter 4911: Stalling","For a time, his heart was filled with curiosity, more and more he felt that this little thing was very mysterious, her body seemed to be an infinite treasure, and no one knew what would be found in the next moment.","Looking at the little place they were holed up in, the corner of his lips curled up. Hiding here these days? It was not a bad place to hide, only, after all, she was still too tender, even if she was intelligent, but she was also careless.","He gently leapt down from the tree and walked towards the cave.","Yue’er who was still enjoying her meal did not know that someone had close in, but the lion first noticed that there is unfamiliar breath into their range, at once quickly scurried up, came to the cave entrance to look out.","At first, he thought it would be a beast, but he didn’t expect it to be that teenager.","“Master, that person found us and is here again.” The lion stood at the entrance of the cave and did not retreat, because that teenager had already seen it, even if he retreated and hid again at this time, it was useless.","“Hm? Who? Who found us?” Yue’er was stunned, she jumped up in a hurry and took a look at the cave entrance, she saw that the person called Xiao Junyan was walking this way, she froze for a moment, and immediately frowned: “Why is this person like a lingering ghost, he keeps haunting us?”","“A lingering ghost?” Xiao Junyan stopped his steps and looked at the little thing looking at him with a disgusted face, her gaze also cold.","Yue’er didn’t move and prepared to move out of the cave entrance to take the lion and slip away, when she heard his voice.","“Where do you want to escape to again?”","“What do you want?!” Yue’er paused in her steps and stared at him with an angry pair of eyes.","“That should be me asking you.” He took a step closer, and at that moment, he saw the lion scurry forward to block in front of that little one, rushing at him with a threatening low growl.","He stopped his steps and glanced at that lion, then looked at that little doll and asked, “Who are you? How did you get here?”","Without waiting for her to speak, he said, “You’re not a member of the Xiao family, this can no longer be hidden, I’ve gotten word that the family has sent people out to look for you, you’d better tell me the truth, or else, no one will be able to protect you at that time.”","Yue’er’s eyes rolled, she did not know what came to her mind and asked, “You are also here to catch me?”","Xiao Junyan didn’t say anything and just looked at her.","At first he just found this little doll interesting, but he didn’t realize that this little thing was still a little fox, actually slipping away from under his eyes twice. Capture her? Didn’t really want to, but, he wouldn’t let her slip out from under his eyes again either.","“Come back to the Xiao family with me.” He spoke, looking at her, saying, “I’ll keep you safe.”","“Don’t wanna.” Yue’er directly refused, she looked at him, revealing a wry smile to her, patting the lion beside her with one hand, “As you can see, this Sacred Beast is mine oh~ It listens to me!”","Upon hearing this, Xiao Junyan gave her a deep look and asked, “So?”","“So? Hee hee hee.” She laughed, patted the lion’s head, and said, “You stall him, I’ll run first.” As soon she spoke, Yue’er immediately swept out and headed towards the forest.","Xiao Junyan was ready to chase after her when he saw the lion pouncing over, and could only turn in a different direction to attack the lion.","As the young master of the Xiao family, the future Patriarch of the Xiao family, Xiao Junyan’s strength talent was naturally excellent, otherwise the elders in the family would not have let him come here to seek that Sacred Beast.","At this time, he fought with the lion, his body’s pressure and aura was released, the lion’s heart was shocked, he did not expect this person’s strength to be this powerful, with its strength that had just advanced not long ago, he could only barely engage him."]},{"number":4912,"title":"Chapter 4912: Bleeding","paragraphs":["After dragging it on for a while, the lion let out a low roar and quickly withdrew.","When Xiao Junyan saw the lion withdrawing, he didn't chase after it, but instead chased after the direction where the little one had fled.","In terms of escape pace and stance, Yue'er's young age could be considered the top among the three siblings, and her speed was also the fastest. With the time that the lion had stalled, she quickly left, as long as she escaped first, then joining up with the lion would be easy.","Only, what she didn't expect was that when she ran out a long distance and looked back, she saw that Xiao Junyan was chasing after her.","\"Ahh! He's catching up! He's catching up! He's simply bullying little kids!\" She muttered while trying to pull the distance away. Paying no heed to where she was headed, all she had in her head was to use her fastest speed to escape!","\"It's that kid!\" Ahead, a group of young teenage girls gathered together to talk while walking, when they saw a child not far in front of them running towards their side, they couldn't help but point at her in surprise.","\"The news from the family says it's a five or six year old child, isn't it her? Quickly! Catch her!\" A teenager said and hurriedly swept towards the running child.","One must know that catching someone back would be a great feat!","Yue'er was running, looking back from time to time, and didn't notice the front for a while, when she noticed those people in front of her, she let out a cry of alarm, and hurriedly turned in a different direction and ran.","\"Quickly! Quickly catch her, don't let her run away!\"","Seeing that the child turned a corner and ran to the other side, the people hurriedly shouted, \"Flank! Flank from that side!\"","When these people were stopped, Xiao Junyan, who was chasing after them, also rushed up, and when he saw that the children of the family were holding swords in their hands and encircling the little one, he immediately twisted his eyebrows and droned in a cold voice: \"Don't hurt her!\"","The crowd was stunned, after hearing the voice they looked towards the place of the voice, when they saw that it was Xiao Junyan, their faces changed slightly, and they hurriedly called out respectfully, \"Young Master!\"","\"All put away your swords, don't hurt her.\" Xiao Junyan coldly commanded, lifted his Qi and swept forward, grabbing towards that little guy.","\"Ah!\"","Yue'er exclaimed in shock, but her body dodged away with a nimble flash.","Xiao Junyan grabbed an empty hand and was stunned for a moment, as if he did not expect this little doll to actually have such a good stance, and once again leaned forward to grab towards her, when a lion's roar came.","\"Roar!\"","\"Ahhhh! Fierce beast!\"","\"Nope! That's a Sacred Beast! You guys, look at the tattoo on that lion's head! Hiss! How is that possible? This Sacred Beast has been contracted?\" A teenager huffed backwards while suddenly thinking that the Young Master was right here, and surprise erupted in his eyes.","\"Could it be that the Young Master contracted this Sacred Beast?\"","But as they were saying that, they saw the Sacred Beast pounce out violently, and they thought that the Sacred Beast was going to pounce and bite at that child, but they didn't expect it to actually pounce towards their Young Master.","\"Young Master be careful!\"","The crowd's faces changed in fear, and they instinctively exclaimed in alarm, when they saw their Young Master's hand reaching out to grab the child lurch, turning his grip into a fist and twisting it tightly, and on top of his fist, a stream of air that was visible to the naked eye coalesced, and at a very high speed, he turned in a direction and swung towards the head of that Sacred Beast that was pouncing on him.","Yue'er ran away and looked back to see that Xiao Junyan's fist smashed down heavily on the lion's head, and the lion's grasping paw also clawed fiercely on his arm, leaving several deep marks.","At the same time the lion wailed and was knocked back, Xiao Junyan was scratched arm blood also violently gushed out, the smell of blood, instantly permeated the air ..."]},{"number":4913,"title":"Chapter 4913: Bring Back","paragraphs":["Chapter 4913: Bring Back","“What audacity! Dare to injure my Xiao Family’s Young Master!”","A stern and low voice came from the sky, and along with that voice, there was also a powerful pressure, as well as a golden net with a golden glow.","Yue’er looked towards the place of the voice when it sounded, only to see a group of cultivators wearing the same colour robes swept down from the sky, eight of them were holding a corner of the golden net in their hands and headed towards the lion below, seemingly wanting to capture it.","Immediately, she exclaimed, “Lion, come back!” As soon as the voice came out and her mind moved, she saw the lion turn into a ray of light and scurry into her space with a swoosh.","At the same time, the golden net covered but caught an empty net, but those people turned their pace, and surrounded the little person who was ready to escape.","“Don’t even think of escaping!”","The group of people surrounded and attacked, one of them reached out towards Yue’er and grabbed her, extremely fast speed with a stern momentum, making Xiao Junyan’s heart sink, not caring about the injury on his arm, dodged and swept up, and when that person attacked her, he reached out and picked up that small figure and put it into his arms.","“Young Master! ”","When that person looked up and realised that it was Xiao Junyan, it was too late to retract the outstretched hand, hence he could only redirect the force that had condensed as he grabbed to the side of the tree , leaving a few deep handprints in the trunk.","Yue’er was protected in his arms, along with Xiao Junyan’s turn and see that attacked to the tree trunk and left those handprints, the little gaze was cold as she looked at the person who had attepmted to attack her with such malice","Only to see, that is a middle-aged man, the face looks ordinary, but the body has a stern ruthlessness, he does not have wounds on his body, but, his body exudes a smell of blood, it can be imagined that there are countless people and beasts who have died in his hands.","“Junyan, you are injured.” Xiao Junheng came down from the back and frowned when he saw his hand that was hanging down at his side with blood dripping downwards, “Tend to the wound first!”","He stepped forward and glanced at the little girl with a complicated look in his eyes, and did not say anything more, but took out medicine and cloths to prepare to help him treat his wounds.","Xiao Junyan looked down at the little doll in his arms who stayed still and didn’t say anything, seeing her glaring coldly at the person who had just attacked her, that gaze was so calm that it was somewhat less like that of a five or six year old child.","“It’s alright, don’t worry, I’m here, I won’t let you get hurt.” He opened his mouth to speak, somewhat clumsily comforting this little one that he thought was frightened.","Yue’er didn’t say anything, just lowered her eyes to converge, her gaze just touched his bleeding hand, her small mouth pursed, didn’t move.","After helping him simply treat the injury on his arm, Xiao Junheng looked at him and said, “The clan already knows about her, we have to bring her back, my father and the clan elders want to question her personally.”","“Go!” Xiao Junyan said. From the moment he saw this team of Guards arrive, he knew that this little thing could not be hidden.","He led the men to follow them back, while the others all pinched their teleportation jade tags to return to the clan first due to the order.","Along the way, Yue’er did not speak until she arrived in front of the gate of that Immortal Mansion, then she spoke, “Put me down, I’ll walk by myself.”","Upon hearing this, Xiao Junyan glanced at her and put her down.","Xiao Junheng, who was at the side, saw that the little girl was generous, and did not have a trace of restraint or discomfort in front of the crowd, so he could not help but let his gaze flash slightly as he walked in front to lead the way for them, leading them towards the main hall."]},{"number":4914,"title":"Chapter 4914: Bold","paragraphs":["Chapter 4914: Bold","Patriarch Xiao and the clan elders in the hall were already sitting there waiting, and when they saw the few people who came in, their gazes fell on Xiao Junyan first.","“Junyan, how is the injury on your hand? Is it serious?” Patriarch Xiao inquired, hearing the report from the person who had returned earlier that he had been scratched by the Sacred Beast.","“It’s fine.” Xiao Junyan said and bowed towards them.","“This is that child?” Patriarch Xiao’s gaze looked towards the little girl who had walked in at the back, not expecting it to be such a young child, after all, he had heard that the Sacred Beast had been contracted by her, something that none of them had expected.","Such a small child, how did she make a Sacred Beast recognize her as its master?","At this time, carefully sizing up this child, seeing her come in from the back with her short little legs, not panicked, not shocked, not afraid, in the face of their sizing up and probing, she didn’t lower her head or avert her gaze, but instead stared at them with those beautiful eyes, seeming to be sizing them up as well.","The people in the hall were all of the older generation now, naturally they could tell at a glance that this was not some several hundred year old strong person who had manifested, after all, the age of the bones in her body couldn’t be changed, this, was just a five or six year old child.","Such a small child, with such poise and boldness, naturally would not be a child of an unusual family, therefore, after everyone looked at each other, Patriarch Xiao opened his mouth and asked, “What is your name? How did you come here?”","“My name is Yun Qi, Azure Emperor of Yunxiao Mountain is my master.”","Yue’er, the tiny person standing in the hall, with a soft and clear voice, reported her own master’s great name. Because she knew very well that when it came to this place, she had to say it even if she didn’t.","What’s more, her master had said that if she caused any trouble outside, she would not dare to make things difficult for her if she reported his name.","Perhaps it was not expected that this child actually said his name and master’s name as soon as she was asked, the people in the hall were stunned for a moment, and then a little stunned.","Especially Xiao Junyan and Xiao Junheng, it was not that they hadn’t asked her about her name and origin, but she had never said anything.","One of the clan elders asked with some skepticism, “You said that Yunxiao Mountain’s Azure Emperor is your master?”","“Mm hmm.” Yue’er nodded.","“Bold!” That clan elder’s expression sank, his palm slammed on the tabletop and his entire body stood up as well, and his entire mighty pressure struck out due to this angry shout of his, heading towards that little person.","Xiao Junyan frowned and took a step forward to block the pressure released from that clan elder.","Seeing this, that Clan Elder’s brow also wrinkled, and after looking deeply at Xiao Junyan, he did not say anything, but only put away the mighty pressure.","Being blocked by someone in front of her, Yue’er glared and reached out to poke the waist of the person in front of her, her voice soft and glutinous but with displeasure, “You’re blocking my line of sight.”","She was not afraid of that old man’s pressure, if he dares to bully her, she will complain to her master! Let him do the honours!","Junyan listened to the words behind him, the corner of his mouth twitched, slightly sideways back away, at the same time glanced at her, saw her with a small beast like a fearless appearance, his heart sighed lightly: after all, is still small, do not understand things, not to mention do not understand that the clan old man’s pressure can make the blood qi inside her body turbulence and suffer from internal injuries.","The people in the hall looked at the little girl even this good courage, the eyes could not help but slightly flashed a bit, looking at her gaze with a few points of thought."]},{"number":4915,"title":"Chapter 4915: Rebuke","paragraphs":["Chapter 4915: Rebuke","The Clan Elder who had stoold up had his hand in the air, as he swept a glance at the audacious little girl, and walked slowly, his old voice carrying a bit of harshness as he hollered, “At a young age, you’re full of lies! As we all know, Azure Emperor does have a disciple named Yun Qi, only, how is his disciple not as old as you, and that disciple of his, is even in earlier years due to the failure of the tribulation and died! So tell me, where did you come from?”","He walked to Yue’er’s front and looked down on her, his majestic presence and aura made Xiao Junheng by the side tremble, but Yue’er raised her head and looked straight at the clan elder, no fear in her eyes.","When the crowd saw this, they became more and more amazed, and were even more curious about her origins and origins.","When Xiao Junheng saw this, he sighed softly in his heart, he didn’t even know that this little girl had guts.","When Xiao Junyan saw this, the corners of his lips were slightly hooked, and his gaze was filled with admiration and affection. This little doll, was very interesting indeed.","That clan elder then stared at the little dot in front of him and droned in a deep voice: “Just who are you? What are your intentions of sneaking into my Xiao Family’s Immortal Island which has gone in seclusion? And who ordered you? And how did you come here? If you don’t quickly tell me the truth, you will not be spared!”","Yue’er stared at him with bony eyes, and said in a soft and sticky voice: “You said that this is a secluded place, so how do you know that my master has taken me as his disciple? And what evidence do you have to prove that I’m lying?”","Saying that, her voice gave a beat, her clear gaze stared at him and said with a serious face, “I have long since not been a three year old child, it’s useless for you to threaten me, I’m not afraid of you, and also, don’t bully me just because you’re older, I can’t beat you, but, my master can.”","The corners of the crowd’s mouths twitched as they listened to her words.","Has this child not actually a child? Or were all the children out there nowadays had such powerful mouths?","That clan elder was disliked by such a child, and immediately had a look of blowing his beard and eyes, as he glared at such a small fat little girl in front of him, asking, “You said that you’re Azure Emperor’s disciple, what’s your proof?”","Yue’er blinked her eyes and asked curiously, “What credentials do I need for this? I am clearly my master’s disciple! My master and I both know that, what more proof do I need?”","At this question, that clan elder was instantly speechless.","The people in the hall also fell silent, and the hall was filled with a strange and inexplicable silence for a moment.","Xiao Junyan had a hint of a smile between his brows as he said, “If you want to know if what she said is the truth, you only need to send someone to check it out.”","“Cough!” Patriarch Xiao lightly coughed against the corner of his lips with one hand clenched in a fist, and immediately whispered a few instructions to a person behind him before looking at Yue’er again and asking, “That Sacred Beast was contracted by you?”","“Yes.” Yue’er nodded and said. They had seen it anyway, so they couldn’t rely on it even if they wanted to.","“That was a Sacred Beast, how did you make it willingly contract with you?” Patriarch Xiao asked again, unable to hide his curiosity in his heart.","“It wasn’t originally a Sacred Beast, it was originally just a fierce beast at the peak level of a Sacred Beast, it’s still that much closer to being a Sacred Beast.” Yue’er stretched her small hand and gestured.","Hearing these words, the expressions of the people in the hall moved slightly. They naturally knew that the Sacred Beast had just advanced, only, why was it contracted by her as soon as it advanced?","Just as she was thinking, she saw that little girl reveal a proud and triumphant smile, “However, when I saw that it was dying from its injuries, I gave it one of the medicinal pills that my master gave me for defense, and then it advanced.”"]},{"number":4916,"title":"Chapter 4916: The Truth","paragraphs":["Chapter 4916: The Truth","Saying this, Yue’er’s small face revealed a helpless look, “Later on, it insisted on following me, and I had no choice but to accept it.”","Hearing her words, the crowd’s faces darkened. The way in which she said it, she actually meant that the Sacred Beast that was born on their Immortal Island was desperate to establish a contract with her? However, if it was really a medicinal pill that had helped that Sacred Beast advance, it was really possible that it was the Azure Emperor’s handiwork, after all, that was a great emperor level powerhouse, how could he not have some medicinal pills that possessed divine effects on hand?","Could it be that this little chubby girl with the nature of a fox was really a disciple of Azure Emperor? If that’s the case, then her coming here was the Azure Emperor’s doing? Only, if that was the case, what did Azure Emperor intend to do with this move?","For a while, countless speculative thoughts swept through the minds of the crowd, but in the end, they all turned into a soft sigh.","It seemed that right now, they could only wait for news to see if this little girl was really Azure Emperor’s disciple as she said.","“Take her away and guard her first.” Patriarch Xiao said, ordering people to bring her away.","At this moment, Xiao Junyan stepped forward and said, “Second Uncle, I will just bring her to my courtyard.”","Hearing this, Patriarch Xiao’s brows wrinkled as he said, “Junyan, her identity is still unknown and with a Sacred Beast by her side, it’s not quite right to place her in your courtyard.”","“I’ll personally watch her to be at ease.” Xiao Junyan said.","Seeing this, Patriarch Xiao frowned and fell silent, not opening his mouth to respond, as if he was pondering something.","When the clan elders in the hall saw this, they did not open their mouths either, because Patriarch was right, this child’s origins were unknown, and with her identity still uncertain, how could they place such a variable as her at the side of their Xiao family’s young master? It was too dangerous.","Xiao Junheng on the side saw that someone amongst the clan elders wanted to speak, so he immediately stepped forward and said to the person on the main seat, “Father, she and Junyan are quite familiar in the forest, so there shouldn’t be any major problems with her being watched over by Junyan, if you are not assured, I can also help watch over her.”","Yue’er listened to them talking, a pair of eyes turned around for a bit, staring at each of their expressions, secretly skimming her lips. What watching over her? Thinking she was a dangerous person? She had even reported her family master’s name, and these people were still guarding her like a thief, it was really boring.","“I’ll take her back first.” Junyan didn’t wait for them to say more, he directly turned around, reached out and picked up Yue’er, and took big steps outside.","Watching this scene, the brows of the people in the hall wrinkled even tighter. One of the Taoist Priests said, “Why is Junyan so attached to this child? Right now her identity is unknown, if she does anything to harm Junyan ...”","“From my point of view, she should not dare, after all, this is our Xiao family’s territory, if she really hurt someone, she would not live to leave.” Another clan elder said.","One of the clan elders then said, “Patriarch, if this child is truly Azure Emperor’s disciple, shouldn’t we tell the Old Predecessor?”","Patriarch Xiao nodded and said, “Well, after we have definite news, I will personally go and speak to the Old Predecessor, after all, it is about Azure Emperor, so there will be no room for sloppiness, moreover, if she really is Azure Emperor’s disciple, what is he trying to do by sending this child here? It’s probably necessary to consult Old Predecessor as well.”","Seeing that he already had an idea, the crowd didn’t say anything more, and after standing up and bowing their hands, they left one after another.","With their Xiao family’s power outside, they believe that it will only take a day’s time to know whether this child was telling the truth or not ..."]},{"number":4917,"title":"Chapter 4917: Know","paragraphs":["Chapter 4917: Know","On the other hand, Xiao Junyan brought Yue’er back to the courtyard and settled down, then ordered people to let the kitchen prepare food, originally there was no maidservant in the courtyard, also because of her arrival and let people go to the front yard to transfer two maidservants over to wait for her.","Yue’er, led by the two maidservants, went into a room and took a bath, changed her clothes and then came out, she saw Xiao Junyan, who had already changed his clothes, sitting at the table in the courtyard. On the table, there were more than a dozen of exquisite dishes with their tantilising aroma wafting in the air.","Each of those exquisite dishes had only one small plate, about two people’s portions, and there were different dishes on the dozen small plates, which made people’s appetite wide open before they could eat them.","“Is this made by your family’s kitchen?” Yue’er sat down at the table, looking at the exquisite dishes on the table, her eyes shining brightly.","“Well, how about you give it a try and have a taste.” He gave her some dishes and put them into the bowl in front of her.","Seeing this, Yue’er was not polite and directly took her chopsticks and started to devour the food before her.","Xiao Junyan didn’t say anything, he just watched her eat, occasionally helping her clip some dishes, and only after she had eaten enough and put down her chopsticks and burped, did he have someone remove the things on the table.","“How long have you been with Azure Emperor?” Xiao Junyan poured her a glass of water and asked as if he had no intention of doing so.","“A long time.” Yue’er said with a smile.","“Is there food in the mountains?”","“There is! There are wild foods in the mountains, and Master will let us go down to the mountains to pick them up.” Yue’er got out of her chair and walked around the courtyard looking around.","“Us? Azure Emperor has other disciples besides you?” Xiao Junyan’s gaze flickered slightly as he once again inquired.","“There are, I also have two Senior Brothers.” These, but also not afraid to let him know, after all, as long as they check naturally can be found out, her master received the three of them also did not hide, many people know them.","On this side, Xiao Junyan in between words, intentionally or unintentionally inquired about news about her. On the other hand, the people under the Xiao family also spread the word, knowing that they somehow came in a little girl here.","And that little girl also stayed alone in the forest for an unknown number of days, and was not discovered until recently. For a while, the people underneath were talking, and more than that, they were curious.","In the early morning of the following day, Patriarch Xiao received the news that had been sent back, he then had someone call Xiao Junyan and Yun Qi.","Yue’er got up early and rode her lion around Xiao Junyan’s courtyard. After hearing the summons from the Patriarch of the Xiao family, she rode the lion and followed Xiao Junyan to the front yard.","The people of the Xiao family had long been curious about her, and now that they knew that Patriarch had summoned her, many of them came to the road early to watch. When they saw that tiny person riding a majestic lion following their young master to the front yard, many people were surprised.","“See, that’s the lion, that’s the Sacred Beast that advanced some time ago, I didn’t expect it to become her mount.”","“She’s so young, how did she take in that Sacred Beast?”","“I heard that she is Azure Emperor’s disciple, I don’t know if it’s true or not.”","“Azure Emperor? But he’s as strong as our family’s Old Predecessor who are both great emperors?” Another younger youth asked.","One of the older youths nodded and said, “That’s right, I heard that Azure Emperor is also a very powerful Great Emperor, and that he is also acquainted with our family’s Old Predecessor, so if she is really Azure Emperor’s disciple, our Xiao family would still have to treat her as an honored guest! If she had told a lie, she probably wouldn’t have survive today.”"]},{"number":4918,"title":"Chapter 4918: Seeing the Divine Whip","paragraphs":["Hearing those words, the crowd could not help but fall silent. That was only a five or six year old child, if she really told a lie, would Patriarch and the others really kill her?","In the gazes of the crowd, Yue'er rode the lion and followed Xiao Junyan to the front hall, only when she reached the front of the hall did she get off the lion's back and walk in.","The people sitting in the hall looked at the little girl who came riding the lion, their eyes flickering slightly. Their eyes skimmed over her and landed on the lion that followed her.","This was that Sacred Beast.","Unexpectedly, a Sacred Beast that had been born with great difficulty had actually allowed a little girl from outside to contract it.","\"Patriarch, all clan elders.\" Xiao Junyan saluted them.","\"Junyan, sit down!\" Patriarch Xiao gestured.","Xiao Junyan paused for a moment, then walked to his seat and sat down, while looking towards that Yun Qi standing in the hall. From amongst his intentional and unintentional inquiries yesterday, he could conclude that she was indeed Azure Emperor's disciple without a doubt, thus, at this moment, he was not worried about her.","\"Yun Qi, you said that you are Azure Emperor's disciple? Then let me ask you, how many disciples does Azure Emperor have in total?\" Patriarch Xiao inquired, his majestic gaze falling on the small human standing there.","\"My master has three disciples right now, and there are two Senior Brothers other than me.\" Yue'er opened her mouth and spoke, her large eyes looking at Patriarch Xiao at the main seat, unperturbed and unafraid.","Hearing these words, Patriarch Xiao and a clan elder sitting on his left glanced at each other, and asked again, \"It is rumored outside that Patriarch Xiao had schemed from Immortal Elder Lingmu to obtain an Ancient Divine Whip, which is also known as the Nine Sections Red Flame Phoenix Scale Whip, and gave it to his young disciple as a weapon, since you are Azure Emperor's disciple, you should know about this whip.\"","Upon hearing this, Yue'er turned her hand and took out the whip from her space, smilingly saying, \"You are talking about this? It was indeed given to me by my master, could it be, is this what you call a token of evidence?\"","Looking at that whip, quite a few clan elders stood up, their gazes tightly fixed on that whip. This whip, they have also heard of it, only, this whip was in Immortal Elder Lingmu's Moon Reflection Illusory Spirit Realm, no one has been able to take it out for many years, they didn't expect ...","\"Can you let me have a look?\" Seeing that whip, Patriarch Xiao's heart was basically sure of her identity, only that he had heard about the power of this whip, but had never seen it.","\"It's possible!\" Yue'er responded, not afraid of letting her whip be taken, but walked forward to hand her the whip.","When she got this whip at that time, she was worried that there would be someone who would snatch her whip, then her master said not to worry, no one would dare to use this whip or snatch it .","At that time she did not know, until after a period of time to know, the original master of her family put out the word, the master of this whip can only be his disciple, who dares to take, who dares to grab, who dares to use, he is bound to kill his entire clan!","It is also because of this put out, those who look at her whip, even if it is envious eyes, but also only dare to look at, do not dare to take her whip.","Otherwise, the person who seized the whip must have the ability to withstand her master's anger and killing intent, otherwise, who dares to rush to death? A treasure was no better, if it could not be taken out and used, then it was no different from waste.","Patriarch Xiao looked at the whip in his hand, his palm stroked over the body of the whip, he felt an ability coalesce on top of the whip, and he couldn't help but marvel, \"It's truly worthy of being a Divine Whip.\""]},{"number":4919,"title":"Chapter 4919: It’s hard to refuse the favor","paragraphs":["Chapter 4919: It’s hard to refuse the favor","Clan elders also surrounded forward to see, to their eyes, can be called by them treasure, that is naturally a piece of extraordinary treasure undoubtedly, just, look at this whip, but they do not dare to mess with the mind.","Now that they had seen this whip, naturally they had determined that this little girl was no doubt Azure Emperor’s disciple Yun Qi. Not to mention, no one dared to harbour the idea of keeping this whip as their own and they had to also treat her as a distinguished guest, can’t be neglected.","Not to mention the origin of her birth, alone her master is Azure Emperor this point, it was already extraordinary.","Patriarch Xiao walked down and handed the whip to her personally, saying, “Now that it has been established that you are Azure Emperor’s disciple, it is just that, how did you appear here? Does your master know?”","Yue’er’s gaze moved, then she said, “My master told me to come out for training, it’s just that I didn’t know how I came here, originally, I wasn’t meant to come here.”","“Oh? Then where were you originally going?” Patriarch Xiao asked.","Yue’er pursed her lips and shook her head, “Can’t say.”","Upon hearing this, Patriarch Xiao smiled lowly and said, “That’s fine, then you are here in my Xiao Family now, are you going back to Yunxiao Mountain? Or do you want to stay in the Xiao Family for a while longer? Or do you want to go to the place you originally wanted to go? Do you need me to send someone to send you?”","“You can just send me out of your boundary here, I can go back by myself, I don’t need you to send me.” She said in a hurry. She had snuck out and had yet to see Mother! Didn’t want to go back so soon.","“That’s fine, then ...” Before he could finish his words, he saw Xiao Junyan standing up while interrupting him.","“Patriarch, I’ll send her back! After all, she’s still so young, it’s not too safe for her to be out alone.”","“No need, my master let me come out to train, it was to let me be alone.” Yue’er immediately said.","As Azure Emperor’s beloved disciple, with Azure Emperor’s skill, naturally it was impossible to let her be alone outside, there would definitely be some arrangement, he was also clear about the strong man’s divine sense guarding, it was estimated that Azure Emperor’s wisp of divine sense “was in her body, and if she really encountered any fatal dangers, she would also definitely show up to save her.","If he let someone follow her to protect her, it would be redundant.","Thinking of this, he said to Xiao Junyan, “Junyan, you are the young master of the Xiao family, our Xiao family has been avoiding the world for many years, without the order of the Old Predecessor, no one is allowed to go out of the Immortal Island for even half a step, and that’s you as well.”","He glanced at Xiao Junyan who pursed his lips and said, “Yun Qi is Azure Emperor’s beloved disciple, Azure Emperor will give her the magic treasure to protect her, it is not our turn to worry about her safety, since she wants to leave alone, we will take care of it ourselves.”","Xiao Junyan didn’t say anything, just looked towards that little doll, his complexion slightly moving, he didn’t know what he was thinking about.","“Many thanks, Patriarch Xiao.” Yue’er made a decent bow towards him and thanked him.","Patriarch Xiao smiled, looked at her, and said, “Yun Qi, your master and my family’s Old Predecessor are also acquainted with each other, so since you have come here, then stay for two more days before leaving! I’ll have Junyan show you around our Xiao Family’s Immortal Island, it’s not too late to leave after a couple days.”","Upon hearing this, Yue’er thought for a moment and was about to speak when she heard that Xiao Junyan immediately responded.","“Don’t worry Second Uncle, I will take her around for a bit to fulfill the duty.” Xiao Junyan said, and when he looked at Yun Qi, the corner of his lips slightly hooked up.","Seeing this, even though Yue’er was unwilling, she had no choice but to respond, “Mm....alright, then I will stay for two more days.”"]},{"number":4920,"title":"Chapter 4920: Arriving at the Immortal Island","paragraphs":["Chapter 4920: Arriving at the Immortal Island","Seeing this, Patriarch Xiao told Xiao Junyan to take her to look around and have some fun.","After watching them leave, a clan elder stroked his beard and then spoke, “I really didn’t expect her to be Azure Emperor’s disciple, it seems that this lion, too, is not going to come back.”","“Ha ha, it’s fine, after all, it was only after eating her medicinal pills that it advanced. It’s also considered to be destiny with her, so it should be hers.” Patriarch Xiao waved his hand nonchalantly and said with a smile. After all, a Sacred Beast was just a Sacred Beast, and would not be too much of a concern.","On this side, the people on the hall were sitting and chatting about some things, over there, Xiao Junyan brought Yue’er to the Xiao family’s immortal mansion and started to show her around...","On the other side, Feng Jiu brought her two sons to the immortal island, when the airship arrived at the island, she brought them down from the airship, and flew towards the boundary.","The flying feather at her waist was thrown out, she sat on top of the feather, reached out and wrapped her arms around her two sons, one sitting on her left and right, and said to them with a smile, “Look, this is our home, after Mother removes all the potential dangers, she will pick you up and bring you back to live here.”","“Mother, this place is so beautiful, it seems like a fairyland, even better than both Master’s Yunxiao Mountain and Immortal Elder Lingmu’s place.” Hao’er said, his eyes glowing brightly as he looked at everything underneath with relish.","“Mother, there’s also the Rainbow Bridge there!” Hao’er pointed towards that rainbow bridge, his little face also glowing with surprise.","“Well, Mother will take you there to take a look.” Feng Jiu smiled and said, leading them towards that rainbow bridge. They didn’t come down to walk around, but sat on the flying feather and slowly flew over.","The two children reached out their hands to caress it, as if they felt that the rainbow was right between their palms, that feeling, it was marvelous.","“Everything here is immortal qi illusion, all in the real existence will not disappear. Other places are also very beautiful, not losing out to here. Some time ago, I received another great emperor’s immortal island. Now that the two islands have been merged, the place has expanded a lot so even if you want to stroll through the entire immortal island, it is estimated that you would need at least teo to three days to completely tour it.”","Feng Jiu laughed lightly, leading them towards the immortal mansion, while saying, “Due to the fact that Dufan and the others are unable to come up, nowadays there are fewer people here at Mother’s place. However, during this period of time, I’m also met and brought over a few interesting people. One of them cooks very well, so later on, I’ll let her make you guys some delicious food.”","“Yeah!”","The two of them responded crisply as their eyes glowed, and thinking of their Father, they asked, “Mother, when will Father be able to come up to be with us?”","“It’s not too easy to say about your Father’s condition, but when he awakens in the day, it’s probably not far from the day of ascension.” She spoke softly, rubbed the two’s heads, and laughed, “Don’t worry about him, he’s warming up his divine soul, he’s very safe there, he’ll be fine, if we wait for too long and he hasn’t come up yet, then when that time comes, Mother will think of a way to break through the Nine Heavens’ Heavenly Realm’s territorial isolation, and bring you guys down to look for him.”","“Mother, in the future, will Grandfather and the others also come here to live with us?” Muchen asked, having missed that relatives on the distant territory.","Hearing this, Feng Jiu smiled, softly said, “As long as they want to come, naturally they can come up to live with us, however, the Feng family old mansion there, is where your Grandfather and Great Grandfather they grew up, also have feelings, they can’t let go of there may be, in the future, even if it is separated from the two places, as long as the heavenly boundary territory is opened, it is also convenient to go back and forth. ”","As she spoke, she saw the figure waving her hand towards her in front of the Immortal Mansion’s door ..."]},{"number":4921,"title":"Chapter 4921: Stay","paragraphs":["Capítulo 4921: Stay","“Sister Feng!” Song Mi’er stood in front of the Immortal Mansion’s door waving her hand, looking at the red figure coming back, her face filled with excitement. Just a little surprised, she looked at the two delicate and good-looking children beside her.","Feng Jiu brought the two children to a stop in front of the gate of the mansion, collected the flying feathers, smiled at Song Mi’er and asked, “Why are you here? Could it be that you still know that I’m coming back?”","“No, I was preparing to go to the forest to take a look around, I didn’t expect to see Sister Feng come back.” As she said that, a pair of eyes stared straight towards the two children and asked curiously, “Sister Feng, who are they?”","“These are my two sons, Xuanyuan Hao, Xuanyuan Muchen.” Feng Jiu looked at the two children beside her and said, “She is Song Mi’er, the one Mother told you about, the sister who can cook a lot of delicious food.”","However, the two listened to her words, but they looked at each other, Hao’er said, “Mother, she called you sister, then we can still call her sister?”","Hearing this, Feng Jiu was stunned, then smiled, “Then how about calling Aunt?”","“Oh my, aunt is too old, I’m still young! Just call me Mi’er!” Mi’er said smilingly, her soulful gaze turned to look at Feng Jiu and said with some embarrassment, “I’ve thought about it for a while, hey, this, that ... Can I call you Master like Uncle Tie and the others? I also want to stay here in the future as well.”","Hearing this, Feng Jiu raised her eyebrows, “Recognize me as master? Stay here with me? Don’t you still have to travel around and cultivate?”","“I think this place is quite good, it’s a big place, and there’s really a lot of mountain treasures in that forest, so ...” she looked at her, a pleasing smile on her face.","The more important point was that she was the Phoenix Sovereign! Such a big golden thigh in front of her, if she didn’t hug it, wouldn’t she be scolded to death by her father and several brothers back home?","What’s more, she does like her, although she is the Phoenix Sovereign, but she does not treat others with arrogance. Instead, she felt she was very affable. After living here for a period of time, her cultivation has also improved, and the environment here was really very good.","If she didn’t recognize her as her master, it wouldn’t be a good idea to keep on staying here, so she thought about it, the best way was to let her accept her, then she would be able to live here with peace of mind.","“Master, just take me in! You’re short of a cook by your side anyway, so I’ll take care of all the meals here from now on!” She went forward and lightly held her hand and acted coquettishly.","Seeing this, Feng Jiu smiled and said, “Alright, go in first! Later on, you will make some food for the two children, so that they can replenish their bodies properly.”","“Sure thing!” She instantly smiled and looked at the two Hao’er and Muchen, saying, “Let’s go in! I’ve recently developed a new dish, so I’ll make it for you later.”","Once inside, Mi’er went to cook first, while Feng Jiu took the two children to the compound she had reserved for them first.","When Tie Song and Yueniang learned that Feng Jiu had returned, they came to pay their respects, and were also a little surprised that Feng Jiu had two children.","After all, there was no one else in this immortal island other than them, not to mention they didn’t hear about her other relatives or anything like that, and all of a sudden they brought back two children, saying that they were her children, the two of them were naturally surprised.","However, the two didn’t ask more questions, after all, Feng Jiu was their Master, and they had no right to ask about her matters."]},{"number":4922,"title":"Chapter 4922: Sending Off","paragraphs":["Capítulo 4922: Sending Off","After paying their respects, the two men retired first.","And after they left, Hao’er asked, “Mother, why would you want to bring them here?” Even though their Mother did not have many people to call on, if Du Fan and the others came up in the future, she would naturally not worry about not having people around her, so he wondered how she could have taken in those two people who did not have any special features.","“Tie Song is an excellent refiner, leaving him behind is naturally so that some weapons and such can be refined by him in the future.” She smiled as she looked at the two children and said, “As long as one is talented and feels that the person is usable, they can keep them.”","Upon hearing this, the two nodded, while their hearts were thinking about what their Mother had said. As long as one was talented, no matter what type of person they were, they could be taken in for their own use.","Due to their arrival, Fire Phoenix and Old White they also came in front of the two and circled around them.","When Feng Jiu saw this, she smiled and said to the several contracted beasts, “Alright, all disperse!” Saying this, she looked at the two children again and said, “Take a rest first, I’ll call you two in a while when the food is ready, and tomorrow I will accompany you to look around again.”","“Mm hmm.” The two of them responded and watched her and the contracted beasts leave before going to the courtyards their Mother had prepared for each of them to rest.","What made this place different from their master’s Yunxiao Mountain was that there were immortal maidservants that were transformed into illusions, and some of those immortal maidservants were transformed into cranes, while others were transformed into flowers, herbs, and spiritual medicines, which could be used for them to call upon.","Moreover, this place was also large, the two of them each have an exquisite and secluded courtyard, which is also some distance away from each other. For them who often lived in the cave abode, they naturally preferred this kind of tranquil and elegant courtyard.","Compared to how cozy and happy they were in this immortal mansion, Yue’er on the other side was bored. Even with Xiao Junyan accompanying her around, she still had a lack of interest.","It was not easy to stay for two days, but early in the morning, she ran to find that Patriarch of the Xiao Family and said that she wanted to leave.","“You’re leaving? Not staying for a few more days?” Patriarch Xiao asked, looking at that little tiny person, a smile came on his face.","“Not staying, I’m leaving.” She blinked a pair of beautiful eyes and looked at him as she spoke.","Seeing this, he nodded and said, “That’s fine, then I’ll send you off! Follow me.” Saying this, he took a step outside, signaling her to follow.","A smile appeared on Yue’er’s face as she hurriedly followed.","He brought her to the exit of the Immortal Island, looking at the sky outside, he then smiled, “Whenever you have the chance in the future, come over with your master to walk around, our Xiao family is always welcome.”","“Good. Thank you Patriarch Xiao.” She said with a small adult look as she bowed towards him.","Patriarch Xiao nodded, looked back and asked, “When you came over to me, Junyan didn’t know?”","“I didn’t tell him and came out early myself.” Because they lived in the same compound, but it was also divided into the front and back yards, she woke up early and came out by herself, he naturally did not know.","Hearing this, Patriarch Xiao didn’t say anything else, but just said, “Alright! Take care of yourself with more protection along the way.” Saying that, with a flick of his sleeve, the boundary formation in front of him opened an opening, and in the next moment, he sent Yue’er out.","Only after watching her silhouette disappear into the clouds, and not knowing where she landed, did he withdraw his gaze and close the boundary and formation again."]},{"number":4923,"title":"Chapter 4923: Smashed down","paragraphs":["Capítulo 4923: Smashed down","As soon as he turned around, he saw Xiao Junyan hurriedly swept from afar, seeing this, he waited for him to arrive before he said, “You are late.”","The moment Xiao Junyan came to his side and heard his words, a glint flashed past his eyes as he looked to the clouds where her silhouette had disappeared.","In fact, the moment she had left the courtyard, he had noticed it. Only, he rushed to see his grandfather early in the morning, wanting to ask for permission to leave the island, but, in the end, was not allowed.","“After so many years, it’s the first time I’ve seen you so attached to someone.” Patriarch Xiao looked at him with his hand in the air and said, “You work hard on your cultivation! In the near future, you will also have to go out to the island to travel, she is Azure Emperor’s disciple, at that time, if you want to see her, you can just visit Yunxiao Mountain again.”","Perhaps because he heard his words, the original somewhat lost look was swept away, and what appeared instead was a look of anticipation in his eyes, he arched his hand and said a thank you to him, “Thank you, Second Uncle, I know.” With that, he also stopped staying, but turned to leave.","After watching him regain his old demeanor, Patriarch Xiao let out a light sigh, and followed him back.","On the other side, Yue’er who was sent away directly landed on a stage in the city below, the two cultivators on the stage were fighting, which knew that they had just divided the winners and losers, and the one who won stood on the stage and was unexpectedly knocked out by Yue’er, who smashed down from the sky on the stage.","This scene came extremely fast, even, let the cultivators under the stage could not react in time, just one by one stunned to look at that little girl who suddenly smashed down from the sky.","The surroundings became silent due to this sudden scene, and after a moment of bizarre silence, the stage clamored and the crowd talked.","“Where did this child come from? How did she smash down from above?”","“How did this happen? How did it knock someone out?”","“This is also too unreasonable, who threw such a small child down from the sky?”","“It doesn’t seem like it was thrown, right? Just now there seemed to be a current of air holding her down, otherwise the person who was knocked out wouldn’t have stood there dumbfounded and unresponsive and been knocked out.”","“Yes, I also saw just now, when this child smashed down, there was a very powerful aura protecting her, and that aura only disappeared after she smashed down on that cultivator.”","The people under the stage were discussing, and Yue’er who was sitting on that person’s back was also stunned, looking down at the person she was sitting on, she hurriedly stood up, patted her little buttocks, and then by the way, straightened up the little dress on her body.","Looking around, she wanted to get off the stage, but saw that people were surrounding her, with pairs of eyes staring at her as if she was looking at some rare animal.","“Make way, make way, I’m going down.” Yue’er stepped off the stage from the side, saying that while squeezing down.","“Kid, where did you come from? Where is your family’s adult? You smashed someone unconscious shouldn’t just want to leave like this, right?” A cultivator asked, while also blocking her path to prevent her from leaving.","Yue’er raised her head towards that person, seeing his pair of tiny eyes swirling around her body, she asked crisply, “You won’t let me leave?”","“Of course you can’t leave, you smashed someone unconscious, how can you just walk away? Naturally, you have to compensate something.” The cultivator said, revealing a light smile.","The surrounding people listened, but didn’t say anything, they just glanced at the cultivator. This person wouldn’t be trying to get something out of this child, right? It was also a little too shameless."]},{"number":4924,"title":"Chapter 4924: Invitation","paragraphs":["Capítulo 4924: Invitation","After Yue’er glanced at the man, she looked back at the man she had smashed unconscious, her childish voice softly said, “He was only smashed unconscious by me, he is not injured, he will wake up in a while.”","“Heh! Who said that? Call out your family’s adult!” The cultivator wrapped his hands around his chest and sneered.","Yue’er’s eyes turned and looked at him with a sweet smile, “Mm, alright.” As soon as her voice fell, she moved her mind and with a flash of light, a majestic lion appeared in front of the crowd.","“Rooooooar!”","A lion’s roar, accompanied by the pressure of a Sacred Beast, instantly scared off the circle of people around them, along with the cultivator who was blocking the front, he also backed up due to shock, and inadvertently fell to the ground.","Yue’er patted the lion beside her and said with a smile, “What do you have to say? Tell it!”","The surrounding crowd looked at the lion that had suddenly appeared, each of them staring at it with a pair of wide eyes. If they hadn’t seen it with their own eyes, who would believe that such a little girl actually had a contracted beast this powerful!","“This, this is a Sacred Beast!”","A cultivator said, his pace involuntarily backing up. For a little girl to have such a powerful contract beast, there were only two possibilities.","One was that she came from an extremely prominent family, and the other was that she had an extremely powerful backer behind her.","And no matter which one of these two it was, it was not something they dared to mess with.","The people around her automatically made a path for her, even the cultivator who had blocked her path earlier, at this time, he also hurriedly got up and retreated to the side, his eyes looking at the lion with a few moments of fire and a few moments of fear.","Sacred Beast ah! Such a powerful contracted beast, how is it that such a child contracted it?","Watching the crowd make way, the lion plopped down so that its little master could climb onto its back.","Yue’er called the lion out, naturally, she didn’t want to hide it in the space anymore, after all, when she was a child outside, in order to avoid trouble, it was best to have something that could shock them, so that those who had bad intentions wouldn’t dare to hit her.","Therefore, after the lion got down, she rolled over and rode onto its back, which led her away from the path that the crowd had retreated from, and rode the lion through the streets of the city, looking for an inn to stay.","A Sacred Beast came out of the city, and it was also a little girl riding around on the streets, once the news spread, the City Lord of the city personally came out to see what was going on.","“City Lord, it’s that little girl.” A guard pointed at the little girl riding a lion at the entrance of the inn ahead and said.","“Is this her looking for an inn to stay in?” The City Lord looked at the scene in front of him with a bewildered expression, because that lion was too conspicuous, wherever it went, it commanded a circle of people surrounding it.","“Yes, she should be an outsider, and has no relatives in this city, so she can only look for an inn to settle down, only, because that lion is too scary, those inns don’t dare to receive her.” That guard whispered.","Seeing this, that City Lord paused for a moment, and then walked forward. The people surrounding saw that it was the City Lord arriving and automatically made way.","When Yue’er, who was riding the lion, saw the crowd retreating, she looked back and saw a middle-aged man walking towards her.","“Little girl, I am the City Lord of this city, you are from out of town, right? How about, how about landing at the City Lord’s Manor?” The City Lord revealed a smile and inquired, while not moving, he sized up the child in front of him."]},{"number":4925,"title":"Chapter 4925: Far Away","paragraphs":["For having a Sacred Beast at such a young age, it was obvious that she must be from a great family, or behind a powerful backer. Since she came to the city, as the City Lord, it was only right to extend a warm invitation and host her properly during her stay.","Yue’er thought about it, since she had yet to find a place to stay, and seeing that this person was the City Lord, she then nodded, revealing a touch of innocent and joyful smile: \"Thank you, City Lord, then I’m sorry to bother you.\"","See, at this young age, her demeanor was generous, and it was even more evident that she was from an extraordinary background.","The surrounding crowd secretly thought, a pair of eyes fell on that child, all guessing, which sect was she from?","When the City Lord saw her nod, he immediately led her towards the City Lord’s Manor.","When the people in the city saw this, they discussed a bit and then dispersed.","Not to mention the City Lord’s reception, even without the City Lord’s appearance, that little girl was surrounded by Sacred Beasts, and the general public would not dare to take action against her easily.","In the City Lord’s Manor, after Yue’er was brought to a courtyard by the City Lord himself, he said to him with a smile, \"Little girl, I still don’t know what’s your name? Can you tell me?\"","Yue’er looked at this courtyard, and then looked at this City Lord, listening to his self-introduction on the way, she heard that he was surnamed Guo, and that the Guo family was a big family here, due to being elected by the various families in the City to be the City Lord.","After roughly understanding some things, listening to his inquiry, she thought for a moment and then said, \"My name is Yun Qi.\"","\"Oh? Yun Qi? Which place are you from? Why are you here alone?\" City Lord Guo asked with slight surprise.","Yue’er smiled sweetly and said crisply, \"My master doesn’t like me saying his name around.\"","As soon as her voice fell, Yue’er asked again, \"City Lord, which Great Emperor’s territory is this?\"","The City Lord heard her say that she couldn’t speak her master’s name around, and was contemplating what her master could be. Just as he heard her inquiring about the Great Emperor of this territory, he couldn’t help but laugh and said, \"The Great Emperor of this territory we are in is surnamed Xiao, and is known as the Great Emperor of the Southern Heaven, one of the Ten Great Emperors, what are you doing asking about this when you’re a little kid?\"","\"So, this is the territory of that Southern Heavenly Emperor, huh? I heard about a very powerful Great Emperor who ascended some time ago, is her territory still far from here?\" Yue Xin asked, her heart a little anxious. When this Patriarch Xiao sent her away, why did he even send her to their Patriarch Xiao’s territory? Why didn’t he send her farther away?","\"The one you’re talking about is the Female Emperor Phoenix Sovereign, she’s the first female emperor in the last ten thousand years, moreover, she’s also an extraordinary figure.\" The City Lord laughed, walked to the table in the courtyard and sat down, saying, \"It is true that her territory is a bit far from here, after all, the territories that separate them are different.\"","Saying that, he looked towards the little girl whose expression was a bit tangled, and asked with a smile, \"You’re so young, how come you’re net interested in those big characters? Those kinds of characters are not something that people like you and I can see.\"","Yue’er looked at him, and secretly thought: that is my Mother, why can’t I see her?","However, she was just a bit listless on the table, the tiny person sighed and said, \"I’m not curious! I heard that it’s very powerful! I also want to see it, who knows it’s still so far away.\"","Saying that, she sat up straight again and asked, \"If we go from here, how long will it take to get there if we fly?\"","The City Lord thought for a moment and said, \"It would take a month or so at the earliest.\""]},{"number":4926,"title":"Chapter 4926: Appointment","paragraphs":["As he said that, he looked at the little person across from him and said, \"You should rest here first! It’s a long way to go, so there’s no rush, but if you’re going to such a faraway place, do your elders know about it?\"","After all, it was such a young child, even if there was a Sacred Beast protecting her, there was still something wrong after all.","\"Know know know, they know.\" Yue’er immediately nodded and said, only her gaze flickered. It was estimated that her master had already known that she had snuck away, it was just that she didn’t know if her master would be angry?","\"Then you rest first! If there is anything you need then order your maidservant to go and do it, or go to the front yard to find me as well.\" City Lord Guo stood up and handed over a few words before leaving first.","Because there was such a little girl in the mansion, the people underneath did not know where she came from, therefore, he gave instructions to treat her with the manners of a honored guest, so that the people underneath would not be half-indulgent.","Yue’er walked around in the courtyard for a while, looked around, and then went to one of the biggest rooms in the center to rest.","Here in the City Lord’s Manor, due to the City Lord’s instructions, the people in the mansion didn’t dare to disturb that little noble guest.","On the contrary, at noon on the following day, the Guo’s family Old Predecessor, who had just come out from seclusion, and heard that there was a little girl in the house accompanied by a Sacred Beast, and so, he sent someone to summon the City Lord over to inquire about it.","\"Honored Predecessor, that child said that her name is Yun Qi, and that she came out to practice by order of her master, but from her words and actions, I learned that she wanted to go to the territory of the Phoenix Sovereign, and since I saw that she was generous at her young age, and that she had a Sacred Beast accompanying her, I invited her to come to the house to rest.\"","Patriarch Guo respectfully reported what he knew about Yun Qi related matters to the Old Predecessor sitting at the stone table in the courtyard, this was their Guo Family’s Old Patriarch, it was because of the Old Patriarch’s existence that their Guo Family could be the City Lord of the City.","To know, his father and grandfather as well as his great grandfather had all perished after failing to advance, and nowadays, their Guo Family, there was only such an Old Predecessor left to sit on the throne.","Without this Old Predecessor, it was estimated that their Guo Family would not even be able to squeeze into the circle of the city’s families and nobles.","That old man with white hair and beard, wearing a simple white wide robe, at this time was drinking tea while listening to what he said, after a long time, he said, \"I just received an invitation yesterday, an old friend from my old life invited me to go to a banquet, if that child is really as you said, I can also give her a ride.\"","Hearing these words, Patriarch Guo was stunned and cautiously asked, \"The place where Old Predecessor is going to the banquet is also the territory where the Emperor Phoenix Sovereign is located?\"","\"That’s right.\" The old man stroked his beard, revealing a hint of a smile and said, \"Speaking of which, it has been a long time since I’ve seen this old friend, and this time, because of the great joy of his coming out of seclusion for many years and advancing in rank, he invited me to go.\"","Knowing that his Old Predecessor had a late friend that powerful, Patriarch Guo was also very joyful, and immediately said, \"Then I will summon Yun Qi here for Old Predecessor to meet?\"","The old man paused for a moment, stood up with a flick of his sleeve, and said, \"No need, you take me over there, I’ll take a look first before I say anything.\"","\"Yes.\" Patriarch Guo respectfully responded and led him to the small courtyard.","Even though Yue’er had left Yunxiao Mountain, she did not fall behind in her cultivation even when the conditions allowed it. Just like at this moment, she was practicing her fist technique in the courtyard, one move at a time, over and over again.","City Lord Guo brought his own Old Predecessor to the small courtyard and was about to open his mouth when he raised his hand to stop him."]},{"number":4927,"title":"Chapter 4927: Travelling together","paragraphs":["Seeing his Old Predecessor quietly observing the little girl in the courtyard, City Lord Guo didn’t say anything and just waited quietly.","The old man watched for a while, but he couldn’t tell which of this little girl’s stance paths was actually from which family? His eyes turned and landed on the lion lying in the corner.","It was indeed a Sacred Beast, but the aura should be that of a Sacred Beast that had just recently advanced. Just, no matter when the Sacred Beast was advanced, for such a young child to be able to contract this Sacred Beast, it would indeed not be simple.","The lion was lying on the corner of the compound looking at the two people at the entrance of the compound, after all, it was someone else’s place, therefore, it didn’t let out a roaring sound at them, it just reminded its own master.","Yue’er stopped after practicing for a while, she looked towards the entrance of the courtyard, her soft and sticky voice called out, \"City Lord?\"","\"Cough.\" City Lord Guo coughed lightly and glanced at his family’s Old Predecessor, only after seeing the Old Predecessor walk into the courtyard did he hurriedly follow her in, smiling as he said, \"Yun Qi, this is my Guo family’s Old Predecessor, who just happened to be passing by, and came over to see if you’re used to living here.\"","Hearing these words, Yue’er’s big beautiful eyes curved, smilingly looked at the two of them and said, \"Thank you City Lord, this place is very good.\"","\"The little girl’s name is Yun Qi?\" The old man looked at the little girl in front of him and asked.","\"Uh-huh.\" Yue’er nodded.","Seeing her unperturbed and smiling little appearance, the old man’s smile deepened and he said, \"I heard that you are going to the territory where the Phoenix Sovereign is located? Are you going to visit your relatives or return home?\"","\"To play.\" Yue’er said with a smile.","\"So, you have no destination?\" The old man asked again.","Yue’er blinked her two innocent eyes and she did not speak.","The old man stroked his beard, walked over to the table and sat down, saying, \"The old man was invited by an old friend, and intends to go to a banquet in the next two days, if you are also going there, you can also take a ride along with me, and spare you the pain of running all the way around.\"","Upon hearing this, Yue’er asked, \"How long will it take you to arrive from here?\" If it was also a month or so, why would she need to follow him?","The moment her words came out, it caused the two to freeze for a moment, their gazes sweeping over Yun Qi’s body, a smirk crossing their eyes.","The moment this little girl’s words came out, they knew what she meant. Dare they still think that if the time to go together is the same as her going on the road alone, she still plans to go on the road alone, doesn’t she?","The old man laughed, stroked his beard, looked at Patriarch Guo, and asked, \"How long did you tell her this trip would take?\"","\"Back to Old Predecessor, I told Yun Qi that the fastest estimate would be more than a month.\" Patriarch Guo said.","The old man nodded, looked at Yun Qi, and smiled, \"For this trip, ten days is sufficient for the old man.\"","\"Ten days?\" Yue’er was delighted, her eyes widened in surprise, \"It’s really only ten days? Then, I’ll go with you!\" Ten days, that’s a lot of time to shorten! She was stupid not to follow along.","When the old man heard this, he laughed and was about to speak, when he heard the sound of her stomach rumbling, he was stunned.","\"Hee hee, I’m hungry.\" Yue’er touched her stomach with one hand, but she did not feel a trace of discomfort.","\"I’ll have someone prepare food.\" City Lord Guo said, then turned around and went outside, delivering a message.","The old man looked at her and asked with a smile, \"You haven’t started to fast yet?\"","\"I usually eat, eating is the only way to grow up.\" Yue’er said in a serious manner.","Rarely seeing such a child who was not afraid of him and was quirky, the old man’s smile grew wider as he said to the City Lord who walked back and stood by the side, \"Turn around and give instructions to the kitchen, prepare some things for her to eat on the road as well.\""]},{"number":4928,"title":"Chapter 4928: Vacation","paragraphs":["\"Yes.\" City Lord Guo responded, glancing towards that Yun Qi. It seemed that this child was very much in his family’s Old Predecessor’s favor, knowing that no one in the entire Guo Family dared to speak to their Old Predecessor in such a casual manner.","The next day, early in the morning, when City Lord Guo handed Yue’er the prepared dried food and pastries and whatnot, he said, \"There’s meat and dried food in here as well as some pastries and whatnot, all of which can be put away for a long time, it should be enough for you to eat on the road.\"","\"Many thanks City Lord.\" Yue’er took it and bowed.","\"Alright, come up!\" The old man had already waved to release a small airship at some point, looking simple and plain, and it wasn’t too big.","\"Bye~\" Yue’er waved her hand and then leapt up to land inside the small airship. Because the lion was put into the space, although the boat was small, the two of them had some places to sit, whether they wanted to sit or lie down.","Below the City Lord waved his hand, saw the small airship swoosh to the clouds, instantly disappeared in the clouds, see this, he looked for a moment, then turned around and walked back.","He didn’t expect that the Old Predecessor hadn’t gone out for a long time, but this time he would be willing to bring such a child along, however, with the Old Predecessor traveling with her on this trip, that Yun Qi child should be able to safely reach the place she wants to go ...","On the other hand, in the middle of the immortal island, since Feng Jiu had instructed Song Mi’er and told her that she wanted to raise the two children to be stronger, therefore, it could be said that the food in the past few days were mainly for the two children.","On the one hand, Feng Jiu was not idle either, taking the two children around this immortal island she merged, while instructing them on their cultivation, allowing the two to spar more.","It could be said that the days here with their Mother accompanying them were joyful and fulfilling, but not easy either. However, the two of them were happy with it, because here, they had their Mother with them.","This day, Feng Jiu called the two over, looking at the two sons, her eyes with doting as well as soft, said: \"Mother take you to go around the city below! It’s also good to let you guys practice more, as well as learn to cope with problems.\"","Upon hearing this, the two looked at each other and asked, \"Mother, if we go down like this, won’t our identities be known?\"","\"How difficult is that? A bit of disguise will do.\" She laughed softly and pinched the two children’s cheeks, saying, \"I heard you guys say that your master has also allowed you to experience alone, so let Mother see your abilities as well as your resilience, and when we get down there, Mother will only be an onlooker and won’t make any moves to help you.\"","\"Mother don’t worry, we won’t let Mother down.\" The two immediately said.","\"Master, Master, I want to go along too!\" Song Mi’er trotted in and said, \"I’ll go cook for you guys!\"","Feng Jiu smiled, glanced at her and said, \"That’s fine, follow along!\"","Muchen hesitated for a moment and looked at his Mother and asked, \"Mother, is it true that after taking us on a training trip this time, Mother is going to send us away?\" Compared to his master’s Yunxiao Mountain, he wanted to stay by his Mother’s side even more.","Feng Jiu rubbed his slightly wrinkled little eyebrows with both hands and laughed, \"Don’t frown all the time at a young age, don’t worry, I won’t send you guys back so soon, in a few days, Mother will take you guys to visit your Uncle Mo Chen.\"","\"Yeah!\" Hearing that they would not be sent away too quickly, Muchen’s brows loosened, and between his brows, a joyful smile overflowed."]},{"number":4929,"title":"Chapter 4929: Poisonous Hand","paragraphs":["Feng Jiu left a transmission jade for Tie Song and Yueniang, asking them to send a message to her if someone named Yuan Jing came to the island to seek medical treatment, and after arranging the following day, she took the two children and Mi’er out of the immortal island together.","On the other hand, Yue’er followed the Guo Family Old Predecessor in that airship, she sat on the side of the boat and looked at the clouds passing by outside, blinked her eyes and said, \"How can this small boat fly so fast? It’s much faster than flying with a sword and magical artifacts in general.\"","The old man stroked his beard and half-smiled off his eyes as he said, \"Naturally, it’s because this airship of mine is not an ordinary magical artifact, otherwise, how could I have told you that we would arrive in about ten days?\"","\"Although that’s the case, but, Grandfather Guo, can’t we go down and rest for a while?\" Yue’er was lying on the edge of the small boat, blinking her beautiful eyes at him.","\"Hm? Take a break? You can rest on this airship!\" He glanced towards the inside of the small boat. There was still plenty of room! How did she want to rest?","Seeing this, Yue’er sighed with a small adult look and said bitterly, \"You don’t eat grains and meat and even exempt people from the three urgent matters, but what I eat are still grains and meat! I want to relieve myself.\"","Hearing this, the old man was stunned for a moment, his gaze looking her up and down, frowning as he asked, \"So this is you wanting to go down and relieve yourself?\" Why had he not thought that this child had these three urgent problems? It looked like he was incidentally bringing trouble to himself!","\"Uh huh.\" Yue’er hurriedly nodded. She had been holding her breath all the way, only to see that he didn’t want to stop and take a break, so she couldn’t help but open her mouth.","Seeing this, with a flick of the old man’s sleeve, the airship headed downwards, stopping in a small forest, he came down and walked around for a bit, and said to Yun Qi, \"Go quickly! Don’t go too far.\"","\"Mmm hmm.\" Yue’er responded, coming out of the airship and running towards the place in the forest with lots of weeds.","The old man walked around with his hands on his back, stretching his muscles and bones, with his eyes closed, he only listened to the light wind in the woods that made a rustling sound as it brushed the leaves, the birds on the branches squeaked, and he took a deep breath, but his brows were furrowed, and he opened his gaze.","Between the air, there was the odor of blood.","The smell of blood with the light wind and blowing, do not know from which direction, he slowed down the pace, to one of the direction, about out of more than fifty metres away, see in the distance of about a hundred metres, the ground was littered with corpses.","He paused for a moment, thinking that this kind of thing, it is best not to be curious, so as not to get into what should not be caused by the trouble on the body. However, just as he was about to withdraw his sight and turn around to leave, he felt a divine sense locking onto him.","Upon sensing that a divine sense had landed on his body, his body stiffened and he immediately stepped back, a flash of vigilance crossing his eyes. Because, from that divine sense alone, he felt a powerful pressure and killing intent.","\"Swoooosh!\"","Just as he was retreating, a stern sound swooshed through the air at an extremely fast speed and attacked Old Predeccessor Guo, who reacted swiftly with his instincts to avoid it, and saw that airflow swoosh into a large tree at his side.","Fixed eyes to see, that is only a palm little finger thick flooded with black light sleeve arrow, from that arrow end of the black light to see, that arrow oozing poison!","\"I’m just passing by, I have no intention of making an enemy of Your Excellency, why would Your Excellency do such a poisonous thing!\""]},{"number":4930,"title":"Chapter 4930: Killing Intent","paragraphs":["Old Predeccessor Guo’s face at this time also sank, the other side of the cold will be killed, this is simply intended to silence. But all he did was had a look at those corpses only, yet that person even want to kill him just becaue of that! What a malicious and vile person!","\"Who let you have such bad luck? You met this seat here!\"","A cold and low voice came, and the next moment, he saw that about a hundred metres away, several black silhouettes swept out at an extremely fast speed, and the murderous aura came along with them.","Old Predeccessor Guo turned his sleeves, he held his wide sleeves in his palms, at the same time, his spirit energy surged, and as the powerful airflow surged out, a fist struck heavily towards the figure that swept in front of him.","\"Whoosh!\"","The speed was fast, the force was heavy, and it brought up a harsh whistling sound, and immediately afterward, it was the sound of bang after bang that landed heavily on the chest of that black figure.","Just, in that black figure was knocked out dozens of meters away with a grunt, at the same time, Old Predeccessor Guo also quickly retracted his hand down on the side, blood, from his hands between the loose wide sleeves seeped out, dripping into the ground in the soil.","That person’s chest has armor! And it was still the kind of armor with spikes!","\"Kill!\"","A kill order was issued, and several figures attacked, bringing with them a chilling killing intent straight towards Old Predeccessor Guo, intending to take his life in an instant!","Old Predeccessor Guo’s figure swayed slightly, the blood dripping from his hands had turned black and purple at some point, and along with it, his palms swelled up, glowing with a deadly black and purple color.","His lips were also covered in a layer of black purple, cold sweat seeped out from his forehead, while a mouthful of blood sprayed out from his mouth, he quickly retreated to avoid those people’s attacks, and was bracing himself for the fight, only that the toxins were flowing down his hands as well as his luck and into his body, making the poison he had been infected with get deeper and deeper, and at the same time, the speed of his fight was also gradually weakening, and his dodging figure was much slower as well.","Because of this, in no time at all, his body was covered in wounds.","Yue’er heard the commotion and trotted back, but was stunned when she saw the scene in front of her. She had only gone to relieve herself for a moment, how did that Guo Family’s Old Predecessor’s entire body become like that?","Seeing one of the black robed men slashing his sword towards Old Predeccessor Guo, she was shocked and hurriedly shouted, \"Lion! Quickly save him!\"","The moment her voice came out, a flash of light flew out, swooping towards that Old Predeccessor Guo, bringing him away while taking a few leaps, retreating to that airship farther away to put him down.","\"Puh!\"","Old Predeccessor Guo spewed out a mouthful of blood, looking at the tiny figure that ran up to him, his gaze narrowed, and his pale voice exclaimed in shock, \"No! Run away!\" That tiny child, how could she be a match for those people? For her to go up, it would be a death sentence!","After the lion put him down, it quickly darted towards its little master.","At the same time, when those several figures saw the child that suddenly came out, one of them turned the blade of his sword in his hand, and the sharp edge attacked towards that little girl.","As the killing intent came, Yue’er’s little face was calm and composed, facing the long sword in the other’s hand, she didn’t pull out the dagger, but turned her hand, a whip snapped in the air, and swooshed towards the long sword.","The long whip rolled the other party attacked the long sword, holding the whip hand a pull, the other party tightly holding the sword does not let go, she clenched her teeth, the palm of the palm of the spirit energy a flip, will see the long whip hooting burst out a tuft of flames coldly scurried to the black robed men who held the sword."]},{"number":4931,"title":"Chapter 4931: Recognize","paragraphs":["\"Arghhhhh!\"","The flames burned head-on, the black robed men instinctively let out a cry of alarm, their hands loosened, the sword in their hands was snatched by the long whip, and with a swoosh, they were flung towards one of the figures that swept towards the airship.","\"Whhosh!\"","Coldness came from behind, that black robed men instinctively avoided, just as he sidestepped to avoid it, he saw the long sword stabbing through, piercing into that large tree pole not far away.","That person’s grim gaze narrowed, turned back to look, his eyes fell on that little girl holding a whip in her hand, killing intent was thick around him.","\"Seek death!\"","With a cold shout, that person folded back and attacked towards that little girl.","\"Roar!\"","The lion roared, pouncing on the black robed men in front, tearing up with them.","Yue’er’s small human strength was not comparable to the other party, but she won because of her marvelous stance, and she also held the Ancient Divine Whip in her hand, which raised her combat power by several notches.","But even so, when those few people surrounded her, she was no match for them.","While she was holding on strongly on her side, she didn’t know that those few black robed men had shock and dismay in their hearts. To know along with the battle their pressure will also attack out, but this little girl can withstand their pressure, but also flexible in their sword drill to avoid, have to say not let them surprise.","And in the dark, that didn’t appear the leader of the people at this time narrowed their eyes, staring at that little girl in the hands of the strange whip, the eyes flashed, also don’t know what came to mind, all of a sudden, opened his mouth and drank: \"Retreat!\"","With a command, those few people, although not understanding, but also quickly backed up to the place where the other party’s whip attack could not stop, bloodthirsty eyes still staring at that little girl who was penetrating a different kind of viciousness.","This child was very perverse.","Look is a five or six years old little girl, but, once the battle, her body’s breath will change, the shot is also extremely harsh, the attack special pick their fatal place, and they fought, no panic, but instead of life-like dead hand, they have killed so many people, or this time to meet such a perverse child.","Yue’er was holding a whip in one hand, and a dagger in the other, and the lion was also guarding her side, at this moment, one person and one beast were vigilantly staring at the person who came out from behind the human tree.","That was a person whose whole body was hidden in a black cloak, and his face was also wearing a mask, so that his face could not be seen, but one could see that his pair of grim gazes were staring at her at that moment.","No, correctly speaking, it should be staring at the whip in her hand.","\"Ancient Divine Whip ?\" He narrowed his eyes, his voice chilling with a trace of unconcealed surprise, \"You are Azure Emperor’s disciple?\"","\"Not bad.\" Yue’er didn’t deny it, but directly admitted it. Because these few people were all very strong, she couldn’t beat them and could only use her master’s name to save her life.","\"I heard that Azure Emperor obtained the Ancient Divine Whip from Immortal Elder Lingmu and gifted it to his young disciple, I never thought that it would actually allow me to encounter it one day as well.\" He spoke with an inexplicable expression, staring at Yue’er and then at the whip in her hand, and in the next moment, pursed his lips taut.","\"Since it’s Azure Emperor’s beloved disciple, it’s just as well, withdraw.\" He withdrew his gaze and turned around, and with a flourish of his cape, he was about to leave.","\"Wait!\"","Yue’er hurriedly opened her mouth to call him back, seeing the man stopping his steps before she said, \"Give me the antidote!\" That Old Predeccessor Guo’s poison was on his face, if he didn’t have the antidote, wouldn’t he be dead?","At this moment, she didn’t realize that she still had her Mother’s antidote medicinal pill in her space! Just thinking, this poison was administered by them, they will naturally have the antidote in their body."]},{"number":4932,"title":"Chapter 4932: Many Thanks","paragraphs":["At those words, the masked man snorted and looked back at Yue’er, saying, \"This seat has only heard that Azure Emperor has taken in a few disciples, but I didn’t expect that there is still that old man.\"","\"Antidote!\" Yue’er stubbornly said.","Staring at the little girl, seeing that her gaze was not frightened or fearful, but rather staring at him like a small beast, he pulled the corners of his mouth, threw out a bottle to her, turned around and left.","When they saw their Master throw out the antidote, a flash of surprise crossed the eyes of several black robed men. It seemed that they didn’t expect their Master to actually give her the antidote.","A few figures disappeared extremely fast, after seeing them leave, Yue’er secretly sighed in relief and quickly came to the airship, at this time, Old Predeccessor Guo, who had been holding up strongly, saw Yue’er running here, and finally couldn’t hold on any longer and fainted.","Yue’er opened the bottle and smelled it, at least she had studied medicine for so long, she could tell whether it was a poison or an antidote, and when she saw that it was indeed an antidote, she quickly poured out the antidote and stuffed it into Old Predeccessor Guo’s mouth.","\"Shui Shui, drink some more water.\" Yue’er said, taking out her own water and pouring it into his mouth. The water was poured down, but it also drenched Old Predeccessor Guo’s blood-stained robes.","On the other side, the few people who had followed their Master away looked at each other, and one of them bravely asked, \"Master, is that little girl really Azure Emperor’s disciple? Why don’t we kill her? Even if we kill her and take that whip from her hand, I guess no one will know.\"","\"Joke.\" The masked man walking in front gave a sinister sneer, looked askance at the person who had spoken, and said, \"That whip in that little girl’s hands is the Ancient Divine Whip, and if it falls into someone else’s hands, then it would be a murderous object that destroys a family and a clan.\"","\"What’s more, if that Azure Emperor can give the whip to his disciple, would he not have a way to protect his disciple? Do you believe that if you really lay your hands on that little girl, Azure Emperor will definitely appear?\"","At those words, several people were stunned and somewhat hesitant, saying, \"This, this is impossible, right?\"","\"Impossible? Hmph! That’s because you guys don’t know how terrifying a great emperor really is!\" His gaze narrowed, and his hand that was behind his back clenched, as if he had remembered something, his breathing heavier by a few points.","It was precisely because he was clear about how terrifying the Great Emperor’s strength was that he guessed the identity of that little girl as Azure Emperor’s disciple after recognizing the whip in her hand as the Ancient Divine Whip, and if he hadn’t recognized it at that time and killed her with a hit, he was only afraid that the Azure Emperor would have chased after him at the ends of the earth to put him out of his misery!","Hearing their Master’s words, several people looked at each other, fear welling up in their hearts. Even their Master was this scornful, and it was fortunate that they didn’t kill that little girl earlier.","In the woods, Old Predeccessor Guo, who had taken the antidote, was gradually getting better, but he was still unconscious, and the airship was unable to take him away, so Yue’er could only wait here for him to wake up.","In the evening, Old Predeccessor Guo regained his consciousness, slowly opened his eyes, and saw that the little girl who was staring at him with her chin in both hands opened her eyes wide in surprise.","\"You woke up!\"","Old Predeccessor Guo was a bit complicated and surprised. He had never thought that this little girl would actually be Azure Emperor’s disciple, and remembering the scene where she had approached that person for the antidote before she fell unconscious, the taste in his heart was somewhat indescribable.","\"I didn’t expect you to be Azure Emperor’s disciple, if it wasn’t for you today, I’m afraid that old me would have to die here.\"","He said with emotion, sitting up with one hand on the edge of the boat, seeing that his hand as well as the other injuries on his body were bandaged up, he said to her gratefully, \"Many thanks.\""]},{"number":4933,"title":"Chapter 4933: Get out of the way","paragraphs":["\"You’re injured now, do you want to recuperate for two days?\" Yue’er asked with a crooked head.","\"It’s fine, I can recuperate on the airship.\" He looked around and knew that he was still in he forest, so immediately, with a single thought, the airship flew up.","Although the sky was getting dark, the airship was illuminated with night pearls.","As the airship flew up, Yue’er was also lying on the deck, looking at the dark sky outside, thinking about those people earlier, she could not help but look at Old Predecessor Guo, and asked: \"Who are those people? Aren’t you quite powerful? How come you couldn’t beat them either?\"","Old Predecessor Guo was half lying down, listening to her words, then said, \"They were from the Killing Alliance, they are an assassin organization, every one of them is extremely powerful. Even I, didn’t expect that they’re still wearing soft armor which has been imbued with poison. After being hit by the poison, naturally I’m no longer able to fight them. Otherwise, even if I’m not able to win them, I won’t be in such a sorry state and even almost lost my life because of it. \"","Saying that, he paused and looked at her and said, \"It’s also fortunate that you are Azure Emperor’s disciple, otherwise, we would all have perished here today.\"","Upon hearing this, Yue’er smiled and narrowed her eyes, saying, \"I didn’t realize that my master’s name really does work.\"","The two chatted while they rested until the night was deep, while the airship slowly flew towards their destination ...","A few days later, Old Predecessor Guo brought Yue’er down from the airship and put the small airship away, Old Predecessor Guo said, \"Not far ahead is the town where my late friend’s family is located, so you can go with me to rest first! If you want to leave, it’s not too late to leave after a day or two, after all, this journey has been a bit faster than we expected.\"","Yue’er thought for a moment, then nodded and responded, \"Mm.\"","The two of them headed to the city, and the moment they entered the city, the old man looked at the prosperous place sighed: \"It’s been too many years since I’ve visited this place. I did not expect it to change so much, wait a moment, I need to ask the way.\" After he spoke, he walked to the nearest stall to ask for directions.","Yue’er stood on the street and looked around, watching the bustling streets as the hawkers were yelling, seeing the street lined up with all kinds of stalls, her eyes couldn’t help but lit up the moment she noticed a stall selling cotton candy. She quickly walked to the stall.","\"I want one please.\" Yue’er was looking eagerly at the cotton candy, her eyes sparkling brightly.","\"Alright! One cotton candy coming right up!\" The vendor smiled and said, holding a bamboo stick in his hand, he deftly started rolling it around skillfully, as his hand holding the bamboo stick rotated, when it finally took shape, it was a large white fluffy flower.","\"Here, take it.\" The vendor handed it to her with a smile, and saw the child hand over a silver coin, and was about to find the change when he heard her wave her hand and say keep the change.","Yue’er was holding the cotton candy in her hand and was a little reluctant to eat it, looking at the large flower, she smiled and narrowed her eyes gleefully, while walking, she carefully stretched out her little tongue and licked it gently.","\"Mmm, it’s delicious!\"","The sweet and tasty flavor spread out on the tip of her tongue, and she smiled happily, however, just as she crossed the street to return to Old Predecessor Guo’s place across the street, she heard a burst of chaotic voices on the street accompanied by exclamations of alarm coming from the street.","\"The beast is frightened! The beast is frightened! Quickly, get out of the way! Get out of the way!\"","As the cries of alarm from afar came closer, the street became a more chaotic, as cries of alarm were resounded, a two-beast carriage was rushing furiously towards Yue’er’s side."]},{"number":4934,"title":"Chapter 4934: Avoid","paragraphs":["\"Quickly! Get out of the way! Get out of the way!\"","Yue’er was munching on her cotton candy when she heard the shouts. She looked toward the commotion and saw a spirit beast carriage careening wildly down the street, completely out of control.","Yue’er calmly licked her cotton candy again, watching the beast-drawn carriage approach. Amidst the surrounding crowd’s gasps and sighs of regret, she lightly pushed off with her toes. Her small figure then sat down on the second-floor balcony railing of a nearby tavern.","Perched on the second-floor railing, her feet dangling over the edge, she held onto a pillar for balance with one hand while eating her cotton candy with the other. Curiously, she watched the erratic carriage crash into a small stall, scattering its wares everywhere.","The onlookers stared in astonishment at the child sitting on the second-floor railing, dangling her tiny legs. They had expected such a small child to be thrown off, yet the little girl proved surprisingly agile.","Old Predecessor Guo paused, looking up to find the little girl sitting above, smiling down at him.","\"Can we eat first? I’m hungry!\" Yue’er said sweetly, flashing an innocent, adorable smile as she nibbled on her cotton candy. She noticed it was shrinking even though she was reluctant to eat it.","Seeing this, Old Predecessor Guo nodded and smiled. \"Alright, find a seat upstairs. I’ll be right up.\" \" With that, he stepped inside the tavern.","Traveling together, they knew this child wouldn’t touch a single grain pill, yet she was indeed more sensible and diligent than most children. During their journey, she rarely complained about eating only dry rations and pastries. Now that they had the opportunity to enter a tavern, it was only right to let her enjoy a proper meal.","The chaos on the street hadn’t fully dispersed yet, but the city guards arrived swiftly to handle it. However, many people had witnessed the little girl’s light and agile movements, so they kept glancing up at the second floor of the restaurant.","After finishing her cotton candy, Yue’er sat by the table waiting for the food to arrive. She had already ordered from the waiter before Old Predecessor Guo had even come up.","\"Were you startled just now?\" Old Guo sat down and inquired.","\"No, it was those two beasts that got startled. But they didn’t hit me.\" Yue’er said, twirling the teacup on the table with her small hand as she asked, \"Grandpa Guo, is your friend’s house far from here?\"","\"Not very far. There’s no rush. Now that we’re in the city, we can have a meal and rest a bit before going. \" Old Master Guo chuckled, glancing down at the street below. He saw the city guards arriving and the two spirit beasts, which had gone out of control for some unknown reason, being slain, their blood splattering the ground.","He frowned slightly, seemingly surprised by the brutality and bloodshed of the city guards’ enforcement.","\"Those two beasts died so unjustly.\" Yue’er propped her cheek with one hand. Turning to see the scene below, she couldn’t help but sigh softly.","\"Oh?\" Old Predecessor Guo paused, somewhat surprised by her remark.","\"I just caught the scent of herbs on them—the kind that drives beasts mad,\" Yue’er said, still twirling a teacup on the table.","Hearing this, Old Guo asked no more. Certain matters within the city were best left unquestioned; otherwise, they would only invite trouble.","\"Food’s ready! Braised golden pig’s trotters, crispy-skinned spirit pig meat...\" The waiter called out loudly as he placed the dishes he was carrying onto Yue’er and the others’ table."]},{"number":4935,"title":"Chapter 4935: Missed","paragraphs":["Meanwhile, Feng Jiu, disguised in plain clothes, entered the city with Mu Chen, Hao’er, and Song Mi’er. They blended in seamlessly, strolling through the streets without drawing any attention.","After all, clad in the most commonplace attire, their cultivation and aura concealed, and their appearances entirely transformed, they blended in as seamlessly as any random passerby. No one would give them a second glance.","\"Mother, let’s rest here tonight. We’ll continue our journey tomorrow,\" Hao’er whispered softly, glancing around at the surroundings. His eyes flickered when he spotted the cotton candy. \"If my little sister were here, she’d definitely want to try that cotton candy.\"","At that moment, the sister he spoke of, Yue’er, was buried in a feast of delicious dishes. Completely oblivious to the scene unfolding on the street below, she had no idea that the mother she longed for was right there, just downstairs.","\"This pork knuckle is so good!\" Yue’er mumbled, stuffing a piece of meat into her mouth with rice.","Old Predecessor Guo chuckled. \"Take your time, no one’s rushing you.\" He ladled her a bowl of soup. \"Here, have some broth so you don’t choke.\"","\"Mmm,\" Yue’er mumbled in response, continuing to pick at a stewed dish on the table.","Down on the main street, Feng Jiu and the others walked past. After glancing around, Song Mi’er suggested, \"Master, there’s an inn up ahead. Let’s rest there first!\"","\"Alright, we’ll rest here today. We might as well see what we need to buy and get everything sorted.\" Feng Jiu nodded in agreement and headed toward the inn with her.","While eating, Yue’er suddenly felt as if she heard her mother’s voice near her. She paused her chopsticks and looked around, but saw no trace of her mother’s signature red robe. With the street bustling with people and chaotic voices, she began to wonder if it had been her imagination. After all, she hadn’t spotted her mother’s familiar figure anywhere on the street.","\"What’s wrong?\" Old Predecessor Guo asked, also looking toward the street.","\"Nothing,\" Yue’er shook her head, her small face slightly furrowed. Her previously hearty appetite vanished, replaced by a sense of loss.","Seeing she didn’t wish to elaborate, Old Predecessor Guo didn’t press further. \"Then try this,\" he said, \"it tastes quite good.\" He proceeded to place some of the delicious food into her bowl.","After walking a short distance, Feng Jiu suddenly stopped. She felt as though a familiar aura lingered nearby, yet when she scanned her surroundings, she saw no familiar faces or objects.","Mu Chen sensed her unease and looked up, asking, \"Mother, what’s wrong?\"","\"It just feels like there’s a familiar presence nearby,\" Feng Jiu murmured softly. Her gaze swept the area once more, but she found nothing. She could only chuckle to herself, \"I’m just overthinking things.\"","With that, she led the children toward the inn.","Shortly after Feng Jiu and the others entered the inn, Old Predecessor Guo emerged from the restaurant with Yue’er, heading toward the residence of his old friend’s family. Their path diverged from Feng Jiu’s group.","When the old man and the child came to a halt before an imposing gate, Yue’er watched as he reached out to knock on the door ring. After the crisp sound of \"knock, knock, knock\" echoed, he withdrew his hand and stood quietly, waiting. Finally, the gate opened a narrow crack from within."]},{"number":4936,"title":"Chapter 4936: Surprise","paragraphs":["\"Who are you? Looking for someone?\" A head poked through the open door crack, sizing up the two men before asking.","\"I’m your family’s old ancestor...\"","Old Predecessor Guo paused, mentally searching for his late friend’s title and which generation back he might be. The hesitation lingered.","But in that brief pause, the gatekeeper’s expression darkened, turning grim. Withdrawing his head, he barked an angry rebuke: \"How dare you! Who are you, you shameless scoundrel? To speak such insolence! To insult my family’s venerable Old Predecessor!\"","The door, which had been opened just a crack, slammed shut with a loud bang. The speed of it startled Old Predecessor Guo, leaving him momentarily stunned and unable to react.","He was, after all, a venerable immortal. For the gatekeeper to show such utter disregard for etiquette was truly arrogant and presumptuous.","His expression darkened slightly, his brow furrowing. Just as he prepared to knock again, the gate swung open, and several figures wielding sticks rushed out.","\"Beat him soundly! How dare he insult our Old Predecessor? Beat him!\" The gatekeeper barked the order, his face twisted with viciousness.","Behind him, Yue’er, who had been munching on spirit fruits, watched the scene in stunned silence. Her beautiful eyes widened in shock. Seeing the men charging out, she didn’t flee but instead stepped forward to stand beside Old Predecessor Guo. Curiously, she asked, \"Did you knock on the wrong door?\"","Old Predecessor Guo took a deep breath, his brow furrowing. As he saw several men charging at him with sticks, he swept his sleeve, sending them all flying backward. Only then did he call out in a steady voice, \"I am an old friend of your family’s Old Predecessor. I came at his invitation to attend the banquet!\"","Hearing this, the repelled men froze, exchanging bewildered glances. They knew that their Old Predecessor had recently hosted guests, but could this old man before them also be one?","If so, offending such an honored guest would spell real trouble.","The gatekeeper hesitated, glancing at him before cautiously asking, \"May I inquire... your honorable surname?\"","\"Guo,\" he replied, frowning.","Hearing this, the gatekeeper’s legs buckled. His knees buckled, and he fell directly to his knees. \"I... I failed to recognize your stature, sir. Please... please do not hold it against me...\"","Old Predecessor Guo said nothing, instead leading Yue’er inside. Those within saw them and hurried to usher them into the hall, while others swiftly went to report.","Yue’er, having just finished eating, couldn’t sit still. She wandered about, touching this and examining that, while waiting for the others to arrive.","Old Predecessor Guo remained silent too, merely sipping his tea with calm composure, looking thoroughly at ease.","\"Ha ha ha ha! Brother Guo! We’ve been waiting for you!\" An elderly man strode in, his laughter reaching their ears before he did.","Yue’er looked over curiously. The man appeared quite old, yet radiated a powerful aura. Dressed in simple gray robes, his presence commanded respect.","\"The Yu family’s gates are no easy place to enter! I finally made it here, yet nearly got thrown out,\" Old Predecessor Guo remained seated, twirling his teacup as he watched his old friend approach with a light snort of displeasure.","Hearing this, the Yu family Old Predecessor froze, his surprise evident. \"Is that so? I truly had no idea.\" Without waiting for a response, he turned with a dark expression and barked orders to those behind him.","\"Go! Replace the gatekeeper! Who was wielding that stick to chase people away? Deal with them all!\""]},{"number":4937,"title":"Chapter 4937: I’ve heard","paragraphs":["\"Brother Guo, I offer my sincerest apologies here. It’s my fault for not keeping my subordinates in line. Please don’t hold it against me, don’t hold it against me.\" He stepped forward with a smile, bowed his hands in greeting with a cheerful expression, then turned to the little girl in the hall and asked in surprise, \"Brother Guo, who is this...\"","Old Predecessor Guo glanced at Yun Qi beside him, thought for a moment, and said, \" This is a young friend of mine, Yun Qi. She traveled here with me and will likely be staying at your place for a couple of days.\"","Hearing this, he was surprised but didn’t press further. He simply smiled and said, \"I see. Since she’s a friend of Brother Guo’s, she’s also a guest of my Yu Family. A couple of days? No problem. Even if she stays for ten days or half a month, that’s perfectly fine.\"","With that, he chuckled. \"Brother Guo, my recent breakthrough to a higher realm is cause for great celebration. I should have personally invited you, but after years of seclusion, I’ve only just emerged. Then, on my first outing, an old friend pays a visit... so...\"","\"No need to apologize. The distance between us is considerable; traveling back and forth would be time-consuming. My coming here serves the same purpose.\" Old Predecessor Guo waved his hand dismissively.","\"How swiftly time flies! Without you, Brother Guo, I wouldn’t be where I am today.\" He spoke with deep emotion, his gaze brimming with gratitude.","Yue’er watched from the side as the two chatted. From their conversation, it seemed Old Predecessor Guo had saved him many years ago. Now that he had advanced, he had specially invited him to share in the celebration.","After chatting for a while, he turned to Old Predecessor Guo and Yun Qi: \"You must be weary from your journey. Let me show you to the courtyard to rest first.\"","So the two followed him toward the guest quarters. Along the way, Old Predecessor Guo inquired, \"How many guests did you invite this time? Have the others all arrived?\"","\"I’ve been in seclusion for so many years. I only have one or two old friends I still keep in touch with. Besides you, there’s only Old Man Zeng. The others are from some of the city’s families.\" Old Predecessor Yu said, adding, \"After I emerged from seclusion, I heard that the Great Emperor here now is a female emperor, known as the Phoenix Sovereign. Have you heard anything about her background?\"","At the mention of her Mother, Yue’er, who had been following nearby, flashed a glance and looked up at them.","\"This Empress Phoenix Sovereign is no ordinary figure!\" Old Predecessor Guo declared, turning to him. \"Are you aware of the recent incident involving the Great Emperor Northern Flame?\"","Old Predecessor Yu nodded, stroking his beard as he replied, \"Yes. I heard he was utterly annihilated, body and soul. And this was the work of none other than Empress Phoenix Sovereign.\"","Indeed. She is truly formidable. This incident shook the entire Upper Immortal Realm, reverberating far and wide. Presumably, the other Great Emperors have all heard of it, and now know both her methods and her power. Yet, in the time since, no one has dared to stir. It can be said that the might of this Empress Phoenix Sovereign is universally acknowledged.\"","Old Predecessor Guo spoke with admiration, then added with a hint of regret, \"Yet this Empress Phoenix Sovereign remains profoundly mysterious. Rumor has it that she favors crimson robes—a flowing crimson gown—and possesses breathtaking beauty. Her peerless grace and bearing leave an indelible impression upon all who behold her.\"","Yue’er’s eyes sparkled with a smile. She loved hearing others praise her Mother more than any compliment directed at herself.","As they chatted along the way, they eventually arrived at a small courtyard. Old Yu then addressed the little girl beside him, \"Young friend Yun Qi, you shall reside here. Should you require anything, simply instruct the servants below.\""]},{"number":4938,"title":"Chapter 4938: Seeking Help","paragraphs":["Capítulo 4938: Seeking Help","“Alright.” Yue’er smiled brightly in response, glancing at Old Predecessor Guo and adding, “Then I’ll go rest for a while.”","“Very well.” Old Predecessor Guo nodded once, watching her enter the courtyard before following Old Predecessor Yu to another section of the grounds.","Once inside the courtyard, Old Predecessor Yu didn’t leave either. He had tea and pastries served, then sat down at a table in the courtyard. With no outsiders present, Old Master Yu finally asked, “How did you come to call Yun Qi ‘young friend’? What is her background? I see you take great care of her—what is the reason for this?”","“Heh, her? Well, she does come from an extraordinary background. A descendant of my family brought her to the estate. When I heard she was coming this way and I happened to be attending a banquet, I brought her along.” Old Predecessor Guo chuckled. “Don’t let her young age fool you. Her composure and calmness in handling matters are beyond what most children possess.”","Hearing such high praise for a child of five or six, Old Predecessor Yu paused, though he said nothing more. Instead, he inquired about Old Predecessor Guo’s recent years.","After sitting and sipping tea in the courtyard for a while, Old Predecessor Guo stood up with a smile. “Alright then, you should rest for a bit! If we keep chatting, you won’t even have time to rest. Since you’ve come this far, you should definitely stay a few more days. Let’s properly catch up.”","“Alright, you go ahead and attend to your duties!” Old Predecessor Guo also stood up, preparing to escort him out of the courtyard. Just then, a thunderous crash echoed from ahead, accompanied by a surge of air pressure rippling outward.","Hearing the sound, Old Predecessor Yu looked toward the front, his brow furrowing slightly. He said to Old Predecessor Guo, “You rest.” “I’ll go see what’s happening,” he said. With that, he headed outside.","Old Predecessor Guo considered following, but then thought of his own considerable strength after advancing, and the many powerful figures present at the Yu Manor. Even if something serious occurred, they could handle it. Thus, he stood in the courtyard for a moment before turning and walking toward one of the side rooms.","At the Yu family’s main gate, an elderly man was sent flying by a palm strike, crashing into the gate with such force that the entire structure collapsed to the ground.","“Pfft!”","The old man spat out a mouthful of blood, his face deathly pale as he turned to see several figures pursuing him. He struggled to his feet.","“Who dares to cause trouble here!”","Upon hearing the commotion, members of the Yu household rushed out. Seeing the old man lying upside down, coughing up blood near the shattered gate, they froze in shock.","“Who are you?”","A middle-aged man barked the question, his brows knitted tightly as his piercing gaze locked onto the group. There were four of them: two men who appeared to be in their forties or fifties, a woman around thirty, and an elderly man who looked to be in his sixties.","A palpable aura of hostility emanated from them. Their gaze wasn’t fixed on the surrounding crowd, but solely on the old man struggling to rise from the ground.","“Old Master Zeng?”","Old Predecessor Yu, drawn by the commotion, stared in shock at the struggling figure. “Why is it you? What happened?” He hurried forward, reaching out to steady the old man.","“Old Yu, I’m truly sorry for causing you trouble. Cough, cough...” He looked at him apologetically, but as soon as the words left his mouth, he began coughing violently, blood spilling from his mouth.","Pursued relentlessly, with nowhere left to flee, he had sought refuge at the Yu Manor. He’d hoped his old friend, who had recently advanced in cultivation, might protect him. Yet before he even crossed the Yu family’s threshold, the pursuers struck with lethal force."]},{"number":4939,"title":"Chapter 4939: Face","paragraphs":["At this moment, even if he hadn't died, his injuries were so severe that he likely couldn't fight anymore.","Though they knew he'd led them to the Yu family to trap them in danger, if he hadn't done so, he wouldn't have had even a sliver of hope.","People are selfish. At this moment, he didn't even care about diverting the blame; he only hoped for a shred of chance to survive.","Behind him, the Patriarch Yu and the elders who followed heard that this man was someone the Old Predecessor knew. Their expressions shifted slightly.","This man had brought disaster upon their Yu family, plunging them into peril. Such a person cared only for his own survival, utterly disregarding the safety of others. Frankly, this kind of person was selfish and self-serving.<wjtkd> Fresh chapters posted on novel·fıre·net</wjtkd>","\"Old Predecessor,\" the middle-aged man stepped forward, calling out softly. Seeing him still supporting the old man, he added, \"Old Predecessor, perhaps we should not involve ourselves in this matter?\"","Old Predecessor Yu's face darkened slightly, as if he hadn't heard the words from behind him. Supporting Old Zeng, he looked at the four men, his aged voice low and resonant: \"Who are you?\" Why did you strike with lethal blows? What wrong did he commit against you that you must see him dead?\"","\"I don't know them. I merely acquired a treasure at the auction on my way here, intending to congratulate you on your advancement. But these four men targeted me and pursued me all the way,\" Old Zeng said weakly.","Hearing this, Old Predecessor Yu's eyes flickered. After glancing at him, he turned to the four men across from them and said, \"Gentlemen, do me a favor. Call it quits here, and I won't pursue this matter further.\" Old Predecessor Yu spoke, his gaze fixed on the group.","\"Do you a favor? Who do you think you are? What favor could you possibly grant?\" A middle-aged man sneered coldly. \"We've decided to take his life today!\" As the words left his mouth, the sharp blade in his hand shot forward, striking toward Old Zeng.","\"Support him!\" Old Predecessor Yu pushed the man toward those behind him for support. His own palm flickered, sending a palm wind whistling toward the middle-aged man.","Despite his fierce momentum, the middle-aged man was forced back by the strike, stumbling several meters before regaining his footing. His expression shifted, his eyes darkening with menace.","Seeing this, the other three men's expressions shifted as well, their gazes growing heavier, all fixated on Old Predecessor Yu.","Old Predecessor Yu bowed his hands toward them. \" Gentlemen, I know not your origins, but today he is my guest. There is no way I would allow a guest to die before the gates of the Yu family. I ask you to please leave!\"","\"Are you Yu Chengzhi?\" The old man narrowed his eyes, staring intently at Old Predecessor Yu as he asked.","Perhaps because he had spoken his name so directly, Old Predecessor Yu's gaze flickered slightly. He bowed his hands and replied, \"Indeed, it is this old man.\"","Seeing this, he paused, looking at him and saying, \"You're protecting him out of righteousness, which is understandable. Since this man is your guest, I'll give you face and not kill him at your doorstep. But once he steps outside your Yu family gates, if you dare to obstruct him again, don't blame us for being impolite!\"","\"Go!\"","The old man barked the command. As he turned to leave, the three men accompanying him swiftly departed as well. And so, a visible slaughter came to an end.","After seeing the man settled inside, Patriarch Yu stepped out. Spotting the figure waiting outside the courtyard, he walked over.","\"Old Predecessor, I believe keeping him here is not advisable.\""]},{"number":4940,"title":"Chapter 4940: Danger","paragraphs":["Old Predecessor Yu walked with his hands behind his back until he reached a tree outside the courtyard. Only then did he let out a soft sigh. \"Ah! How could I not know? But now, with his injuries so severe and having come at our invitation, how could we stand by and watch him die?\"","He shook his head. \"I’ve already sent word to the Zeng family, instructing them to send someone to take him back. It’s also a way of escorting him home.\"","Hearing this, Patriarch Yu’s frown eased momentarily before he added, \"Old Predecessor, I feel his actions today were unwise. A man like him isn’t worth the Yu family taking such great risks to protect.\"","\"Enough. I know what I’m doing.\" He waved his hand dismissively and departed without another word.","As dusk fell and the sky darkened, a figure slipped silently into the Yu residence. Approaching the well in the rear courtyard, they unscrewed the cap of a small vial and poured a portion of its contents into the water.","The arrival was utterly unnoticed—no one from the Yu household, whether in plain sight or hidden, saw a thing.","When Yue’er awoke, night had already fallen. Stretching lazily and yawning, she stepped out of her courtyard. After inquiring with a servant, she made her way to Old Predecessor Guo’s quarters.","\"Grandfather Guo?\" Yue’er called out. Seeing no one emerge, she addressed the maid standing outside the courtyard gate, \"Is he sleeping too?\"","\"Probably. The door’s been locked, and he hasn’t come out,\" the maid replied, glancing inside before adding, \"A welcome banquet is prepared in the front courtyard. The Old Predecessor arranged it especially for the two of you. Young Miss, please go over!\"","\"A welcome banquet?\" Yue’er frowned, pouting slightly. \"I hate welcome banquets the most. They’re so boring!\" She rolled her eyes in boredom.","Her eyes twinkled mischievously as she grinned. \"Here’s what we’ll do! Since he’s still asleep, just tell him when he wakes up that I’ve gone out to explore the night market. He doesn’t need to look for me—I’ll be back later.\"","Without waiting for the maid’s response, Yue’er giggled and skipped toward the front gate.","\"Huh? Why is the gate broken?\" Yue’er arrived at the entrance and was startled to find the gate missing, replaced by several guards standing watch.","\"Something happened today. The gate was smashed. It won’t be reinstalled until tomorrow,\" explained one guard who recognized her as an honored guest of the household.","\"I see,\" Yue’er nodded, though inwardly puzzled. Who would dare smash the Yu family’s gate? Old Predecessor Yu had mentioned that their family’s strength had grown after his recent advancement. Yet here was someone attacking their gate—either he wasn’t strong enough, or the attacker was even more formidable.","She shrugged her small shoulders. It wasn’t her concern anyway. Stepping outside, she headed toward the city gates.","\"When Mother took us to the night market before, there were so many delicious treats!\" Yue’er chattered as she skipped along the street, stopping to examine anything intriguing and buying snacks whenever something tasty caught her eye.","\"If only Mother and Brother were here too,\" she murmured, blinking her eyes as a wistful expression flitted across her small face.","Unbeknownst to her, Feng Jiu had just left the inn with the two children and Song Mi’er, also heading toward the night market.","\"Master, the waiter said the liveliest spot in town is the night market on West Street. Let’s go check it out!\" Song Mi’er walked beside them, her pretty face lighting up with eager anticipation."]},{"number":4941,"title":"Chapter 4941: Meet","paragraphs":["Chapter 4941: Meet","“Alright!” Feng Jiu smiled in agreement, letting her lead the way to the night market on West Street.","Feng Jiu strolled leisurely, her gaze drifting to her two well-behaved sons beside her. A tender, doting expression softened her eyes as a smile touched her lips. “If you see anything you like,” she told them, “just say the word. Mother will buy it for you.”","Hearing this, the boys looked up at her, smiling as they replied, “Mm hmm! Thank you, Mother.” Truthfully, they had money of their own—their cosmos sacks held many treasures, and wealth was no exception.","Being boys, they weren’t particularly drawn to trinkets. Instead, they simply held their Mother’s hand as they strolled down the street, taking in the bustling night market.","Arriving at the night market on West Street, they found a small stall by the roadside, sat down, and ate some snacks.","Meanwhile, Yue’er had also made her way alone to West Street. She’d wandered over, having heard that the night market here was the liveliest, so she decided to check it out.","“Bowl rice cake? Is this a pastry?” Yue’er stopped curiously in front of a small stall, tilting her head to look at the transparent object stuck on the side and the three characters hanging above the stall.","“It’s a delicious cake, little sister. Want to try one?” The young vendor selling bowl cakes saw Yue’er standing there, tilting her head in curiosity. He carefully scooped out a portion, skewered it with a bamboo stick, and handed it to her.","Yue’er took it, took a small bite, and found it soft, springy, and utterly delicious. Her eyes lit up as she pulled out money and handed it to him: “I’ll take ten more to go.”","“Sure thing!” The young man smiled, deftly packing ten for her and giving her her change. “Come back if you like it!”","Yue’er responded with a beaming smile. She stowed the snacks in her spatial pouch and immediately headed to the next food stall. Munching on her bowl cake, she scanned the wares at another stand. “Is this candy? Give me half a pound.”","As she spoke, she handed over more money. She visited several stalls in succession, eating as she walked until her stomach was full. Stopping to rest, she rubbed her belly and let out a satisfied burp.","“So full, can’t eat anymore, but I still want to eat. What should I do?” she murmured to herself. Glancing around, she headed back toward the main street. Spotting a stall making sugar sculptures, her eyes lit up. She ran over and called out, “I want a sugar sculpture! Make one that looks just like me!”","Muchen, who had been eating at a stall, froze. He suddenly looked up, scanning the area as if searching for something.","“What’s wrong?” Feng Jiu asked, glancing around too. The street bustled with people, a lively chaos of vendors’ shouts and the chatter of passersby, creating an almost overwhelming din.","“I think I heard my sister’s voice,” Muchen said. Whether it was the telepathic bond between twins or something else, he felt intensely that his sister was somewhere nearby.","Hearing this, Feng Jiu raised an eyebrow but said nothing. Instead, she released her divine sense to scan the area. The divine sense’s search far surpassed what the naked eye could achieve, sweeping over every person. Even on such a crowded street, nothing would escape its notice.","“She really is here?” Feng Jiu’s surprise gave way to a smile as she rose to her feet. Her gaze locked onto the tiny figure about fifty meters ahead, and her smile widened."]},{"number":4942,"title":"Chapter 4942: Reunited","paragraphs":["Chapter 4942: Reunited","“That little girl is buying sugar sculptures over there!” Feng Jiu shook her head.","Hearing their Mother’s words, Muchen and Hao’er’s eyes lit up with joy. They quickly stood up and looked in the direction their Mother was pointing, but being short and the street crowded, they couldn’t see where Yue’er was.","“Little sister? The young daughter our master mentioned?” Mi’er beside them also jumped to her feet, scanning left and right but spotting no one.","“Over there,” Feng Jiu said, striding forward.","Yue’er was currently watching the candy sculptor deftly shaping sugar figures. Her wide eyes fixed on him as she said, “Make it look just like me! And make it pretty, okay?”","“Little Sister!”","“Little Sister!”","Hao’er and Muchen approached and called out the moment they spotted her.","Yue’er, who had been staring intently at the sugar sculptures, froze upon hearing the familiar voices. She turned to look around and saw two figures running toward her from a short distance away. When she saw those two figures, she paused in surprise.","Those two faces weren’t familiar to her, but their builds and the expressions in their eyes were unmistakably familiar. Without a second thought, she knew they were her two brothers, disguised.","Her face immediately broke into a delighted smile as she ran toward them. “Big Brother! Brother!”","“Little Sister, we finally found you! Are you okay? Did you run into any trouble out here alone?” Hao’er took her hand, his eyes brimming with unhidden joy as he looked at her.","“Running off like that—don’t you know how worried we get?” Muchen scolded, his face stern, carrying himself with all the authority of an older brother.","Yue’er stuck out her little tongue, feeling both guilty and remorseful. “I... I just missed Mother so much, I snuck out. But don’t worry, I’m fine. Nothing bad happened.”","Then she whispered, “Um... is Master angry with me? Is he really upset?”","“If you were worried he’d be angry, why did you sneak out?”","A voice suddenly spoke. Yue’er’s eyes widened in shock as she stared at the figure approaching slowly. Though the face wasn’t Mother’s, the voice was unmistakably hers.","“Mother?” she called out in disbelief, her voice trembling.","Feng Jiu approached, her expression softening at the sight of her daughter’s bewildered little face. Though she’d intended to scold her for running away, the sight of her soft, delicate daughter made her words die on her lips.","“Have you suffered? Were you hurt out there? Did you eat properly? Why have you lost weight?” Feng Jiu stroked her daughter’s head and pinched her arm. Though the flesh was soft, she still felt her daughter had grown thin.","“Waaah... Mother, I missed you so much, so very much...” Yue’er recovered her senses, threw herself into her arms, and burst into tears.","Hearing her little daughter’s words, Feng Jiu’s heart ached with both tenderness and guilt.","“There, there. No more crying, sweetheart.” She wiped the tears from her face and said, “Do you know how worried your Mother would be if you ran off alone? What if something happened to you? What would your Mother do then?”","“Mother, I’m sorry. Yue’er disobeyed both you and Master,” she whispered softly, lowering her head in remorse.","Seeing this, Hao’er spoke up: “Little Sister, not long after you slipped away, Mother came to see us. She brought us out too. We’ve been by Mother’s side all this time.”"]},{"number":4943,"title":"Chapter 4943: Know","paragraphs":["Chapter 4943: Know","Upon hearing this, Yue’er stared blankly at her Big Brother. His subtle barbs cut far deeper than her own brother’s stern reprimands—this was making her truly regret sneaking away!","Had she not slipped out while they were gone, she could have waited for Mother to arrive at the mountain and left with her.","At this thought, she hung her head dejectedly. “I know I was wrong. I really know I was wrong. I’ll never disobey again.”","Seeing this, Hao’er didn’t say much else. He simply reached out and patted her shoulder. “Master went out on business. We happened to run into you here. Until Master returns, we’ll stay by Mother’s side.”","“It’s crowded and noisy here. Let’s sit in the tavern up ahead!” Mi’er chimed in beside her, eyeing the little girl curiously. Who’d have thought someone so young dared to roam alone? Impressive! Truly the child of her master.","“Alright.” Feng Jiu agreed, leading the children toward the tavern ahead.","Upon reaching the second floor, they found a quieter spot to sit. Only then did Feng Jiu inquire, “Yue’er, how long have you been here? Where are you staying now?”","“Mother, I came here with Grandfather Guo. I wasn’t traveling alone. I’m staying at a friend of Grandfather Guo’s house. I was planning to come find you in a couple of days,” she hurriedly explained.","Hearing this, Feng Jiu raised an eyebrow. “Grandfather Guo? Who is he? How did you meet him?”","“Well, when I asked the little fox to take me away, something unexpected happened. I...” She recounted the events after leaving that day, explaining how she escaped from the Xiao family’s place and why she ended up coming here with the Guo family’s Old Predecessor.","After listening, Feng Jiu nodded. “So, because you encountered danger on the road, he discovered your identity?”","“Yes,” Yue’er replied, adding, “But he promised not to reveal it, since I saved his life!”","“Where is the whip your master gave you?” Feng Jiu asked.","“Here.” Yue’er produced it and handed it to her mother, explaining, “Mother, this whip is truly remarkable. It can be used as both a whip and a sword.”","Feng Jiu took the whip, examined it, and nodded. “It is indeed a treasure. Your master has been very kind to you, entrusting you with this Ancient Divine Whip.”","With that, she smiled and handed the whip back. “Put it away. Nowadays, this whip practically represents your identity. Even those who haven’t met you will know you’re Yun Qi, the third disciple under the Azure Emperor, just by seeing it.”","After their long-awaited reunion, they chatted for a while in the tavern. Yue’er then said, “Mother, I should go back to the Yu Manor and tell Grandfather Guo and the Yu family, so they won’t worry.”","“That’s a good idea. After you’ve told them, come to the inn! We plan to leave the city tomorrow. Now that we’ve met you, you should come with us. We’ll take you back to the island to see it then.” ” Feng Jiu said with a smile.","“Master, I’ll accompany Yue’er! I’ll bring her back to the inn to find you later.” Mi’er spoke up from the side.","They had been talking the whole time, and she had been listening nearby. She knew that the Master’s three children were now disciples under the Azure Emperor, and this information was known to very few people indeed."]},{"number":4944,"title":"Chapter 4944: In Peril","paragraphs":["Chapter 4944: In Peril","She was touched that her master hadn’t avoided her when discussing this matter, and silently vowed to keep this secret. At this moment, it wasn’t appropriate for her master to appear either before Grandfather Guo, as mentioned by Yue’er, or before the Yu family. Therefore, she would have to accompany them.","After all, it was the middle of the night, and only with an adult like her accompanying her would the Yu family and that Old Predecessor Guo allow her to leave so late.","Feng Jiu listened to her words without objection, merely nodding in agreement. “Alright, you may accompany her. After bidding them farewell, return to the inn. We shall await your return there.”","“Understood.” Yue’er and Mi’er both acknowledged before rising and heading downstairs.","After they departed, Feng Jiu led the two children toward the inn, intending to wait there for their return.","At the Yu residence, though brightly lit, an eerie silence hung in the air.","Yue’er led Mi’er toward the Yu residence, saying as they walked, “It’s just up ahead. Strangely, their gate’s broken today—no door to close. But there are several guards stationed there.”","As they spoke, they reached the main gate. Just as Yue’er was about to step inside, Song Mi’er suddenly pulled her back with a look of alarm, shielding her behind her.","“What’s wrong?” Yue’er froze, looking up at her.","“Something’s off. I smell blood,” Song Mi’er said, frowning. “Something’s wrong in there.”","Thanks to her obstruction and warning, Yue’er standing by the gate also caught the scent of blood in the air. Her expression shifted slightly. In that instant, a voice echoed from behind them.","“Since you’ve seen us, you’ll stay behind too!”","The voice carried a bone-chilling intent to kill. As soon as it spoke, a gust of air whistled toward them.","With no escape route, the two at the gate had no choice but to retreat into the Yu residence. Yet the moment they entered, they sensed the entire Yu estate was sealed within a barrier. Sounds and the turbulent air from the fight wouldn’t spill out, ensuring no one else was alerted.","Throughout the estate, the guards who should have been stationed at the gates now lay sprawled on the ground. From the direction of the rear courtyard came the sounds of combat and agonized screams.","“Watch out!” Mi’er shouted, twisting her wrist as a frying pan shot out, striking toward the attacker.","The frying pan whizzed toward the figure, spinning and growing larger as it flew. It slammed down with a thud, but after the attack was blocked, it returned to Song Mi’er’s hand.","“Lion!”","Yue’er called out, glancing toward the backyard. “Go check on Grandfather Guo!” After all, they’d traveled together this far. Whatever had happened, protecting him was the top priority.","“Roar!” Lion let out a deep roar and darted toward the backyard.","“A Sacred Beast!”","The middle-aged man who had attacked Mi’er narrowed his eyes, fixing a cold stare on Yue’er. He seemed to be trying to figure out who she was. Such a young child, and she had a Sacred Beast by her side?","In the rear courtyard, Old Predecessor Yu and Old Predecessor Guo were fighting together against the three attackers. Most of the household servants had fallen unconscious after consuming the laced food and water. Only these two, possessing deeper cultivation, remained alert.","Moreover, they hadn’t eaten anything, only drinking tea. Their profound strength allowed them to barely hold on here.","But even now, they were merely clinging on. The entire manor was shrouded in barriers and formations, leaving them with no way to call for help. Even if their entire family were wiped out tonight, it seemed no one would ever know..."]},{"number":4945,"title":"Chapter 4945: Soul Shadow","paragraphs":["Chapter 4945: Soul Shadow","Old Predecessor Yu was now gripped by both shock and dread. He hadn’t expected these men to return after leaving, nor that they would resort to poisoning and ambush. What on earth had he obtained from Old Predecessor Zeng? That it had drawn such relentless pursuers?","“Gah!”","Unable to dodge in time, his shoulder was slashed. Blood seeped out instantly as he stumbled backward.","Thud!","A fierce palm strike sent Old Predecessor Guo flying into the stone wall. He rolled to the ground, coughing up blood as his vital energy weakened noticeably.","“Cough cough!”","As Old Predecessor Guo braced against the wall to rise, the two attackers closed in. With no escape, he braced for the inevitable strike—only to hear a furious roar. A blur of movement swept past, snatching him away to safety.","“Sacred Beast?”","The three attackers narrowed their eyes, staring in surprise at the lion that had suddenly darted out.","Seeing the lion had saved him, Old Predecessor Guo froze, then his eyes filled with urgency: “Why are you here? Quickly, take your master away from here!”","The lion glanced at him and said, “My master told me to save you.”","Old Predecessor Guo’s mouth opened and closed, utterly speechless. That evening, upon learning Yun Qi had gone out to the night market, he had instructed the gatekeeper to keep someone waiting for her. When trouble erupted later that night, he had been relieved she was out at the night market and hadn’t gotten involved. Yet now, she had returned at this very moment, and sent this Sacred Beast to save him.","“Where is she? Has she entered the manor?” Old Predecessor Guo asked urgently.","“In the front courtyard,” the lion replied.","Hearing this, Old Predecessor Guo’s expression darkened. “I don’t need your protection here! Go protect her! She’s no match for these people! Get her out of here now!”","Even if she was the Azure Emperor’s disciple, these men had set up barriers and formations clearly intended to wipe out everyone here. How could they possibly let a child like her leave alive?","Immediately, Old Predecessor Guo barked at the others, “We have no grudge against you! Wiping out an entire family is far too ruthless!”","“Hmph! Protecting those you shouldn’t, taking what you shouldn’t—what’s wrong with killing you?” The elder among the three snorted coldly, clearly holding neither the Sacred Beast nor the two before him in any regard.","“I’ll have Old Zeng hand over the item to you. Will you stop here?” The Yu family Old Predecessor, wounded and gasping for breath, asked with a grim face.","He understood that continuing the fight would likely see the two of them defeated. If they handed over the item and the attackers agreed to withdraw, at least they could survive tonight’s massacre.","“Killing you first, then taking it later is just as good,” the elder retorted, launching an attack toward Old Predecessor Yu.","At that very moment, a shadowy black soul form drifted out from one of the figures. Hovering mid-air, it coldly observed the battle, its sinister voice tinged with displeasure: “It’s taken you this long just to retrieve an item? Useless!”","A thunderous rebuke erupted, unleashing an invisible wave of pressure that slammed down, targeting Old Predecessor Guo and Old Predecessor Yu . The force of the assault sent both men reeling backward, blood spilling from their mouths.","Staring in horror at the soul shadow in midair, they saw it drifting toward a guest room within the courtyard.","Before long, a piercing scream echoed from within, followed by an eerie, soundless silence.","Hearing that sound, Old Predecessor Yu and Old Predecessor Guo felt their hearts sink to their feet. They knew... Old Zeng was likely..."]},{"number":4946,"title":"Chapter 4946: Worry","paragraphs":["Before long, a shadow figure drifted out again. This time, however, its ethereal hand cradled an object glowing with a ghostly light.","The thing was about the size of a bracelet, with two tiny bells attached to its edges. It floated in the soul-like figure’s palm, as if it couldn’t grasp the physical object. Approaching one of the men, it said, \"Take it.\"","\"Yes, Master!\" The middle-aged man responded respectfully, quickly taking the object and stowing it away.","The spirit form glanced at the two elders, too lazy to intervene. Just as it prepared to enter the middle-aged man’s body to rest, it sensed an exceptionally pure aura.","\"Hmm? An innate spirit-gathering body?\" His eyes narrowed, a gleam flashing within them as he shot toward the source of the aura.","Meanwhile, at the inn, Feng Jiu waited for Song Mi’er and Yue’er to return. Yet, the longer she waited, the more uneasy she felt. From Yue’er, she’d learned that the Yu Manor wasn’t far from either West Street or this inn. Logically, they should only have been gone briefly to say their goodbyes. Why hadn’t they returned yet?","Though Mi’er was with them, she couldn’t help feeling uneasy. After a moment’s thought, she turned to her two sons in the room and said, \"You two wait here for me. I’ll go see why they haven’t come back yet.\"","\"Mm hmm, we’ll wait here for you, Mother,\" they replied in unison.","Feng Jiu smiled, ruffling their hair. \"It’s getting late. Stay put and don’t wander off. Mother will be back soon.\"","After giving her instructions, she leapt directly out the window. A flash of movement, and she vanished into the night.","At the Yu Manor’s main gate, a middle-aged man stood, blood trickling down his face. It added a bloodthirsty edge to his already savage features.","Panting heavily, he glared viciously at the girl wielding a frying pan and a cleaver. The pan was larger than ordinary, now radiating a powerful aura—clearly a treasure.","Yet he’d never imagined anyone’s treasure could be a frying pan! When that pan’s base smashed into his skull, even his formidable cultivation couldn’t prevent blood from gushing from his forehead.","Then there was that cleaver—though calling it a kitchen knife was a stretch, as it resembled a bone-splitting blade. Its edge glinted coldly, razor-sharp. Armed with these two weapons, he had fought her for so long yet still failed to kill her!","Mind you, this girl looked no older than fifteen or sixteen, especially while shielding the little girl behind her. Such a pair of seemingly helpless figures would normally be dispatched with a single strike.","Yet now, though the young woman bore significant wounds, she stubbornly guarded the little girl without retreating an inch. This couldn’t go on.","\"Roar!\"","Just as he prepared to strike again, a thunderous lion’s roar erupted. A massive lion lunged at him from the side. Startled, he counterattacked immediately!","\"Sister Mi’er, how are you? Are you hurt?\" Yue’er looked at her with concern. Her body was covered in wounds, large and small. Yet, thanks to her protection, she hadn’t been harmed by that man.","\"You must leave immediately! Go find the Master at the inn. This place is too dangerous. Go!\" Taking advantage of the lion distracting the middle-aged man, Song Mi’er shielded her and rushed toward the gate, determined to get her out of this perilous place as quickly as possible.","\"Indeed, the scent of an innate spirit-gathering body.\" A voice carried a hint of excitement."]},{"number":4947,"title":"Chapter 4947: Recognize","paragraphs":["Chapter 4947: Recognize","The sudden sound made Song Mi’er’s heart sink. Instinctively shielding Yue’er behind her, she looked warily toward the source of the voice—only to see not a person, but an elusive shadowy spirit figure.","“Run!” Song Mi’er shoved her away, rushing toward the main gate.","“Can you really escape?” The spirit entity sneered coldly. With a wave of its hand, Yue’er, who had been running toward the gate, seemed to hit some kind of barrier and bounced back, tumbling to the ground.","Seeing this, Song Mi’er’s unease and worry deepened. They were trapped! There was no escape!","“Who are you? What do you want?” Song Mi’er shouted, brandishing the kitchen knife in her hand at the spectral figure.","The spirit glanced at the frying pan in her grasp, a dark gleam flashing in its eyes. “A member of the Culinary God Song family?”","“That’s right! It’s best you don’t touch us. Otherwise... otherwise, the Culinary God Song family won’t let you off!”","Clearly sensing the terrifying power of this spectral figure before her, Song Mi’er could only attempt to intimidate him by invoking the Song family’s name. Yet she knew this entity—whether human or ghost—exuded an aura so dreadful, and having instantly recognized her as a Song, it likely wouldn’t be easily deterred.","“Hmph, the Song family? A mere family.” He sneered coldly, glancing at Song Mi’er before waving her away with a dismissive gesture.","“Thud!”","“Ah!”","With almost no chance to resist, she was caught by a powerful force, flung against the stone wall. Song Mi’er let out a piercing scream, crashing into the wall before tumbling to the ground, spitting out a mouthful of blood.","“Pfft!”","“Sister Mi’er!” Yue’er cried out, sprinting toward her.","“A child with an innate spirit-gathering body? Truly rare! This scent... so sweet.” The soul entity blocked Yue’er’s path, inhaling her pure, potent Spirit Energy with rapturous delight.","“Get away!” Yue’er snapped, drawing her whip and lashing out at it.","Whoosh!","The crimson whip shot forward like a fiery bolt, striking the soul entity before her. The entity, eyes narrowed in rapture, likely believing the child’s attack couldn’t harm it, paid it no mind.","But when a piercing, menacing aura surged toward him with terrifying force, he jolted awake. Opening his eyes, he saw only a flash of crimson streaking toward him.","The speed was too swift to discern clearly, yet his instincts screamed danger, driving him to dodge. Unfortunately, while he evaded the whip’s frontal strike, he couldn’t escape its sharp crack as it lashed across his midsection.","“Whoosh!”","A searing pain, like flames scorching his very soul, shot through him. The agony made him gasp sharply as his soul-body swiftly retreated. Only then did he glance at the whip in the child’s hand.","“The Ancient Divine Whip!”","His brow furrowed deeply. His face, barely visible in the night, darkened, and a chill aura spread from his soul form.","“You are the Azure Emperor’s disciple!” Not a question, but a statement of certainty. Who else but the Azure Emperor’s disciple would dare wield this whip?","Recalling the Azure Emperor’s words, realizing this child with an innate spirit-gathering body before him was actually the Azure Emperor’s disciple, his brow twitched. A flash of reluctance crossed his eyes.","A child with an innate spirit-gathering body was such nourishment. If he could refine her into a medicinal pill, his divine soul would grow ever stronger. Perhaps in the not-too-distant future, he could ascend to become an Emperor!","But then he thought of that bastard Azure Emperor’s methods..."]},{"number":4948,"title":"Chapter 4948: Soul-Binding Bell","paragraphs":["A faint hesitation stirred within his heart. At present, he lacked the strength to withstand the Azure Emperor's wrath. He dared not take such a risk.","Yet, an innate spirit-gathering body was so rare. If he obtained her and used her to refine a medicinal pill, perhaps he could ascend to become an Emperor. Then, he would naturally be powerful enough to stand against the Azure Emperor...","For a moment, two thoughts battled within his mind. Reason told him not to take this risk, yet another voice in his head urged him not to miss this opportunity.","If he slaughtered everyone here! Then no one would ever know who had taken the disciple of the Azure Emperor! Even if the Azure Emperor discovered the truth someday, by then, he might already have ascended to become an Emperor.","This thought sent a surge of excitement coursing through him once more. He stared at the child clutching the Divine Whip, gazing at her as if she were a priceless treasure.","Children are sensitive, especially to unfriendly gazes.","Now, seeing that strange thing—human or ghost, she couldn't tell—staring at her with such an eerie gaze, Yue'er clutched the Divine Whip tightly and glared back, her voice trembling with fear. \"I... I'm the Azure Emperor's disciple! If you dare touch me, my master won't let you off!\"","Though she hated resorting to her master's name like this, the creature's gaze was terrifying!","She couldn't fight back, couldn't run away, and had no one to call for help. What could she do?","\"Heh, is that so? Rest assured, your master will never know you were taken by this one.\" He seemed to make up his mind, revealing a sinister yet delighted grin as his soul drifted toward Yue'er.","Song Mi'er clutched her chest as she scrambled to her feet. Seeing the soul approaching Yue'er, she shouted, \"Whip him!\" When the whip struck that soul form, half his body became slightly more transparent, and his aura weakened somewhat. So the whip must have been effective against him.","Yue'er gritted her teeth and lashed out at him again with the whip. However, earlier he hadn't taken her attacks seriously. Now that he knew the whip was the Divine Whip, he naturally wouldn't let his soul form be harmed again.","Thus, the instant Yue'er's whip fell, his soul form flickered and flew behind her, reaching out to grab her.","\"Watch out!\" Seeing this, Song Mi'er, ignoring her own injuries, lunged forward violently, shoving Yue'er aside.","His soul form grabbed at thin air. A flash of murderous intent flickered in his eyes as he spoke in a sinister tone, \"Since you wish to die, I'll let you taste the power of the Soul-Binding Bell!\"","As soon as the words left his mouth, he extended his ethereal hand toward the direction of the back courtyard, simultaneously shouting, \"Soul-Binding Bell, come forth!\"","In the rear courtyard, the middle-aged man who heard the call felt a jolt in his mind. Almost instinctively, he retrieved the small treasure he had stowed away earlier. The two tiny bells on the artifact swayed gently, emitting a crisp chime. In the next instant, as if pulled by an invisible force, the object shot forward with a whizzing sound, flying toward the front courtyard.","Clang.","The Soul-Binding Bell landed in the spirit form's hand. Though it appeared held, it was actually controlled by a force.","\"Seal!\" He shook one of the bells toward Song Mi'er. A surge of air rippled, and with another crisp ring, Song Mi'er collapsed. A visible strand of her soul was drawn out and sealed within the bell.","\"Sister Mi'er!\""]},{"number":4949,"title":"Chapter 4949: Feng Jiu Arrives","paragraphs":["Chapter 4949: Feng Jiu Arrives","Yue’er gasped and rushed toward Mi’er, who lay sprawled on the ground.","At that moment, the soul entity held the soul-binding bell in one hand while reaching out for Yue’er with the other, its voice tinged with darkness: “Come with me!”","When Feng Jiu arrived, she saw the Yu Manor shrouded in a barrier and formation. Her brows furrowed, and without hesitation, she leaped onto the wall. From her vantage point atop the wall, she witnessed the scene below. Instantly, she gathered a stream of energy in her finger and shot it toward the soul shadow below.","“Arghhhhhh!”","The soul entity screamed out in pain, snatching its hand back as its form drifted backward. Its icy gaze snapped toward the intruder.","It was only a woman—ordinary in both dress and features. The sole thing that sent a chill down the spine was the murderous intent lurking within her cold, piercing eyes.","“Who are you? How dare you disrupt my plans!” he snarled menacingly, his vigilant gaze fixed on the unexpected intruder.","Feng Jiu approached Yue’er, giving her a quick once-over. “Are you alright?” she asked.","Yue’er knew she couldn’t reveal her connection to her mother. Seeing her mother approach, she didn’t call out but instead said, ” I’m fine, but he extracted Sister Mi’er’s soul using that thing in his hand.”","Hearing this, Feng Jiu narrowed her eyes, fixating on the object in the soul entity’s grasp. In the next instant, a powerful vortex swirled in her palm, and a burst of flame shot forth, enveloping the soul entity.","Perhaps sensing her formidable power, the entity abandoned all caution and immediately drifted toward the rear courtyard. But how could Feng Jiu let it slip away right under her nose?","“Give me the whip.” As the words fell, she snatched the whip from Yue’er’s grasp and lashed it out with a sharp whack toward the soul form.","The whip darted out with astonishing agility, carrying a terrifying aura as it struck the soul entity’s body with a sharp crack. The piercing whistling of the air accompanied the whip’s strike, followed immediately by the soul entity’s shrill, piercing scream.","“Ssshhhh!”","The Divine Whip—even cultivators couldn’t withstand a single lash from it, let alone this mere soul fragment? Moreover, Yue’er had already weakened it with a previous strike. Feng Jiu’s follow-up lash rendered the soul fragment even more ethereal. The Soul-Binding Bell in its grasp fell to the ground amid its agonized tremors, clattering with a sharp clang.","“Whoosh!”","Flames surged forward, engulfing the soul fragment in their embrace. Instantly, piercing screams rose, each more shrill than the last...","Feng Jiu shifted her spirit energy, and the fallen bell landed in her palm. She glanced at it briefly before turning her gaze to the soul fragment, now reduced to ashes and vanishing into the air within the flames.","This was merely a fragment of the soul, not the person’s true form. Destroying this fragment was akin to crippling one hand of the opponent’s body—a severe wound, yet not fatal. Thus, while the soul fragment was extinguished, the person remained alive.","Seeing the man bitten by the lion fleeing toward the back courtyard, Yue’er hurriedly cried out, “There are still people in the back courtyard!”","“Lion, stay and watch over Mi’er. You come with me,” Feng Jiu said, glancing at the lion before lifting Yue’er and heading toward the rear courtyard.","“Retreat! The master’s soul essence has been destroyed...” The middle-aged man who had fled to the rear yard cried out in panic. Before he could finish, a flaming arrow whistled through the air from behind.","“Ahhhhh!”"]},{"number":4950,"title":"Chapter 4950: Bidding Farewell","paragraphs":["Capítulo 4950: Bidding Farewell","The man let out a piercing scream as the flame arrow pierced his body, sending him crashing to the ground. A mouthful of blood spurted forth. He writhed on the floor, frantically slapping at the flames engulfing him, yet the fire proved unquenchable. Soon, the sound of charred flesh mingled with his agonized screams echoed throughout the courtyard.","“Who goes there!”","Though the three in the rear courtyard bore wounds, none were fatal. In contrast, Old Predecessor Guo and Old Predecessor Yu lay barely clinging to life, forced to endure. Both had been knocked to the ground, utterly defenseless. Just as the three prepared to finish them off, the messenger who had come to report was consumed by a burst of flames.","“Grandfather Guo!” Yue’er cried out, seeing the old man covered in blood.","Gasping for breath, Old Predecessor Guo lay on the ground, too weak even to respond. His vision was already blurring.","As for the Old Predecessor Yu , darkness engulfed his eyes as he fainted. He had seen someone approaching, but could no longer make out who it was.","Feng Jiu glanced at the two elders on the ground. A burst of energy shot out, knocking even Old Predecessor Guo unconscious.","Seeing this, the three men were stunned. Just as they were about to demand her identity, a terrifying aura surged forth, carrying a powerful presence that instantly overwhelmed them. They were frozen in place, unable even to utter a sound.","Thud!","Under that overwhelming pressure and aura, the three men collapsed to their knees with a thud. Cold sweat soaked their backs as their hearts pounded in terror. Their eyes widened in fear as they stared at the woman.","Who was this woman? How could her aura be so terrifying?","Feng Jiu handed the whip to Yue’er, then stepped forward to stand before the three. She extended a finger, pressing it against each of their foreheads, and began soul-searching under their horrified stares.","She needed to know the true identity of that soul entity. What were these men’s backgrounds? The best way to deal with such people was direct soul-searching.","Before long, the three collapsed to the ground.","Under Feng Jiu’s soul search, survival was utterly impossible for them.","Seeing them all fainted or dead, Yue’er finally approached and said, “Mother, that thing—I don’t know if it was human or ghost—said I’m innate spirit body and that I’m very fragrant, wanting to capture me.”","Hearing this, Feng Jiu ruffled her hair and said, “It’s fine now. Mother will handle the rest. Don’t worry.”","Because both children possessed innate spirit-gathering bodies, they later developed protective and concealing abilities that ordinary people couldn’t detect. This alone suggested the soul entity’s true form possessed formidable cultivation.","However, no matter who this person was, daring to target her children meant she would never let them off!","“I’ll wake them up and inform them before we return to the inn,” Feng Jiu said to Yue’er beside her.","“Alright.” Yue’er responded as her Mother flicked out two streams of energy.","The two unconscious figures groaned softly and slowly regained consciousness.","“Grandfather Guo, those men are dead, but I must leave now. I only came back to tell you.” Yue’er spoke, glancing at the two seated figures. After a moment’s thought, she took out a medicinal pill and handed it to Old Predecessor Guo: “This medicinal pill will heal your wounds. Once you’re better, hurry home!”","Old Predecessor Guo swallowed the medicinal pill, feeling a gentle energy surge through his body, swiftly soothing his internal injuries. He was astonished by the pill’s potency and curious about the identity of the woman standing beside Yun Qi."]},{"number":4951,"title":"Chapter 4951: Handling","paragraphs":["Capítulo 4951: Handling","As far as he knew, the Azure Emperor had no one else besides those three disciples. So who was this woman? How had she appeared here and saved them?","Moreover, those previous opponents weren’t weak—especially that soul entity. Had it truly been destroyed? By this woman alone?","“Thank you for your rescue. May I ask how I might address you?” Old Predecessor Guo recovered his composure and inquired, his gaze fixed on the woman as he speculated about her identity and her relationship with Yun Qi.","“It was nothing,” Feng Jiu replied, nodding briefly to him. “Farewell.” With that, she led Yue’er forward.","“Goodbye, Grandfather Guo,” Yun Qi called out, waving. She deliberately ignored Old Predecessor Yu, who had regained consciousness.","Outside, Feng Jiu helped the unconscious Song Mi’er to her feet. With Yue’er in tow, they left the Yu residence and headed straight for the inn...","With those individuals now dead, the protective barriers and formations around the Yu Manor dissolved automatically. After taking the medicinal pill, Old Predecessor Guo felt somewhat better. He steadied himself against the wall and stood up, then helped Old Predecessor Yu to his feet. As for the rest, they would have to wait until tomorrow to deal with it.","Hao’er and Muchen waited at the inn for their mother’s return. Their eyes kept darting toward the window until several figures suddenly leapt through the opening, startling both boys.","“Mother! What happened?”","“Something happened at the Yu residence. When Sister Mi’er and I arrived, we found the place sealed off by barriers and formations. Inside, people were either unconscious or dead. We were trapped too. Sister Mi’er sacrificed herself to save me, only to have her soul drained by that thing. Thank goodness you came, Mother. Otherwise, I’d have been taken too.” Yue’er explained beside them. Though small, her words were clear and concise.","By then, Feng Jiu had laid Song Mi’er on the bed. She took her pulse, frowned, then instructed Hao’er and Muchen, “I need to tend to her wounds. Have the attendant bring some clean water.”","“Right away,” Hao’er replied promptly, heading out first.","Instead of having the waiter bring it in, Hao’er personally carried the water and placed it by the bedside. By then, Muchen had already drawn the screen beside the bed to create a partition and stepped back outside.","Being young boys, Hao’er and Muchen waited outside the screen. Yue’er remained by the bedside, watching her Mother tend to Mi’er’s wounds.","When the clothes were removed, revealing the numerous wounds large and small, Yue’er’s small fist clenched slightly. “If Sister Mi hadn’t shielded me, I might be the one injured now. Mother, will Sister Mi be all right?”","“Most of her injuries are superficial, and the internal damage isn’t severe. Treating her shouldn’t be a problem. However, she’s currently in a disembodied state—her physical form remains here, but her soul has been separated from it,” Feng Jiu explained calmly while tending to Song Mi’er’s wounds.","Hearing this, Yue’er urgently asked, “Can her soul return? Didn’t Mother bring back that Soul-Binding Bell? Sister Mi’er’s soul is trapped inside that bell, right?”","“That very Soul-Binding Bell is what brought disaster upon the Yu family,” Feng Jiu replied, her hand flickering as the small object appeared in her palm.","“Mother, is this a cursed object?” Yue’er asked, staring intently at the delicate item in Feng Jiu’s palm. It looked exquisitely crafted, resembling a bracelet, yet it could also extract one’s soul—appearing every bit the cursed artifact used by villains."]},{"number":4952,"title":"Chapter 4952: Prepare","paragraphs":["Capítulo 4952: Prepare","Hearing this, Feng Jiu paused for a moment, then smiled and said, “This isn’t an evil object. In fact, it’s quite a remarkable treasure.” She smiled, looking at Yue’er, and continued, “There are no truly evil objects in this world. Only human hearts can be wicked.”","Her voice paused briefly before continuing, “It’s like a knife. In your hands, it protects you; in the hands of a villain, it takes lives. Yet in Mi’er’s hands, she uses it to prepare delicious meals. The object remains the same—only the user changes.”","Yue’er listened attentively, then nodded firmly. “Mother, I understand. I’ll remember this.”","Feng Jiu ruffled her hair. “Go sit with your two brothers outside for a while. Mother will study this Soul-Binding Bell and figure out how to release Mi’er’s spirit.”","“Mm hmm~” Yue’er replied before stepping beyond the screen. With Mother here, she had no worries.","Hao’er and Mu Chen saw her emerge and quickly pulled her to sit at the table. “Little Sister, are you tired? Should we rest first?” they asked.","“I’m not tired,” Yue’er shook her head, settling beside the table. “I’ll wait here for Sister Mi’er to wake up.”","“Then we’ll keep you company.” The two boys sat down beside her.","Behind the screen, Feng Jiu examined the delicate soul-binding bells in her hands. She took one, infused it with spiritual energy, and gave it a gentle shake. A visible soul form drifted out.","Recognizing it as Song Mi’er, she immediately guided the soul back into its rightful place. Watching the soul merge with the body, she finally gave a sigh of relief. She checked Mi’er’s pulse and found no major issues before rising to leave.","“Mother, how is she?” Yue’er rushed forward the moment she emerged.","“Her soul is restored. She’ll awaken tomorrow morning,” Feng Jiu replied with a smile, handing the soul-binding bell to Yue’er. “This is for you. You might need it someday.”","“Isn’t this for capturing souls?” Yue’er asked, taking the Soul-Binding Bell and examining it. The two small bells looked exquisitely crafted, but the thought of it imprisoning spirits or other entities made her furrow her tiny brow.","“This is a remarkable treasure. Not only can it bind souls, but it can also capture them. Moreover, with it, ghosts and evil entities will dare not approach you.” Feng Jiu smiled. “After you mark it with your blood to claim it as yours, wear it. There’s no harm in it.”","Hearing her mother’s words, Yue’er dripped her blood onto the lock to imprint her mark upon it. Only then did she slip it onto her small wrist. Watching the tiny object adjust perfectly to her size, she gave it a gentle shake. The two bells swayed softly, emitting a clear, crisp sound that made her smile.","“Mother, look! It’s like a little bracelet.”","“Alright, you’ve both had a long day. Go wash up and get some rest!” Feng Jiu said, ruffling her hair.","They’d only intended to stop by the Yu family to say farewell, but this unexpected turn of events had unfolded. Fortunately, nothing serious had come of it.","Still, they couldn’t linger here long. They’d have to leave first thing tomorrow morning. If no one knew Yue’er’s identity as the Azure Emperor’s disciple, it would be fine. But now that they knew, seeing them all together would inevitably draw attention and scrutiny.","Perfect timing. Departing tomorrow, they could take a different route and, while they were at it, eliminate the true form of that soul entity from tonight and the faction behind it! On her territory, she would absolutely not tolerate anyone who dared to use her daughter to refine pills!"]},{"number":4953,"title":"Chapter 4953: Head towards the Song Family","paragraphs":["Chapter 4953: Head towards the Song Family","The next morning, Mi’er awoke. However, Feng Jiu and the others did not linger long; they departed around noon.","Although the incident at the Yu residence had occurred the previous night, and the protective barrier had prevented it from alerting the city’s inhabitants, by early morning, various factions and families within the city had received word that something had happened to the Yu family.","Yet, aside from the Old Predecessor Yu and Old Predecessor Yu Guo from the previous night, no one knew how the matter had ultimately been resolved, nor who had settled it...","Half a month later, Feng Jiu’s airship came to rest in a forest outside a city. She glanced at the few people beside her before stowing the airship away.","“We’re close to the city now. You can walk from here!” Feng Jiu said, ruffling Yue’er’s hair.","“Master, can’t you let my father and the others know your true identity?” Song Mi’er asked. Her recovery had been swift during the flight aboard the airship.","They had come to this area because the faction controlling the soul entity’s true form was based here. Since her family lived in the city ahead, she had agreed to bring them this far. She would handle her business while Song Mi’er waited at her home with the three children.","“The time isn’t right yet,” Feng Jiu replied, her gaze shifting to the three children.","“We’re already here. Won’t you come in with us, Master?” Song Mi’er looked at her and asked.","Feng Jiu shook her head. “Just take good care of these three for me. Once I’ve handled my business, I’ll come to the Song family to pick you all up.” She was preparing to take down that faction, and naturally, it wasn’t wise to bring the three children along. Since Mi’er’s family was right here, having the children stay with her for a few days was the best solution.","“Mother, you needn’t worry about us. Master trained us for trials. We know how to survive and handle dangers outside,” Hao’er spoke up, reassuring her.","Hearing this, Feng Jiu smiled, her eyes brimming with affection. “Mother knows. You’re the eldest, so keep a close eye on them. Alright, go now! Listen carefully to Sister Mi’er.”","“Yes.” The three replied in unison, looking back at her. “Mother, take care of yourself too. We’ll wait for you at Sister Mi’er’s house.”","“Mhm.” Feng Jiu nodded, turning to Song Mi’er. “I’m counting on you.”","“Rest assured, Master. I’ll take good care of them,” Song Mi’er replied with a radiant smile. Waving to her, she then led the three children toward the city gate.","Hao’er and Mu Chen flanked Yue’er, each taking one of her hands as they walked. Beside them, Song Mi’er followed, her face aglow with joy and excitement.","“I never imagined we’d return home so soon! When I left last time, I thought it would be years before I came back!” Her eyes sparkled with delight as she gazed upon the familiar surroundings, her heart soaring with joy.","“Once we get home, I’ll have my brothers cook something delicious for you,” Song Mi’er told them.","Yue’er’s eyes lit up as she looked at her. ” “Sister Mi’er, are the things they cook with you always that delicious?” She had been preparing delicious meals for them every day lately, and the food looked so appealing that it had spoiled her palate.","“Of course! My family is known for our exceptional skills in culinary. Everyone in my family is an extraordinary cook.” She lifted her chin proudly, her eyes and brows radiating confidence."]},{"number":4954,"title":"Chapter 4954: Aroma","paragraphs":["\"Do you think we're intruding by showing up like this?\" Hao'er asked, looking at her.","\"Not at all,\" Song Mi'er waved her hand. \"My family is really nice. Don't worry about feeling out of place.\"","As they spoke, Song Mi'er led them into the city, pointing out landmarks along the way. \"After resting at my place, if you want to go out tonight, I'll take you around. Or we can do it tomorrow—I'll show you all the fun spots in town!\"","\"Miss Mi'er!\"","\"Miss Mi'er is back!\"","\"It's been ages since we saw Miss Mi'er! Where have you been?\"","The street vendors in the city recognized Song Mi'er and greeted her with smiles. Their familiarity left Hao'er and the others utterly astonished.","While waving and responding to their greetings, Song Mi'er explained to the three beside her, \"My family is practically one of a kind in this city. Naturally, our standing differs from other clans. Plus, having grown up here since childhood, many people in town recognize me.\"","The trio understood. Following her along a bustling street, they soon turned into a quieter alley. She explained, \"The city has its exclusive neighborhoods for the wealthy. See that area up ahead? That's where the city's prominent families live. My house is just up there—easy to find.\"","As they neared the house, Song Mi'er quickened her pace. Leading them to the door, she beamed, \"We're here!\" and knocked.","A middle-aged man opened the door. Spotting Song Mi'er outside, his face lit up with delight. \"Miss Mi'er, you're back! Come in, come in!\"","He swung the door open for her while calling inside, \"Miss Mi'er is back! Quickly inform Master, Mistress, and the young masters!\"","Hao'er and the others followed Mi'er into the Song residence. The moment they stepped inside, a delicious aroma filled the air. The three exchanged glances and looked around.","Yue'er took a deep breath, her eyes sparkling as she looked at Song Mi'er beside her. \"Sister Mi'er, your house smells so good!\"","\"It must be my third brother cooking something again,\" Mi'er said with a smile. \"Perfect timing—we'll have something delicious to eat as soon as we arrive. Come, I'll take you to my third brother's kitchen to see what he's cooking.\" With that, she led them toward the back courtyard.","Nearly every member of the Song household had a large, separate kitchen in their courtyard. They often spent their days experimenting with dishes in these private kitchens.","Seeing Song Mi'er head straight for the back courtyard, the middle-aged man called out, \"Miss Mi'er, won't you go see Master and Mistress first? They've been asking about you constantly.\"","\"I'll go later. Tell my parents I'm eating at my third brother's courtyard and will join them shortly,\" Mi'er replied without turning back.","\"Miss.\"","\"Miss.\"","The maids curtsied as she passed, somewhat surprised to see her returning with three children.","\"This is my third brother's courtyard. Come on, let's head to the kitchen.\" Mi'er walked cheerfully toward the kitchen, gesturing for the three to follow.","Yue'er sniffed the fragrant air in the courtyard, her eyes sparkling as she said, \"Big Brother, Brother, Mi'er Sister's family is so interesting. It's different from other households.\""]},{"number":4955,"title":"Chapter 4955: Not the same","paragraphs":["Capítulo 4955: Not the same","“Hmm, it really is different.”","From the moment they entered until now, what they saw was unlike anything found in ordinary aristocratic families. Within the Song residence, places like pavilions and terraces, or areas near rockeries and ponds, featured decorations of animals or fruits and vegetables. These ornaments were so lifelike they seemed real. The very layout of the estate alone made it feel uniquely distinctive.","“I wonder what delicious food Sister Mi’er’s third brother has prepared,” Yue’er rubbed her hands in anticipation, trotting toward the kitchen.","Seeing this, Hao’er and Mu Chen hurried to follow.","In the kitchen, a man dressed in blue robes held a steaming dish as he addressed Song Mi’er: “I just heard you’ve returned and was planning to visit you later. I didn’t expect you’d come straight here. Perfect timing—come try this new pastry Third Brother made.”","His voice trailing off, the man in blue turned in surprise to the three children entering the room, then looked back at Song Mi’er and asked, “Did you bring them back?”","Linking her arm through his, Song Mi’er replied with a smile, “Third Brother, I smelled something delicious coming from your kitchen, so I came straight over.” “She then turned to Yue’er and the others, introducing them: “These three are my friends. I met them during my recent trip. This is Yun Chen, this is Yun Yuan, and this is Yun Qi.”","She then addressed Hao’er and the others: “This is my third brother, Song Yifan.”","Hearing this, the three exchanged glances and unison called out: “Brother Yifan.”","“Mi’er rarely brings friends home. You’re the first she’s ever brought,” Song Yifan smiled, gesturing to the three. “Come, sit over here. Freshly baked pastries—perfect for you to try.”","“Thank you, Brother Yifan,” the three replied gratefully, moving to sit at the nearby table.","Maidservants placed a small bowl, spoon, plate, and chopsticks before each of them. The tableware looked exquisitely crafted.","“You eat these like this,” Song Yifan instructed, carefully picking one up with chopsticks and placing it on a spoon. The thin, glossy skin steamed, releasing waves of enticing aroma. “Be careful—the soup inside is hot.”","“Pierce a corner to let the broth flow out. Sip the broth first, then eat the dumpling,” he demonstrated, ensuring the children wouldn’t burn their mouths.","“Third Brother, isn’t this the same as those soup-filled buns?” Song Mi’er asked, picking one up.","“Improved,” Song Yifan replied, his gaze fixed on the three children. “Thinner skin, more filling, and I used premium broth.”","Despite their young age, their demeanor was composed. The two boys sat upright, their posture straight, and their eating habits naturally exuded an air of nobility and elegance.","“Mi’er, they’re so young. Did their family know you brought them home?” Song Yifan asked, glancing at his sister who was eating without any grace.","“They know, they know! Don’t worry! I’m not kidnapping kids,” Mi’er said cheerfully, blowing on her spoonful of soup before taking a sip.","“Delicious, so delicious,” Yue’er beamed with satisfaction, picking up another piece as she spoke. “Big Brother Yifan, your pastries are amazing.”","“If you like them, have more. There’s plenty left.”","Song Yifan smiled, his gaze drifting toward the courtyard entrance. Spotting his parents and two older brothers approaching, he stood up and greeted them: “Father, Mother, Eldest Brother, Second Brother.”"]},{"number":4956,"title":"Chapter 4956: Heard","paragraphs":["Chapter 4956: Heard","“We knew the moment our little sister returned, she’d come straight to you.” Song Yiming chuckled, glancing inside. As he spotted his sister, he also noticed three children.","“I heard our little sister brought three children back with her. Is this them? They’re so young!” Song Yiming exclaimed, striding forward.","“Yiming, don’t frighten the children,” the matriarch of the Song family said gently, calling her second son to order.","“I know, Mother! I’m not scary-looking—how could I frighten them?” Song Yiming laughed.","“Father, Mother, Eldest Brother, Second Brother!” Mi’er spotted them approaching, quickly setting down her chopsticks, wiping her mouth, and standing up. She then threw herself into her mother’s arms.","“Mother, Mi’er missed you so much!” She wrapped her arms around her mother’s neck and snuggled into her embrace.","“Enough, enough! You’re practically an adult and still hugging your mother like this.” Song Lingbo, the head of the Song family standing nearby, felt his eyelid twitch at the sight of his daughter clinging to his wife. He grabbed her collar and pulled her away, scolding, “Stand up straight! You’re always so unladylike. How do you expect to marry properly someday?”","“Father, why are you so petty? What’s wrong with hugging Mother? You sleep with her every night, and neither I nor my brothers ever complained.” She stuck her tongue out at him.","Song Lingbo shook his head in exasperation and turned to his wife. “Look at her! What nonsense is she spouting? She’s just asking for a spanking.”","“Enough! Mi’er has been away so long. She rarely comes back. Stop scolding her. Besides, the other three children are here! Don’t make us look ridiculous.” The matriarch of the Song family shot him a reproachful glance before turning to the three children. She asked Mi’er, “Mi’er, where did you bring them from? Do their families know?”","“They know, they know! Don’t worry!” Song Mi’er linked arms with her mother and said, “Come, come, let me introduce you all.”","Seeing how Mi’er interacted and spoke with her family, Hao’er and the others were all taken aback, a bit stunned. They hadn’t expected this to be the Sister Mi’er they knew!","“This is my father, this is my mother, this is my eldest brother Song Yihong, and this is my second brother Song Yiming.” She then introduced Yue’er and the other two children by name.","“They’re my friends. I’m staying home for a while, and they’ll be staying here too,” Mi’er said, looking at them.","“That won’t be a problem at all. It’s rare you bring friends home, and three children at that. We’ll certainly take good care of them,” said the head of the Song family. “But you know how it is—your brothers sometimes disappear into the kitchen for days on end. So you’ll need to keep an extra eye on them yourself.”","“Yes, yes, I know,” Mi’er nodded in agreement.","Song Yihong regarded the three children thoughtfully, then paused. “Their names sound familiar. I heard the three disciples of the Azure Emperor were also named thus. Could there be a connection?”","Hearing this, the Song family members exchanged glances, then looked at the three children in surprise. Finally, they turned to Song Mi’er, silently questioning her.","“Huh?” Song Mi’er froze, her eyes wide with surprise. “How did you know the Azure Emperor’s disciples have these names, Brother?”","Song Yihong glanced at her, his tone calm and measured. “It’s said the Azure Emperor obtained the Ancient Divine Whip from the Immortal Lingmu specifically for his youngest disciple, Yun Qi. This story has spread far and wide.”"]},{"number":4957,"title":"Chapter 4957: Recognize","paragraphs":["After all, this was something the Azure Emperor himself had spoken of. He had inquired about it at the time, so he knew roughly about the Azure Emperor's three disciples and was familiar with their names.","The three individuals his sister had brought back today bore striking similarities in both age and names to the disciples of the Azure Emperor rumored outside. This was precisely why he had asked.","\"Brother Yihong, you're so sharp! Our master really is the Azure Emperor,\" Yue'er said with a beaming smile. Since they were Mi'er's family and had already guessed the truth, there was no harm in confirming it.","Hearing this, the Song family members exchanged glances, their eyes flickering with surprise. They hadn't expected these to truly be disciples of the Azure Emperor. After all, the Azure Emperor was a legendary figure, a great emperor of his realm. They could only hear tales of his majesty; meeting him in person was beyond their reach. Yet today, they had unexpectedly encountered three of his disciples.","Seeing the situation, Mi'er quickly interjected, \"Father, Mother, Eldest Brother, Second Brother, Third Brother—just know this much. Don't mention it to anyone else.\"","\"Understood. But how did you come to know them?\" the head of the Song family inquired curiously.","\"Hehe, well... I'll tell you later. I can't say now,\" Mi'er replied with an air of mystery.","\"Alright, alright. Take good care of them. Since they're rarely in the city, have your eldest brother accompany you all for a tour tomorrow.\" Patriarch Song then addressed Hao'er and the others: \"Consider this your home. If you need anything, just ask Mi'er. She'll see to it.\"","\"Thank you, Uncle Song,\" Hao'er bowed respectfully.","\"Thank you, Uncle Song,\" Mu Chen and Mu Yue echoed their elder brother's gesture, bowing in gratitude.","\"Third son, prepare some food for the children. Let them eat their fill before taking them to rest,\" Patriarch Song instructed. Turning to Song Mi'er beside him, he added, \"Come with me.\" With his hands clasped behind his back, he turned and walked back into the house.","Seeing this, Song Mi'er addressed the three children: \"Stay here and eat with my third brother. I'll be right back to take you to the courtyard.\" She then turned to Song Yifan: \"Third brother, keep an eye on them for me.\" With that, she hurried out of the courtyard.","Seeing their parents and younger sister leave, the three Song brothers exchanged smiles. Turning to the children, the eldest said, \"Come, sit over here. Third brother, bring up two more steamer baskets of those pastries—I'm hungry too.\"","\"Alright, take a seat!\" he called before heading toward the kitchen.","\"Brother Yihong, do you all enhance your strength just by cooking?\" Yue'er asked curiously.","\"Our family is a lineage of culinary cultivators. We have our own cultivation methods. It's not that cooking directly boosts our strength, but the dishes we prepare can enhance a person's cultivation base. Think of it like elixirs—that might make it easier for you to understand.\" \" Song Yihong added with a smile. \"You don't need to use our names. Just call us Brother Song, Second Brother Song, and Third Brother Song.\"","\"Alright.\" The three agreed, looking at the two men with their distinguished bearing. It was hard to imagine that men like cooking too.","Song Mi'er was summoned by her father to recount her recent journey, but she dodged his questions with vague answers. Instead, she slipped away to her third brother's courtyard, bringing Hao'er and the other two children there to rest.","The next day, the three Song brothers accompanied Mi'er and the children out to explore the city..."]},{"number":4958,"title":"Chapter 4958: Dilapidated Temple","paragraphs":["Capítulo 4958: Dilapidated Temple","On the other side, Feng Jiu headed in the opposite direction after leaving. From the soul-searching of those individuals, she learned that the faction had deep roots within Blazing Sun City.","To locate the true form of that person among the scattered strongholds within Blazing Sun City, she would likely need to conduct further investigations.","She sped along at an extraordinary pace, yet Blazing Sun City remained distant. Combined with her stops to rest, she hadn’t yet entered its territory.","Mid-flight, she noticed the sky darkening and the wind strengthening. After a moment’s thought, she decided to find a place below to rest her feet.","After gliding a considerable distance, she saw no inhabited dwellings. Only at the foot of a mountain did she spot a dilapidated temple. Yet, upon seeing it, her brows furrowed slightly, and her pace hesitated.","This dilapidated temple stood in a remote spot. Though it was now midday, a pervasive aura of Yin-sha energy still hung around it, clearly marking it as an extremely inauspicious place.","She paused only briefly before heading toward the temple. With her current cultivation and strength, such a place and its sinister aura could not harm her. Moreover, this area fell within her domain. If she hadn’t encountered such a sinister place, that would be one thing, but since she had, she naturally intended to purge it.","Stepping through the temple’s doorway, she cast a casual glance inside. Several cultivators sat cross-legged in meditation. Noticing her entrance, they glanced at her briefly before returning their focus to their practice.","She withdrew her gaze, walked to a corner, and sat against the wall. She retrieved water from her spatial pouch and drank. Her features were altered, her aura subdued, and she wore plain blue robes. Even as a woman, she drew no attention.","The Yin-evil aura within this dilapidated temple was faint yet perceptible, especially to cultivators. Even if they couldn’t discern its full nature, they could sense its presence to some degree. Yet these cultivators had chosen to rest here. Was it sheer overconfidence in their own strength and cultivation? Or had they simply failed to notice the latent danger lurking within this ruined temple?","She took a couple sips of water to moisten her throat, listening as the wind grew stronger, whistling through the dilapidated temple. The sky darkened, and it seemed a downpour was inevitable.","Though cultivators could shield themselves with spirit energy, stopping to rest and shelter from the rain wasn’t unthinkable unless truly urgent matters demanded otherwise. Especially in such a place steeped in Yin energy.","Seeing the storm approaching with ferocity, she decided to close her eyes and rest for a while. Putting away her water, she settled in to rest.","The corner she occupied sheltered her from the wind, and with Spirit Energy protecting her, even the strong gusts didn’t feel cold. After a while, she faintly heard the patter of rain, growing louder and louder. As the wind and rain intensified, muffled thunder rumbled in the distance.","Perhaps due to the shifting weather and the howling storm, the atmosphere within the dilapidated temple gradually grew colder.","“Why is it getting colder? This wind is giving me goosebumps,” a cultivator in his twenties muttered while rubbing his arms.","Another suggested, “There’s a door panel over there. If we prop it up to block the wind, it should help.”","“Alright.” The younger cultivator agreed, stepping forward to lift the door panel from the corner and wedge it against the temple entrance. Once shielded, the wind stopped blowing in. Though the chill remained, it felt considerably better."]},{"number":4959,"title":"Chapter 4959: Hidden Danger","paragraphs":["Chapter 4959: Hidden Danger","“I didn’t expect so many people passing through here today. Two more carriages are coming up ahead—probably seeking shelter from the rain too.”","The twenty-something cultivator remarked in surprise, peering through the door crack. But as their carriage drew nearer, someone leaned out from the front carriage to glance at the dilapidated temple before retreating back inside. Simultaneously, both carriages and their entourages began backing away, eventually halting by the roadside about a hundred meters back.","“Weird. Why did they back off?” the young cultivator in his twenties asked, his gaze fixed on the two carriages and their entourage a hundred meters away.","“Hmph! Probably scared off by this dense Yin place,” a middle-aged cultivator scoffed, arms crossed as he rested with eyes closed. “Bunch of cowards.”","“What dense yin place?” the other two cultivators asked, their brows furrowing.","“This dilapidated temple, of course! Haven’t you sensed the heavy yin energy here, mingled with a touch of murderous energy?” the middle-aged cultivator said, glancing at the two beside him. “It was better before the rain. Now that it’s raining, the yin energy has grown heavier, and the atmosphere feels even colder.”","Hearing this, the two men’s expressions shifted slightly. They immediately stood up. “We hadn’t noticed it, but since this place is like this, we certainly can’t linger here long, lest we invite trouble.”","With that, they headed toward the entrance of the dilapidated temple. Glancing back at the seated middle-aged cultivator, the young cultivator standing by the door with a puzzled expression, and the green-robed woman sleeping with closed eyes in the corner, they hesitated briefly before offering a well-meaning warning: “You lot, I’ve heard my master say that Yin-Shattered Qi is no ordinary force. If your strength and cultivation aren’t sufficient, you could easily become entangled by it. You’d best leave quickly! Especially you, young lady. As a woman, you’re even more susceptible to its grasp.”","Hearing this, Feng Jiu opened her eyes and glanced at the two. Nodding, she said, “Alright, you may go.” She remained seated, unmoving.","“Two grown men, yet not as bold as a woman,” the middle-aged cultivator remarked with a dismissive glance, his eyes brimming with contempt.","The two cultivators refrained from arguing. Instead, they bowed respectfully to Feng Jiu. “Farewell, young lady. Take care.” With that, they turned and walked out.","Outside, they immediately shielded themselves with spiritual energy. The rain was deflected by the protective barrier, leaving them completely dry. Though sustaining this shield drained their spiritual energy reserves, they had no other choice. Their sole focus was to distance themselves from this place. Thus, they flew through the storm on their swords, their bodies constantly shielded by the energy barrier.","Along the mountain path, two horse-drawn carriages stood. While the passengers inside were sheltered by the carriages themselves, the seven or eight attendants remained by the vehicles, hastily erecting small tents along the roadside for shelter.","The fierce wind and heavy rain made the muddy path treacherous. To prevent the carriages from overturning in the storm or the horses from bolting in fright, they had no choice but to halt here and wait for the downpour to ease.","Inside the lead carriage, a middle-aged man tucked a blanket around the reclining elder and said, “Father, the storm is too violent now. We must wait for it to subside before continuing.”","“Mm.” The old man, eyes closed and face pale, responded weakly.","“Brother, isn’t there a dilapidated temple up ahead? Why not take shelter there?” The man in his thirties sitting beside him asked in confusion, glancing toward the ruined temple. “There are people taking shelter inside!”"]},{"number":4960,"title":"Chapter 4960: Kind","paragraphs":["\"That place is too heavy with Yin energy,\" the middle-aged man said, frowning.","\"But aren't there people sheltering from the rain inside? If they aren't afraid, we certainly don't need to be,\" the man in his thirties countered, dismissing the notion of it being a Yin-ridden place.","\"Listen to your elder brother,\" the old man murmured without opening his eyes, his voice weak. He trusted his eldest son's judgment; if the place were truly unsafe, they wouldn't have stopped by the roadside.","Hearing his father speak, the man in his thirties said no more.","\"You stay here with Father. I'll go to the back to make arrangements, then check that dilapidated temple to see who's inside and give them a heads-up.\" The middle-aged man said, preparing to dismount.","Hearing this, the man in his thirties couldn't help but twitch the corner of his mouth. He grabbed his brother's arm and said, \"Big brother, why do you care so much about those people? Maybe they aren't afraid of the dense yin? Besides, it's none of our business. We're not related to them. Why meddle? Instead of worrying about them, we should figure out a way to deal with this storm. Look, it's so fierce it's shaking our carriage. It might get blown over any minute now!\"","The middle-aged man glanced at him and replied, \"When traveling, cultivating good karma never hurts. A simple warning costs us nothing, but for them, it might just save their lives.\"","As the words fell, he felt the fierce wind and rain outside, blowing and scraping against the carriage, causing it to sway gently. He said, \"I'll get off and take a look up ahead to see if there's any shelter from the storm. This wind and rain came on so suddenly and feels rather ominous. Who knows when it will stop.\"","\"Go ahead! Be careful,\" the old man opened his eyes and said to him.","\"I'll be back soon.\" With that, he stepped down from the carriage. He first went to the rear carriage to give a brief warning before heading toward the dilapidated temple. However, he didn't approach too closely. Instead, he called out from a distance, his voice carrying a hint of spiritual energy.","\"Friends in the temple, this place is heavy with Yin energy. It's not a good shelter from the storm. You'd be better off leaving and finding another place!\"","He called out once, not waiting for a response, and swiftly moved forward along the path to investigate.","His formidable strength and spiritual energy shield made him unafraid of the storm. Yet, hearing the muffled thunder, he couldn't help but glance back, hesitation creeping into his steps.","Something felt off about this storm.","After walking a considerable distance without spotting any dwellings, he returned to the carriage to shelter from the elements. As the sky darkened further and the storm showed no sign of abating, he pondered briefly before instructing his attendants to drive the carriage into a small grove.","Thus, the group sought refuge in the grove, distancing themselves further from the dilapidated temple.","Inside the dilapidated temple, Feng Jiu's lips curved slightly. It seemed the world wasn't entirely filled with cold-hearted souls. At least, within this broken temple, she'd already encountered two kind-hearted people who'd warned her.","As the sound of wind and rain grew louder, the whistling within the temple intensified, and the air grew colder and colder. She stood up and walked towards the temple's doorway.","The young cultivator standing by the doorway wore a troubled expression, lost in thought. Seeing Feng Jiu rise and approach the entrance, he assumed she too intended to leave and promptly stepped aside to make way for her.","Feng Jiu stood by the doorway and looked outside. This storm was indeed unusual. It didn't feel like a normal wind and rain, but rather...","Just as she pondered this, a piercing scream echoed from behind her."]},{"number":4961,"title":"Chapter 4961: Hard to live","paragraphs":["Chapter 4961: Hard to live","She immediately turned to look and saw the middle-aged man convulsing on the ground, a dark, malevolent aura coiling around him.","“Uncle Master!”","The young cultivator cried out in alarm but dared not approach. Instead, he stumbled backward, turned, and fled into the storm with a startled cry.","Feng Jiu glanced at the fleeing cultivator, her brows furrowing slightly. In the next instant, a flame coalesced in her palm. Whoosh! It shot from her hand, streaking toward the convulsing middle-aged man on the ground.","“Ah!”","A piercing, shrill scream echoed faintly. The moment the flame struck, the sinister aura coiled around the middle-aged cultivator retreated as if encountering something dreadful, vanishing without a trace.","Feng Jiu stepped forward. With a flick of her intent, the flame enveloping the middle-aged cultivator split into three. One cluster hovered above his head, while two smaller ones settled beneath his feet.","As the flames burned, the middle-aged cultivator’s hair was reduced to ash. The intense heat radiating from the flames beneath his feet forced the last trace of Yin-Shadow Qi within him to retreat. A visible wisp of Yin-Shadow Qi rose from his now-bald head, only to be consumed entirely by the flames.","“CRACK!”","A thunderbolt suddenly struck from the sky, landing precisely at the willow tree behind the dilapidated temple.","Sensing this was no ordinary storm lightning but calamity lightning, she swiftly rotated her palm. Several clusters of flame floated and hovered in the corners of the dilapidated temple. Simultaneously, she stepped out of the temple and headed toward its rear.","The middle-aged cultivator on the ground awoke shortly after Feng Jiu departed. Still shaken, he scrambled up and glanced around frantically. Seeing only himself, his face paled further. Recalling that earlier feeling of being utterly powerless, he disregarded the storm outside and rushed toward the exit.","But as he reached the temple entrance, he was violently repelled, as if an invisible barrier held him back, preventing his escape.","“Help! Help! Let me out! Let me out!”","He shouted, trying to break through the barrier of Yin energy with sheer force. But the storm raged outside, thunder boomed louder still, and the Yin energy within seemed to stir, howling and roaring through the dilapidated temple. Yet it too appeared trapped, unable to escape.","Behind the temple, Feng Jiu stood in the storm. Her protective aura of spiritual energy caused the rain to automatically avoid her. Her gaze fell upon the willow tree struck by lightning, observing the dense, sinister aura spreading out from it as its focal point.","She had already sensed something amiss about this storm. Now it became clear: the source of the gathering Yin energy within the temple lay beneath this willow, and this Yin energy sought to take shape through the tree.","Willows themselves possess the power to ward off evil spirits. Yet, the fact that this Yin energy could entwine itself around the willow revealed its extraordinary nature.","In the small grove, the middle-aged man who had paused at the sound of thunder had been resting inside the carriage. Now, he leaned out once more, gazing toward the dilapidated temple, a sigh escaping his lips.","That disturbance could be felt even here. The few people inside that ruined temple... they likely wouldn’t survive.","“Help me up,” the old man who had been lying in the carriage spoke."]},{"number":4962,"title":"Chapter 4962: Saw","paragraphs":["Chapter 4962: Saw","“Yes.” The middle-aged man hurried back to the carriage, helping him sit up against the wall. The man in his thirties beside him pulled the blanket up higher.","“Father, has lying down too long made you uncomfortable? Sitting might be better. I’ve just brewed some tea—let’s have a warm cup!” The man in his thirties spoke as he prepared to pour a cup.","The old man waved his hand, lifted the curtain, and gazed toward the dilapidated temple. His brow furrowed as he spoke weakly, “This storm and thunder... likely signify the Yin and murderous intent are condensing within that ruined temple and is nearing its formative stage—the Heavenly Thunder Tribulation. Should that truly take shape, the calamity would be endless.”","Hearing this, the middle-aged man fell silent for a moment before replying, “Father, once Yin and all the murderous energy condense and takes form, it will be unstoppable. I fear even we won’t be able to prevent it.”","“No,” the elder countered, his gaze fixed on his son. “That commotion sounds like someone has already intervened. Go see. Give that person a hand.”","“Father, why send my elder brother? What if something happens to him? Besides, we’ve retreated this far. Whether that yin-evil exists or not, it’s none of our concern. Why meddle?” The man in his thirties beside him voiced his disapproval.","“I’ll go check. If I can help, I will.” The middle-aged man said, then turned to the younger man: “You take care of Father.”","Seeing this, the man in his thirties frowned. Realizing he couldn’t stop him, he said no more, only adding, “Brother, just go and see. If you can’t help, don’t force it. Don’t bring trouble upon yourself.” He paused, then added, “And be careful. If things look bad, get out of there fast.”","Hearing this, a faint smile touched the stern face of the middle-aged man. “Understood,” he replied. Nodding briefly to his father, he stepped down from the carriage, exited the grove, and headed toward the dilapidated temple.","At that moment, Feng Jiu was using flames to cast an array, purging the Yin energy. The visible Yin-evil energy clung to the willow tree, its branches whipping wildly like a raging beast, clawing and snarling.","“Who are you? Why do you obstruct my formation! Why?!”","A shrill, icy voice echoed with intense hatred and resentment. The energies struggled against the constraints of the flame-formed array, but its efforts proved futile.","“Thud! Thud! Thud!”","The willow’s roots, deep in the earth and saturated with the dark aura, suddenly burst upward. Dirt mixed with rainwater erupted from the ground, carrying a chill that surged toward Feng Jiu.","Feng Jiu’s expression remained calm. She merely glanced at the ground, not even shifting her stance. As the willow roots surged upward, she lifted one foot and pressed it back down with what appeared to be a light step.","“Thud!”","“Arghhhh!”","That seemingly light step contained terrifying, immense power. Where her foot landed, flames rippled outward like water, catching the willow roots off guard. The already largely scorched Yin energy was now completely incinerated.","The surrounding Yin-evil aura, along with that within the dilapidated temple, coalesced in that instant into a shrunken mass at the willow tree’s base, emitting a piercing, wretched scream.","The middle-aged man who had intended to assist watched the scene unfold before him with utter shock and disbelief, frozen in place for a moment..."]},{"number":4963,"title":"Chapter 4963: Settled","paragraphs":["He hadn't expected to see a woman in azure here. Judging by her appearance, she was only in her twenties, yet unexpectedly, her cultivation was remarkably powerful.","Possessing formidable strength himself, he could instantly discern the sinister aura permeating this place and knew how difficult it would be to purge. He had assumed an elderly predecessor would intervene here, but never imagined it would be this woman.","He suppressed the turmoil within, hiding the shock and bewilderment in his eyes. His gaze flickered as he watched the flames spreading beneath her feet in the wind and rain.","If his eyes did not deceive him, that was Heavenly Fire. Only Heavenly Fire possessed the power to utterly consume such evil energy. Historically, cultivators who possessed innate Heavenly Fire were mostly alchemists or artifact forgers. But which path did this woman follow? Or both? And how could she wield such formidable power?","Feng Jiu merely turned her head to glance indifferently at the figure approaching from behind before fixing her gaze back on the willow tree.","The flames on the ground rippled outward in concentric circles, converging toward the tree's center. The scorched earth beneath them was not merely drenched by rain—the soil itself had been charred black and cracked dry, let alone the roots hidden beneath.","The air was filled with the sound of a reluctant roar, now growing faint. Yet it persisted, asking over and over: \"Who are you? Who are you? Who are you, exactly? Who...\"","Hearing the echoing voice, the middle-aged man behind stirred slightly. He glanced at the woman in green robes. Not only did the Yin Fiend want to know, but he himself also yearned to discover—who exactly was this woman?","\"Running into me was your bad luck,\" Feng Jiu spoke slowly, her voice cold and detached. As her words fell, the flames on the ground had already reached the middle of the willow tree, climbing upward along its trunk.","Hissing sounds mingled with wisps of black smoke billowing upward, only to dissipate into the vastness of sky and earth. Simultaneously, the roaring voice gradually fell silent.","Just as the willow was completely consumed, the storm-laden, gloomy sky began to clear. The dark clouds lifted, the wind died down, and the rain ceased. After the tempest, blue skies and white clouds emerged, and a rainbow arched over the ruined temple.","At that moment, a ball of flame carried a small, rectangular box, flying toward her and landing before her feet.","Feng Jiu raised an eyebrow, glancing at the so-called rectangular box. To her surprise, it was a small coffin made of black divine wood.","\"So that's how it is.\" It was the black divine wood nurturing that Yin-evil energy—no wonder it dared to take the form of a willow tree. Had she not happened to pass by and encounter this today, likely no one could have stopped that Yin-evil energy from taking shape.","With a flick of her wrist, the ebony coffin plunged into the flames. Soon, the scent of ebony wood wafted from the fire, until finally, not even ashes remained—it vanished completely within the flames.","She turned and glanced at the dilapidated temple.","Originally, she had planned to burn the dilapidated temple after sheltering from the rain, consuming the Yin aura entirely. Now that the Yin aura had been purged, whether the temple burned or not was of little consequence.","She brushed the azure robe on her body, satisfied that the matter was settled, and prepared to leave. Just then, the middle-aged man called out to her."]},{"number":4964,"title":"Chapter 4964: Name","paragraphs":["Chapter 4964: Name","“Please wait, young lady.” The middle-aged man, having regained his composure, hurried forward. Seeing her halt her steps, he bowed respectfully with clasped hands: “Your noble deed deserves this salute from Huangfu Xiao.”","Feng Jiu turned sideways, declining his salute, and replied, “You flatter me. It was merely a coincidence.”","“This Yin aura was exceptionally strong and sinister. Huangfu Xiao admits he had no absolute confidence in handling it. Yet you incinerated it in the blink of an eye. Your skill is truly masterful. Huangfu Xiao is thoroughly impressed.” He spoke with genuine admiration.","Feng Jiu remained silent, merely observing him.","Just as Huangfu Xiao prepared to speak again, a voice called out from behind him.","“Brother, are you all right?”","He turned to see the carriage that had been parked in the grove had somehow appeared on the main road. The curtain was lifted, revealing his fourth brother calling out to him. Inside the carriage, his father’s gaze was faintly visible, fixed upon them.","“Farewell,” Feng Jiu said, gathering her breath to mount her sword and depart.","Hearing her farewell, Huangfu Xiao turned to look, but only her figure was vanishing into the clouds. Before long, she was completely out of sight. He then hurried toward the carriage.","“Father,” he said upon entering the carriage, looking at his father. “I never imagined the one who extinguished that Yin evil was a young lady. It’s a pity I was just about to ask her about her master when I missed the chance.” He sighed. “That young lady might be an alchemist.”","He regretted missing such a prime opportunity to inquire. An alchemist capable of commanding celestial fire likely possessed formidable rank. Coupled with her profoundly unfathomable cultivation, his heart was filled with nothing but regret.","“If fate permits, we shall meet again. If not, even knowing her lineage would be of no consequence to us,” the old man said weakly, a hand pressed to his lips as he coughed.","“The storm has passed. Brother, can we leave now?” asked the man in his thirties.","“Let’s go!”","He signaled the driver to continue, just as a middle-aged cultivator emerged from the ruined temple, muttering to himself. His face was dusty, his head completely bald, giving him a somewhat comical appearance.","“Uncle Master! You... you’re still alive?” A young man, seemingly returning from somewhere, shouted as he ran toward the middle-aged man.","The middle-aged cultivator suddenly broke into a silly grin, shoving him aside and walking onward by himself, muttering to himself as he went. The young man seemed to freeze for a moment before hurrying after him. As for what they were saying... no one cared anymore...","Several days later, in an inn, Feng Jiu sat on the first floor, drinking wine in large gulps while listening to the hushed whispers of the patrons.","“Did you hear about last night’s incident?”","“Heard about it. They say several bases of some faction were wiped out. Now their people are investigating, and even the major clans and factions in the city are on alert. But no one knows who did it.”","“To wipe out those dens in a single night? That must’ve been a full squad, and definitely premeditated.”","Feng Jiu took a sip of wine, summoned the waiter to settle the bill, then rose and headed outside.","She planned to rest today. Come tonight, she’d take out the remaining strongholds. She refused to believe she couldn’t find that person’s hiding place!"]},{"number":4965,"title":"Chapter 4965: Lady Xuanyuan","paragraphs":["Chapter 4965: Lady Xuanyuan","Feng Jiu had been resting at the inn until late afternoon when she finally emerged. Though dusk had not yet fully fallen, night stalls had already been set up along the main street. As it was not yet the peak hour of the night market, the street was not particularly crowded.","As she strolled along, she spotted Huangfu Xiao—the man she’d encountered at that dilapidated temple days ago—hurrying toward her. She continued walking at a leisurely pace without stopping, yet he bowed his hands in greeting before he even drew near.","“Miss, I never imagined we’d meet again here.”","Feng Jiu halted and looked at him, asking, “Is there something you need?”","“Ever since we parted that day, I’ve wondered when I might see you again. Today, one of my household guards went out on an errand and saw you enter the inn. He returned specifically to report it to me. Upon hearing the news, I hurried here to pay my respects and invite you to my residence for a chat.”","Huangfu Xiao spoke, but seeing her silence, he quickly added, “You see, my Huangfu family is one of the prominent clans in this city. With you here, I wish to offer you hospitality as a host. And also... I would like to ask you to examine my father.”","Hearing this, Feng Jiu raised an eyebrow. “Diagnose? How did you conclude I’m a physician?”","“I cannot say for certain, Huangfu Xiao,” he replied. “But witnessing your skill that day, and noticing the faint scent of medicine about you, led me to this assumption.” He added, “Whether or not you can cure my father, Huangfu Xiao would be eternally grateful.”","Feng Jiu’s gaze flickered as she studied the man before her. His earlier warning had shown kindness. Now, encountering him again in this city, lending a hand seemed reasonable. Though, the matter she was about to attend to...","After a moment’s thought, her expression shifted, and a faint smile touched her lips. “Lead the way.”","Huangfu Xiao paused, taken aback. He hadn’t expected her to agree to such an abrupt invitation. His heart leapt with joy, and he immediately gestured, “Please follow me.” He then led the way himself.","Though few people were on the street at that hour, this scene still drew curious whispers. “Isn’t that the head of the Huangfu family?” murmured one passerby. “Why is he being so respectful to that girl? She’s dressed in plain blue robes and looks quite ordinary—she certainly doesn’t seem like someone connected to a great family like the Huangfus!”","Whispers rippled through the crowd. Meanwhile, Huangfu Xiao personally escorted Feng Jiu into the mansion. As night had fallen, he didn’t take her directly to his father’s quarters but invited her to wait in the main hall.","“May I inquire about your noble surname, young lady?” he asked, his gaze resting on the elegantly composed woman in blue.","The Huangfu family was a century-old noble house. Even cultivators from other prestigious families would scrutinize the manor upon entering. Yet this woman remained utterly composed—neither haughty nor humble—as if nothing within the estate could catch her attention. She seemed utterly ordinary.","He began to suspect she might be descended from a similarly ancient lineage. Otherwise, her demeanor wouldn’t be so remarkably steady.","Feng Jiu lifted her teacup, sipped lightly, then set it down. “My husband’s family name is Xuanyuan. You may simply address me as Lady Xuanyuan.”","Huangfu Xiao froze upon hearing this, immediately rising with an apologetic tone. “I was unaware earlier and addressed you as ‘young lady.’ For my discourtesy, I beg Lady Xuanyuan’s forgiveness.”","He hadn’t expected her to be married, for it was common among cultivators of higher cultivation to marry later in life."]},{"number":4966,"title":"Chapter 4966: Identity","paragraphs":["Chapter 4966: Identity","“It’s nothing.”","Feng Jiu spoke, looking at him with a faint smile. “You guessed correctly. I am a doctor and also an alchemist. From that distant glance I caught of your father’s condition that day, it seems not some sudden illness, but rather a long-standing ailment flaring up, draining his lifespan until it is nearly exhausted!”","Huangfu Xiao stared at her in shock, momentarily speechless.","She had deduced his father’s condition merely from a distant glance days prior? Such skill was unprecedented. In recent years, he had taken his father to countless doctors and alchemists, yet never encountered anyone possessing such ability.","His emotions churned violently. His gaze fixed on her, his eyes reflecting not only shock but also speculation and confusion.","A person possessing such abilities could not be obscure. She had not introduced herself by name, but instead referred to herself by her husband’s surname.","Who exactly was this Lady Xuanyuan?","Seeing his stunned expression, Feng Jiu smiled. “I can cure your father’s chronic ailment and extend his life. However, I need you to do something for me in return.”","Huangfu Xiao suppressed his shock. He didn’t agree immediately. Instead, his brow furrowed deeply as he asked gravely, “May I ask, Lady Xuanyuan, what do you require of me?”","Feng Jiu held her teacup, gently scraping the surface of the tea with the lid. Unhurriedly, she replied, “Spread the word that you’ve obtained a thousand-year-old Wu Ling Ginseng.”","“A thousand-year-old Wu Ling Ginseng? The legendary one said to possess miraculous powers—restoring flesh to bones, reviving the dead, and nurturing the soul?” he asked in astonishment.","“Indeed.” Feng Jiu nodded, giving him an appreciative look. She hadn’t expected him to know of such a treasure.","Huangfu Xiao’s brow furrowed deeply as he asked, “What is Lady Xuanyuan intending to achieve? Setting aside the fact that my household possesses no such treasure, merely spreading this rumor could be enough to bring down a clan-wiping calamity upon the Huangfu family.”","Such a heavenly treasure possessed far more than just the power to resurrect the dead and restore flesh to bones. If word of it spread, the Huangfu family would never know peace again.","“I will not allow your Huangfu family to be embroiled in disaster,” Feng Jiu stated.","“No, Lady Xuanyuan, you do not grasp the gravity of this matter,” He shook his head. This matter wasn’t something she could resolve with a single word, nor would her assurance that it wouldn’t bring disaster upon the Huangfu clan truly prevent it.","Seeing his reaction, Feng Jiu merely smiled. “Just watch.”","Huangfu Xiao heard her words and was puzzled by their meaning. A wisp of spiritual energy surged from her body, and between her brows, a blue lotus with flame-like patterns slowly materialized.","“Th-this...”","His eyes widened in shock, his usual composure and calmness vanishing in an instant. Gazing at the azure lotus with fiery patterns between her brows, a tidal wave of dread surged within him. His thoughts immediately turned to the Sovereign Phoenix, the sovereign of their realm...","“Thud!”","His legs buckled involuntarily, forcing him to his knees. His mouth opened, and he stammered out, “So... So... Sovereign Phoenix!”","Feng Jiu had no intention of revealing her identity. Yet, unless she did, Huangfu Xiao would never believe she possessed the power to protect his Huangfu clan without worry. Thus, she allowed the Blue Lotus Seal to manifest upon her brow, displaying the emblem of her status.","“Do you believe me now?” she asked, suppressing her aura and concealing the lotus upon her forehead."]},{"number":4967,"title":"Chapter 4967: Excited","paragraphs":["Capítulo 4967: Excited","“Believe! I believe! I believe!” He said in a rush, sweat oozing from his forehead from nervousness.","“Get up and talk!” She signaled, but saw that after he got up, he didn’t dare to sit on the upper seat again, but instead went to sit across from her.","“Phoe...”","As his words came out, Feng Jiu then raised her hand and signaled, “My identity should not be revealed now, just call me Lady Xuanyuan.”","“Yes yes.” He wiped his sweat and hurriedly answered, then asked, “Lady Xuanyuan, I don’t know what I need to do? Is it enough to directly release the news?”","If there were hesitations as well as worries earlier, after learning of her identity, those scruples no longer existed. Sitting here at this moment, he still felt a bit incredulous.","The existence that was out of reach and high up for them actually came to their Huangfu family like this, sitting in front of him, their Huangfu family was only afraid that their ancestors’ graves were smoking, right?","“You’re so ...” Feng Jiu slowly said, carefully telling him about the matter.","After hearing her words, he then nodded and immediately said, “Yes, I will immediately go and make arrangements.” With that, he added, “Lady Xuanyuan, the night is already late, I wonder if I should first take you to the courtyard to rest?”","“Just call someone at random to take me there, what you’ve been instructed to do, you get to work on it! Tomorrow morning, I will go and help your father.” She stood up and spoke.","“Yes.” With a grateful response, he summoned the butler and asked him to personally take her over to the courtyard to rest.","After she left, he hurriedly ordered down again, telling everyone in the residence to wait carefully, and hurriedly went to his father’s courtyard again.","As soon as he entered the courtyard, he dismissed his subordinates and even laid a soundproof boundary.","When the old man lying on the bed saw him like this, he asked, “What happened?”","“Father, a great joy, the heavens have blessed my Huangfu family!” He couldn’t hide the excitement and joy on his face, and rushed forward to help his father up, using a pillow to cushion his waist with a joyful expression.","“What is the big deal?” Seeing his eldest son, who had always been joyful, this excited and elated, the old man’s heart was also slightly moved and somewhat curious.","“Father, our Huangfu family has come with an honored guest ...” He hurriedly told him the matter carefully.","After hearing his words, the old man’s face also revealed a joyful color, his eyes had a light and radiance that was not present in the past days, holding his hand with one hand, he said excitedly, “It’s actually like this? Is it really that person? Are you sure? There is no mistake?”","“There will be no mistake, she is the Female Emperor Phoenix Sovereign of our piece of heaven and earth, things about her have long been secretly rumored by the people of the various cities and clans, so how could I be mistaken?” Huangfu Xiao said, his brows filled with joy.","“Good good good!”","The old man said three good words in a row, holding his son’s hand while patting the back of his hand, “This is truly God’s blessing on my Huangfu family! You have to do a good job with this matter, you must not make any mistakes.”","“I know.” Huangfu Xiao nodded, paused for a moment, and then added, “However, she didn’t tell me what she was doing this for? However, I have a vague guess in my heart that it is probably related to certain people in our city.”","“Well, it could be that she wants to lure a certain person out, and by releasing the news of this Thousand-Year Wu Ling Ginseng to go out, that person will surely be unable to sit still, and at that time, there is no need for her to go searching for it, and she will be able to find the one she’s looking for by herself.” The old man spoke slowly while calming his agitation."]},{"number":4968,"title":"Chapter 4968: Huangfu Yunxue","paragraphs":["Chapter 4968: Huangfu Yunxue","“Remember to treat them well, you can’t be rude.” The old man uneasily handed over a sentence.","“Father don’t worry, I know, I’ve already instructed the people below to serve carefully.” Huangfu Xiao said.","The old man paused for a moment, and not knowing what came to his mind, he added: “Let Yunxue go over and serve, if she serves well, it might be a chance for her.”","Hearing these words, Huangfu Xiao was slightly surprised, but after a moment of silence, he said, “Father, would it be too deliberate to let Yunxue go over to serve? I’m worried that it will cause that Lady Xuanyuan to be displeased.”","The old man shook his head, revealing a smile, “No, Yunxue is the most quiet and calm person among the juniors, letting her go over to wait on her, firstly, to show the importance of my Huangfu family to Lady Xuanyuan, secondly, Yunxue is also a child that can take care of people, as for whether she can get into that person’s eyes, it’s up to her.”","Upon hearing this, Huangfu Xiao then said, “Good, then I will go and make arrangements now, father rest early, tomorrow morning Lady Xuanyuan will come over to treat father.”","“Well, go!” The old man nodded, his entire person had relaxed, the sorrow that had condensed on his brow due to the worry over his body also finally dispersed at this moment.","Withdrawing the soundproof boundary, Huangfu Xiao left the courtyard and headed for another courtyard.","This night, it can be said that he was excited and thrilled, after arranging all the things, it was already late at night in the wee hours of the morning, but even though it was late at night, he still did not have any sleep.","Noble for Huangfu family’s first-born young lady, Huangfu Yunxue small by the House of the best cultivation, whether it is the cultivation or heart and so on, she in a group of sisters are considered to be out of the ordinary.","Just her nature does not compete, usually talk less, so, even if it is a first-born young lady, but the sense of existence is not big, the only thing that can be said is that the Old Patriarch is very fond of her, in the past when he was physically well, from time to time to point out her cultivation.","For her father suddenly came to hand over to let her to wait for an honorable guest, even for someone like her who was usually calm, she was stunned for a while, and as she asked her questions, but did not get any answers. He only heft her these words: This is an extremely honorable guest, it is your good fortune to be able to serve her.","Such a sentence without a beginning and end, made her not able to sleep the entire night.","Early in the morning, she sent the personal maid beside her to inquire, only to realize that she had set off a series of false alarm in her heart. Originally, she thought that the guest was a man, hence she was pleasantly surprised that it was a lady.","After knowing that the other party was a lady, her heart also put down, early in the morning after cleaning up, she will go to the lady living in the courtyard early to serve her.","Feng Jiu just woke up, because of the movement, then heard a soft and pleasant voice from outside.","“Is the lady awake?”","Always casual she, not yet washed up will open the door, room door opened, will see that the door stood a slender young girl, about sixteen or seventeen years old, a plain dress, the face is born extremely excellent, the whole person through a clean breath.","At this moment, her good-looking face was wearing a shallow smile, and when she saw her, her demeanor was elegant as she gently bent her knees and blessed a line: “Huangfu Yunxue has met you, my lady.”","“Hm?” Feng Jiu’s eyes were only half open as she just woke up, still groggy, she asked: “You are the young lady of the Huangfu family?”","“Yes , I was ordered by my father to come and serve my lady.” She spoke softly."]},{"number":4969,"title":"Chapter 4969: Treatment","paragraphs":["\"Wait outside!\" Feng Jiu didn't say much but closed the door to her room and then washed and changed inside.","After a while, she walked out and saw that breakfast had already been set up in the courtyard.","\"My lady, I asked the kitchen to boil some clear porridge and stir fry a few small dishes, can you taste if it is to your liking.\" Huangfu Yunxue said softly, lightly moved to the table, scooped a small bowl of porridge for her, and then retreated to the side to wait.","Feng Jiu saw her demeanor, movement skillful and natural, then walked up and sat down, looking at the clear porridge in front of her and a few delicious congee small dishes, her eyes flickered slightly, without saying anything, she used a spoon to drink a mouthful of porridge, and picked some small dishes to eat.","She ate unhurriedly, in the meantime, without her having to say anything more, when the bowl of congee was finished, Huangfu Yunxue, who was waiting by the side, would come forward to add some more for her, after she put down her chopsticks, seeing that she had eaten her fill, she softly instructed the maidservant behind her to clean up the things on the table.","\"Young Miss of the Huangfu family, wouldn't it be too much of an honor to have you come over to serve me?\" After Feng Jiu had her fill, she stood up and walked a few steps in the courtyard, her gaze looking towards Huangfu Yunxue.","Huangfu Yunxue was slightly stunned, after looking at her, she converged her eyes and softly said, \"My lady is a honored guest of the Huangfu family, and must not be neglected, Yunxue has come to take care of her. Having my father treat her like this, it can be seen that My lady's status is honored, therefore, Yunxue doesn't feel aggrieved.\"","Feng Jiu smiled, but did not say anything else, but looked towards that Huangfu Xiao who came to the entrance of the courtyard.","\"Lady Xuanyuan.\" Huangfu Xiao bowed towards her, while the corner of his eyes looked towards his daughter who was standing at the side.","\"Lead the way!\" Feng Jiu said, taking a step forward.","\"Good, My lady Xuanyuan this way please.\" He hurriedly said and made a gesture of invitation, leading Feng Jiu towards the other courtyard.","Huangfu Yunxue paused for a moment, then followed suit, unhurriedly following three steps behind them.","Huangfu Family Old Patriarch's courtyard, at this time, had already dismissed the subordinates. Huangfu Xiaoxiao brought Feng Jiu into the courtyard, his pace lurched, turned back to Huangfu Yunxue and said, \"Just wait outside the courtyard, without my permission, no one else is allowed to enter.\"","Hearing this Qing, Huangfu Yunxue was slightly surprised, but did not ask more questions, but gently nodded her head and responded, \"Yes, father.\"","Entering the room inside, led by Huangfu Xiao to the bed in the inner room, only then did she say to Feng Jiu, \"My lady Xuanyuan, this is my father, he has been bedridden due to his health, he was not able to get up to welcome me, please don't be offended.\"","\"No harm done.\" Feng Jiu said, walked up and looked at the old man on that bed who opened his eyes towards her, it was the same old man who had a glance at the broken temple that day.","\"The old man has met Lady Xuanyuan My lady.\" His voice was weak and feeble, while his pale face carried a few moments of excitement from seeing Feng Jiu.","\"Stretch out your hand!\" Feng Jiu said and sat down on the chair beside the bed.","\"Thank you.\" He stretched out his hand and Huangfu Xiao on the side also came forward to help.","Feng Jiu quietly took his pulse, after a while he withdrew his hand, took out the silver needle from the space and said to Huangfu Xiao, \"I will apply the needle to him, you go and wait outside the door of the room, don't let anyone disturb me.\"","Huangfu Xiao glanced at his father on the bed before he nodded and responded, \"Good.\" With that, he then went out of the room and closed the door to the room, before standing outside the room door to guard it."]},{"number":4970,"title":"Chapter 4970: News","paragraphs":["Capítulo 4970: News","In the room, the old man only saw Feng Jiu take out a silver needle and insert it into his acupoints with utmost precision and immediately after, he lost all consiousness.","After seeing the Old Patriarch fall into slumber, Feng Jiu took out the other silver needles and swiftly inserted them into his acupoints. At the same time, the Blue Lotus Qi in her body slowly surged up and imbued into the old man’s body through the silver needles in her hands, repairing the old diseases in his body.","Waiting always feel like time passed very slowly. Huangfu Xiao who was guarding outside the door walked back and forth, finally, the door to the room opened, and seeing Feng Jiu come out, he rushed forward and asked, “Lady Xuanyuan, how is it?”","“Tomorrow, he will be able to get out of bed and walk around, within seven days, he should have recovered to about seventy percent.” Feng Jiu said and walked in, saying, “He’s currently sleeping and won’t wake up until tomorrow.”","“Can I go in to see my father now?” He inquired.","“Yes, just don’t wake him up.” Feng Jiu said and walked outside.","Watching her leave, Huangfu Yunxue glanced at her grandfather’s courtyard, thought about it, but still didn’t enter the courtyard, but followed the lady who left.","The next day, the streets and alleys in Blazing Sun City, and even the restaurants and inns, were then discussing a matter.","“Have you heard? It’s been said that the Old Patriarch of the Huangfu Family would soon be able to get out of bed and walk around.”","“Yes, I’ve heard, that person has been bedridden for around two years, right? I didn’t expect that he would suddenly get better.”","“What do you know, that’s because the Patriarch of the Huangfu family took him around to seek medical treatment, but accidentally got hold of what is called, a thousand year old Wu Ling Ginseng, it is said that this thing is really counted as heavenly treasures amongst all the good things, the Old Patriarch of the Huangfu family’s body can get better, I have heard that it is also because of this.”","“Really? A single root can make a person who has been lying in bed for a year or two and could die at any time get better?”","“This can’t be fake, you don’t know, I’ve heard that this Thousand-Year Wu Ling Ginseng is a good thing that money can’t even buy, it is a miraculous herb, even bringing the dead back to life! There are other unbelievable divine effects, that is, Immortal Cultivators whose souls have been injured and their cores that have been broken can be restored when they take it.”","People in the city in the discussion, things gradually spread, because some people personally saw that the Huangfu family’s Old Patriarch out of bed walking around, so things spread, no one thought it was a fake, after all, the Huangfu family’s that one old disease attack disease into that has long been the parties of the doctor and alchemist asserted that can not be saved.","Now that his body is better, he could also get out of bed to walk around, other than attaining such a heavenly treasure, what other possibilities could there be?","Some families in the city were surprised to hear the news.","In the hall, a middle-aged man in the lower left of the main seat said, ” I heard the people underneath me report early in the morning, saying that the news spread quietly in the city, so I let people go and check it out, and it really is that the one from the Huangfu family is able to get out of bed and walk around, and what kind of treasure is this Thousand-Year Wu Ling Ginseng? Can it really make a dying person come to life?”","“There really is that kind of treasure but letting the news leak out, I’m afraid this Huangfu family can’t keep this treasure.” The middle-aged man in the main seat said, his eyes flickered and said, “Have someone come to the door to check if the Old Patriarch of the Huangfu Family is really recovering and no longer lying in bed, waiting for death?”","Upon hearing this, the people seated underneath looked at each other and nodded, “Yes, this is indeed something that needs to be checked, however, Patriarch, if the Huangfu Family really has that kind of treasure, then ...”"]},{"number":4971,"title":"Chapter 4971: News Spread","paragraphs":["Chapter 4971: News Spread","A middle-aged man who spoke only said half of the words and did not say anything more afterward, instead looking at him in silent inquiry.","“If there really is a treasure like that, then I’m afraid the Huangfu family will only be in trouble.”","The middle-aged man in the main seat said, and as soon as his voice fell, he stood up, “If it’s a small matter, things will simply be taken away, but this obviously isn’t. There is even the risk of extermination of the entire clan! Huangfu Xiao should never have allowed this news to be revealed.” He shook his head and sighed lightly.","At the same time, the various clans in the city were also discussing this matter. Some people did not know the effect of this thousand year old Wu Ling Ginseng, so they deliberately looked it up, and after learning that it had that kind of miraculous effect, they were even more astonished.","“What kind of luck did this Huangfu family have? Even that kind of treasure can be encountered? However, nowadays, Old Patriarch Huangfu’s body hasn’t recovered yet, and he can’t sit on the Huangfu family, depending on Huangfu Xiao alone, if someone wants to take this treasure from him, I’m afraid that his family won’t be able to keep it.”","Saying that, the crowd all shook their heads, with sighs and regret. The same in a city, Huangfu family is not the city’s top family, but also is not that small third-rate family, plus one is, Huangfu Xiao will do people, inside and outside the reputation is very good, and has never fought with people, therefore, many people do not hope that his family because of this thing to get into big trouble.","Some thought of reminding him, while others were prepared to stand by and watch.","Meanwhile, an old man came to a secret room after hearing the news and sending people to inquire and confirm.","” My lord, the city’s Huangfu family got a thousand years of Wu Ling Ginseng, this thing has a very magical effect, it can rejuvenate flesh and bones, as well as the divine effect of repairing the Neidan! That Huangfu Xiao’s father had been bedridden for two years, they have seeked countless doctors, all who were determined that he would not live past this year. However, this morning it was rumored that he has been able to get out of bed and walk around, and I heard that he only ate a Wu Lin Ginseng will have this divine effect. ”","The person who was restored on his knees was wearing a big black cloak, his face was gloomy with a hint of pallor, and his aura was very appalling and eerie.","After hearing the old man’s words, he opened his gaze and came to look at him, his voice was gloomy and eerie: “You should know that this seat does not want any hearings, but rather certainty!”","The old man hurriedly said, “Please rest assured, my lord, my subordinate has already sent people to inquire and confirm, although I didn’t see that thousand year old Wu Ling Ginseng, but I saw that Old Patriarch of the Huangfu family walking in the courtyard, and his mental strength is also good.”","Upon hearing this, that black-robed man’s gloomy gaze narrowed slightly, and his voice was chilling as he said, “Then send someone to seize the thing!”","“Yes!” The old man answered before retreating.","At nightfall, everyone in the Huangfu household was a little nervous as they went back to their rooms early to rest after the sky darkened. This was an order given by the Patriarch, so naturally no one would disobey it.","What’s more, they were aware of the news that was spreading outside, and naturally, they knew that their Huangfu family was only afraid that they would get into trouble because of it, thus, they didn’t dare to wander around outside even after nightfall, lest they invite trouble for no reason.","Not only is the night will rest early, there is a is, this period of time non-essential do not go out, if really have to go out can not, but also have to bring more people to travel in company.","Different from the nervousness of the Huangfu family, Feng Jiu was lying on the roof of the Huangfu family after nightfall, ready to wait for a rabbit.","Because she believed that from this night onwards, the Huangfu family’s night would be very lively ..."]},{"number":4972,"title":"Chapter 4972: Silently","paragraphs":["As Feng Jiu expected, after the sky darkened, one after another, there were people who wanted to sneak into Huangfu's house by taking advantage of the veil of the night, only, after those people sneaked into Huangfu's house, but one by one, they all had no return.","Those who were outside the Huangfu's manor monitoring were secretly surprised. Because those who went in did not come out, not only that, there was not even a single sound of any fighting, those who had entered had mysteriously disappeared.","As the night deepened, Huangfu Yunxue's eyes could not help but twitch as she stood at the front yard, not knowing what to think as she saw the number of unconcious people gradually pile up. From the initial shock to the present numbness, not a trace of surprise was on her face.","She had been called here by Lady Xuanyuan, saying that she needed her help to pack up some things, but she didn't expect to see the cultivators who sneaked in during the night, only, none of these people were able to cross the front yard, one by one, they all inexplicably fell down from the mid-air, either dead or injured, and none of them were awake anyway.","Feng Jiu stretched as she glanced at Huangfu Yunxue who was standing below, her voice was gentle and she asked casually, \"What are you standing there for? Kill all ones alive with a blade, just slit their throats cleanly and then collect all the valuable things on them.\"","Her words made her come to her senses and look at her, a trace of hesitation crossed her eyes as she said, \"My lady, do we really have to kill them all?!\" She was somewhat unable to lay her hands on them.","Feng Jiu's lips curled up as she said very matter-of-factly, \"Kill them, you have to know, if I am not here, the ones who are killed tonight will be your Huangfu family, these sneaky thieves are not people with a soft heart.\"","Maybe because of her words, or maybe because of something else, Huangfu Yunxue held the dagger and stepped forward, gritting her teeth, like a devil reaping the lives of those people ...","Feng Jiu sat on the roof and watched indifferently, the corner of her lips slightly hooked up. This Huangfu Yunxue has followed her for two days now, she was indeed an innocent and clear minded girl, only, such a person, often also can not live for a long time.","Seeing as she had done her best to serve her for the past two days, she naturally didn't mind giving her a push.","She believed that after tonight, she would become different.","Huangfu Yunxue didn't know when she stopped, she only knew that the warm blood splattered all over her, some even splashed her face, her hand was stained with that fishy red blood. As her whole person sat in front of that pile of corpses in a daze, no one knew what she was thinking about.","When dawn was about to break, she had an epiphany. Sitting there with her legs crossed, the spirit energy breath in her body churned, and at this moment, even though her eyes were closed, she could still feel an unprecedented clarity.","The path her feet were walking on, the path she was going to take in the future, as well as her previous confusion, all of them seemed to have been unveiled at this moment, and it was as if there was a voice in her mind that was asking her something ...","Feng Jiu glanced at her, waved his hand and laid a boundary for her, then went back to the courtyard by himself to rest.","The sun rose in the east, and another new day arrived, however, on this day, the various forces in the city were as if they had exploded, they were all somewhat unable to sit still.","There was no other reason, simply because, the people they had sent out did not return for the night, and there was not the slightest movement, it was as if they had disappeared into thin air.","In a hidden place, the old man with a somewhat ugly face hurriedly came to that secret room, and knelt down towards the person who was practicing on his knees."]},{"number":4973,"title":"Chapter 4973: Personally","paragraphs":["Capítulo 4973: Personally","“Lord.”","The black-robed man with his eyes closed opened his eyes, his gloomy gaze looking at the old man kneeling in front of him, a color of coldness crossing his eyes.","“Things didn’t work out?” He inquired, his voice cold and hostile.","“My Lord forgive me.”","He kowtowed his head against the ground before raising his head to look at him, his face grave as he said, “Lord, the ones sent out were all top-notch experts, it’s just that I didn’t expect that not a single person came back alive.”","“Hmm? Isn’t the Huangfu family only occupied by Huangfu Xiao? Other than him, is there any other strong person?” He inquired, the corners of his mouth drooping slightly, a look of displeasure on his face.","“There are no other strong people in the Huangfu family besides Huangfu Xiao, even if there are, it’s just those few clan elders of the Huangfu Family, but the people we sent out naturally have that strength to deal with those people, but not even one returned. It can be seen that there must be a strong expert we don’t know of, in there.”","The old man said, looked at him, said: “Last night in addition to our people, there were another seven or eight groups of people who had also sneaked into the Huangfu family, but all of them have the same result – not a single person returned. Lately, we lost a lot of strong exponents, in addition to last night that we’ve sent out, what should we do?”","Perhaps it was the thought of being exterminated, the black-robed man’s aura chilled as he took in a deep breath.","“Tonight, you go personally with this seat, this seat would like to see what kind of person is sitting in the Huangfu family!” If he could get his hands on that thousand year old Wu Ling Ginseng, his physical condition would recover. His damaged divine soul would also recover, and his strength would be restored to its peak, so no matter who was that person? He had to personally go on a journey to get back his glory!","“Yes!” Hearing that he was going to personally go, the old man’s heart sighed in relief, feeling that if he were to personally go, he should be able to get that thing.","“Have we still no news on that person?” The black-robed man asked again, impatient.","The old man lowered his head and said, “Not yet, mainly because no one saw it, and I don’t know if that person is a man or a woman, we can only ascertain that the cultivator is not from the city, so I haven’t been able to find out even now.”","“Go search! Make sure to find out the person and tear that person into pieces!” He spoke in a gloomy voice.","“Yes!” The old man responded, before bowing and retreating.","At the Huangfu Manor, Huangfu Xiao’s always serious face could not hide his excitement and joy as he came to his father’s courtyard, “Father, Yunxue has had an enlightenment!”","Hearing these words, Huangfu’s old master was slightly stunned, his gaze slightly widened, with surprise and dismay in his eyes, “Enlightenment? Yunxue?”","“Yes, last night because of My Lady Xuanyuan’s words, early to the following people are not allowed to go out, hear the movement is also not allowed to go out of the room door, I was over to see this morning, that the front yard piled up corpses are as high as a small mountain, and one by one, all of them are considerably strong.”","Speaking of this, Huangfu Xiao let out a deep breath and said, “When I went, Lady Xuanyuan had already returned to the courtyard to rest, and only Yunxue, all splattered with blood, was sitting in front of that pile of corpses to have an enlightenment, and there was a boundary surrounding her and no one could approach, it should have been laid down by Lady Xuanyuan.”","At these words, the old man took a breath and said, “Don’t let anyone go over there in the front yard, tell the people below to keep their mouths shut, and keep an eye on Yunxue.”"]},{"number":4974,"title":"Chapter 4974: Wait","paragraphs":["Capítulo 4974: Wait","“Yes, I know, I thought that she had an enlightenment this time, and it is estimated that she will advanceme in a short while. Moreover, being able to enter into an epiphany is a good thing that can be encountered and not sought for cultivators, and it will be extremely beneficial to her cultivation path in the future.”","Huangfu Xiao said, a smile came on his face and said, “Father, it’s also fortunate that you said to let Yunxue go over to serve Lady Xuanyuan, I didn’t expect that, just for a day or two, she would have such an opportunity.”","“That one is a supreme power, as long as she is willing, she can naturally benefit people in many ways.” The old man said, sighing with emotion, “To have met her, it’s also the good fortune of our Huangfu family’s ancestors! This is truly a heavenly blessing.”","“It’s also fortunate that she is the one who guarded for us, otherwise those people last night alone, I’m only afraid that ...” Thinking of that pile of corpses in that front yard, his heart was also a little heavy.","He didn’t expect that a thousand year old Wu Ling Ginseng would be able to attract so many strong people, in this world, strong people really have an incomparable fervor and madness for those rare geniuses and treasures.","“I’m only afraid that the people coming tonight will be even more powerful, you should make preparations early today.” The old man confided.","“Alright, I’ll go make arrangements now.” He said and made a bow before heading out.","In the evening, when Feng Jiu went out of her room, she saw Huangfu Yunxue, who had already changed her dress, already waiting in the courtyard, and when she saw her come out, she went forward and performed a grand bow towards her.","“Yunxue thanks My Lady for her great kindness.” She gratefully bowed towards her, her heart filled with gratitude.","Feng Jiu waved her hand indifferently, “It’s your own opportunity, it has nothing to do with me.” She walked to the table and sat down.","Huangfu Yunxue came forward and scooped a bowl of soup for her, saying, “If it wasn’t for My Lady, Yunxue wouldn’t have had this epiphany, My lady’s great kindness, Yunxue name is remembered in my heart.”","Feng Jiu took a sip of the soup and didn’t say anything, she just picked up her chopsticks to clip some dishes and ate her meal. After the meal, she put down her chopsticks and wiped the corners of her mouth, confiding, “Tonight you don’t have to follow, go back to your room early and don’t go out, and don’t come out when you hear the commotion.”","Hearing this, Huangfu Yunxue thought of last night’s scene, her heart fluttered, she did not ask more questions, but respectfully answered, “Yes.”","Feng Jiu went outside and first went to Old Patriarch Huangfu’s courtyard to apply another needle for him, when she came out after the needle was applied, the sky was already dark.","She looked at the darkening sky, her gaze narrowed, and instead of returning to the courtyard, she walked towards the front courtyard.","The corpses in the front yard had already been cleaned up long ago, even the space gas couldn’t find a trace of last night’s bloody odor, as if last night’s pile of corpses was just an illusion.","Feng Jiu waved her hand and laid down a boundary, isolating the Huangfu family’s backyard from the front yard. She didn’t go to the roof to wait, but instead, with her hand on her back, she found a place to sit in the front yard.","As the night fell. Seven or eight black-robed cultivators quietly sneaked in, and after they took a wary look around, they quietly landed in the courtyard of the front yard.","Feng Jiu was sitting in a corner of the front yard, due to the convergence of her aura, coupled with deliberate concealment, the seven or eight people sneaked in and did not discover her existence in the corner, because, her figure was blocked by a column, and due to the darkness of the night, there were no lights lit in the front yard, so no one noticed.","A black robed men at the head of the group lowered his voice and said, “Be careful, this Huangfu family should have a strong person in there, our target is that thousand year old Wu Ling Ginseng, get it and evacuate immediately!”"]},{"number":4975,"title":"Chapter 4975: Silence","paragraphs":["At this time, they did not know that Feng Jiu was quietly sizing up those seven or eight people. Seeing that these few people were a level stronger and a bit more cautious than the people who came last night, just that, it was still not the one she was waiting for.","\"There seems to be a boundary in here.\" A person said, and his footsteps that were walking forward slightly paused.","\"There is a boundary.\" Feng Jiu's voice came out coldly at this time, startling those people.","\"Who's there!\"","They shouted aloud, looking warily around. However, no matter how much they tried, they could not distinguish from which direction that voice came from, the surrounding was pitch black, but for them who possessed a strong cultivation, their sight, even if it was not as clear as in the daytime, should not be unable to see the person hiding, but right now, they indeed only heard the voice and did not see the person hiding in the dark.","Feng Jiu walked out from the shadows, her eyes skimmed over the bodies of several people, then she asked, \"Who are you people?\"","The vigilant gaze of the one in the lead landed on the person who walked out, somewhat surprised that it was a woman, only, when he wanted to take a look at the cultivation of this woman, the divine sense that was released violently shrank back as if it had encountered something powerful and terrifying, and at the same time, even he took a step back.","\"Your honor is the powerful one who is assisting the Huangfu Family?\"","The black robed men at the head said, his entire body tensing up as he sensed that invisible aura of danger, his entire body taking a stance of being ready to fight and being able to withdraw at any time.","I don't know for what reason, Feng Jiu didn't take out the lives of these people like last night, but after staring at them, she said, \"For the sake of your cultivation, I won't kill you.\"","As soon as her voice fell, she moved her hand and several silver needles instantly attacked out. Almost at the same time that her silver needles struck out, several people instinctively reacted, a powerful spirit energy aura instantly formed a defense shield around their bodies.","However, they did not expect that just as they were forming a defense shield with their Spirit Energy and were about to let out a sigh of relief, they saw that the thin silver needles easily broke through their defense shield with a swoosh and shot into their body's acupoints.","When they were shocked and dismayed, they couldn't even cry out in shock, the whole person felt a burst of weakness, as if all the spirit energy and breath had disappeared in an instant, and their legs fell down weakly due to the soreness and weakness, in this instant, their hearts sank violently.","Feng Jiu's sleeve flicked, a gust of wind rolled over, sending several people to the corner.","They tried to make a sound, but, with their mouths open, they couldn't make a sound at all, and their bodies couldn't move only to fall helplessly to the ground.","\"After losing a lot of people last night, you still dare to come tonight, you guys are quite courageous.\" Feng Jiu glanced at them faintly, looking at them when they tried to struggle to get up, she raised one hand and stretched out her index finger to gently press it against her lips, making a silencing gesture.","\"Don't make any noise, don't spoil my business, otherwise, I don't mind killing the few of you.\"","Although her voice was gentle, however, in the ears of a few people, it was like a clap of thunder as a wave of shock washed over them, a chill emanating from the soles of their feet, as fear shot straight into their hearts, they all could not help but shudder.","Inexplicably, they believe that this unknown woman, what she said is true! She was really going to kill them!"]},{"number":4976,"title":"Chapter 4976: Unlucky Ones","paragraphs":["Capítulo 4976: Unlucky Ones","With this thought, their bodies froze, not daring to move a single bit. Only cold sweat was breaking out.","At this moment, no one thought that with their cultivation and strength, people who had experienced countless storms would be frightened by such a woman.","And on the contrary, no one dared to challenge her bottom line, and even more so, they did not dare to try to make a bit of a commotion to see if she would really do as she said.","As they looked at her, they gulped uncontrollably, trying to suppress the fear in their hearts.","To think that they, the superiors who had been in power for a long time, would actually one day not even have the courage to try ...","Feng Jiu glanced at them lightly before turning away and walking back to sit at the corner, waiting for the next batch of unlucky cultivators to come to her door.","These people at least was also considered to be the strong in her territory, last night she had already wiped out a batch. If they weren’t seeking deaths and weren’t too much, she naturally would also leave them their life, after all, being able to cultivate to such a point was also considered rare.","Just, I don’t know how many more people will come to try this night?","After about half a column of incense, there are a few more people quietly came, they stood on the wall did not go down, but vigilantly looking towards the surrounding, one of them said, “I heard that there are strong people in here, just don’t know who is it?”","“Right now, no one has been detected here either.” Another person said, and as soon as his voice fell, he suddenly eeped, “There seems to be a few auras in that corner over there, just very weak.”","Hearing the words of the few people on that wall, those few people who were said to be very weak were currently staring at the few people on the wall with a pair of eyes. Secretly, they bit their teeth and cursed: very weak? You guys come down and try!","“It seems to say that a few silhouettes came in first, it can’t be those Taoist Priests who came in earlier, right?” Another person said, a little surprised, divine sense swept in that direction, but then said strangely, “But listening to the people staring outside, the seven or eight people who came in earlier were not weak? Maybe it isn’t them?”","At this time, an old man’s tone was slightly condensed and said, “Perhaps, it’s those few people who are good, only, they are already dying.”","Hearing these words, the few people in that corner couldn’t help but glance towards the corner on the other side. Although they didn’t suffer any injuries to become moribund, they were now lying here weakly, and it looked like they weren’t far from being moribund, and the one who caused all of this was that unknown woman at that corner.","“Then we are into? Or pass?” One of the men on the wall spoke.","The surroundings were slightly quiet for a moment, no one opened their mouths, seemingly pondering, and in the end, it was the old man who said, “It’s long been known that the Huangfu family has a strong person in there, hasn’t it? Since we have come, how would there be a reason to retreat? What’s more, our intention is only to press that thousand year old Wu Ling Ginseng, as for the Huangfu Family’s people, try not to hurt them if you can.”","“Good, then go down!” The other person also agreed, and as soon as his voice fell, he swept towards the courtyard below.","Seeing this, several other people also followed and leapt down. And the seven or eight black robed men who saw them leaping down from the corner all revealed inexplicable weird smiles at this moment.","Coming down was good! If they came down, they would have company! It’s just that I don’t know, which of these old guys are the unlucky ones again?","Just thinking, see that just landed a few people with them earlier the same, almost before seeing people, one by one plopped on the ground ..."]},{"number":4977,"title":"Chapter 4977: Hooked","paragraphs":["Capítulo 4977: Hooked","A few people at the corner grunted, when they saw a gust of wind swirling towards the few people above them and seeing them falling towards them, they stared wide-eyed, wanting to retreat, but unable to move, and could only watch as the few of them fell towards them, crushing down towards them.","The few people who were at the bottom could only helplessly utter out a muffled grunt as their body had to withstand the heavy impact falling onto them.","Those who fell on top froze for a moment, stunned by the human cushion underneath them while a sense of dread and horror engulfed their hearts. They had only just come in, how did they also fall? In the end, who could have done this? How could it be so silent?","Feng Jiu did not come out, she was still waiting, other than the weak breath at that corner, there was no one else.","After some time, no one came in and she waited until midnight, thinking that that person would not come tonight when she saw two figures jump down from the wall.","Seeing those two figures, Feng Jiu’s gaze narrowed, that person’s wisp of divine soul was destroyed by her, therefore, even if that person did not reveal his face, she could still tell by the aura of the divine soul on that person’s body.","Obviously, one of them was the one she had been waiting for.","“Lord, there seems to be someone over there.”","The old man following beside her said, his gaze landing at a corner in the courtyard. It was felt that there were quite a few people there, could it be, that they were ambushing there?","That black-robed man didn’t open his mouth, but instead narrowed a pair of chilly eyes as he scanned the courtyard, finally determining that other than those scents at that corner, there were no other scents present.","However, to be able to make people from all forces plant their heels here, this Huangfu Family would definitely not be as simple as it appeared to be!","“Your Excellency’s ability to condense and conceal Qi is well practiced.” He stood at the head of the wall and spoke with a negative hand, his grim voice containing a spirit energy aura penetrating the surroundings at this moment, echoing between the air.","Speaking voice, his eyes were still paying attention to the surrounding, compared to others, he was more vigilant even though he possessed uncommon strength.","Listening to those words, Feng Jiu laughed lightly, sounding gentle yet there was a hint of coldness in it.","“A woman?”","Hearing that voice was actually a woman’s voice, that black-robed man’s eyebrows frowned slightly, and his expression sank. Almost instantly, countless thoughts crossed his mind, and also in that instant he guessed what this woman meant from that laughter.","“It is you! The woman who destroyed a strand of this seat’s divine soul!”","His aura around him turned cold, a powerful aura was released from his body, covering towards the entire Huangfu Family, his voice said eerily, “I guess the person who extinguished several of this seat’s basis points is also you! This Huangfu Family, there is no such thing as a thousand year old Wu Ling Ginseng, but rather, it was your trick to lure this seat here!”","With these words, those people piled up in that corner were shocked. It’s not true, is it? There was no Thousand Year Wu Ling Ginseng? Then they were tricked into coming here? They were seeking such suffering all for naught?","So, that person is the person that she wants to lure out?","At this time, Feng Jiu slowly walked out with her lips slightly hooked. However, the smile did not reach her eyes and not a sliver of her aura could be sensed. Seeing this, it made the black-robed man vigilant."]},{"number":4978,"title":"Chapter 4978: Recognise","paragraphs":["\"Specter Lord of the Specter Palace, with your supreme-level cultivation, , if you hadn't touched my inverse scales, perhaps, after a few decades or a few hundred years you might still be able to ascend to become a Great Emperor level powerhouse, it's just a pity that you have made an unforgivable mistake.\"","A gentle voice with a hint of coldness came out from Feng Jiu's mouth, clearly echoing between the colors of the night.","And, because of the boundary, other than the people in this front yard, those in the backyard of the Huangfu family did not know what was being said here, and couldn't hear a single thing.","The figures in the corner instinctively held their breath. Cold sweat seeped down their backs as they felt a chill creep up their spines, as fear permeated through their hearts. They wished they had never come to the Huangfu Manor at all! Then they would never have witnessed this scene, never heard these words.","Supreme level! Yet that woman had mentioned it in such a casual manner, suggested that she held no regard for such a power at all.","However, they knew that for such powerful exponents, with a casual stomp of his foot, Blazing Sun City would collapse into ruins, not to mention that they were still lying in the corner.","If these two sides truly clashed, wouldn't they be caught in the crossfire? A single misstep could mean death right here.","That woman could speak so boldly, clearly indicating her strength surpassed his opponent's. Such a woman of this caliber was truly rare anywhere. Yet, no matter how much they speculated, they couldn't fathom who this person truly was.","The black-robed man listened to the voice with a murderous aura, his eyes moved slightly, staring at the azure woman below, saying, \"Is it that little girl?\"","He had only crossed paths with this woman once before, when he was preparing to capture the little girl with the innate spirit-gathering body to refine her into a medicinal pill. At that moment, he had recognized the whip and identified the girl named Yun Qi as the disciple of the Azure Emperor.","He had thought he could quietly dispose of her. Even if the Azure Emperor discovered it later, by then he might have already ascended successfully. Yet unexpectedly, this woman who had suddenly appeared had ruined his plans.","\"You ruined this Lord's plans. I hadn't even sought retribution from you yet, but now you've come to me of your own accord. Since that is the case, this Lord shall have a proper exchange with you!\"","He believed that last time, only a fragment of his divine soul had been present, which was why it had been destroyed. Now, facing her was his true form. He refused to believe that with his power and cultivation, he could still be defeated by such a woman!","The moment the words left his mouth, his hand formed a claw and lunged downward at Feng Jiu. The overwhelming pressure and aura emanating from his body formed a powerful, crushing force.","Only, he was not facing anyone else, but Feng Jiu who was the Noble Empress Phoenix Sovereign! From the moment he struck out at Yue'er, he was doomed!","The black-robed man only felt that in that instant, a pressure of strength that was even stronger than him came towards him, causing his entire body to stiffen violently, and his hand also stopped in mid-air at that moment.","\"Arghhhhh!\"","In that moment of dismay, a ball of flames came flying head-on to surround him with a whirring sound, the fierce flames and extremely high temperatures burned him to the point that he couldn't help but scream miserably, not caring about attacking the woman, but quickly wanting to extinguish the flames on his body.","\"This is the Innate Heavenly Flame? No!\""]},{"number":4979,"title":"Chapter 4979: Saw That","paragraphs":["Chapter 4979: Saw That","He screamed in terror, his voice shrill and filled with dread. Flames raged across his body, refusing to be extinguished no matter how fiercely he beat at them. And these were not mere Innate Heavenly Flames—they were Primordial Divine Flames! Even as a mighty Supreme Being, he found himself unable to escape this crisis under the dual assault of the opponent’s overwhelming pressure and the relentless flames!","“Arghhhhhhhhhh! Who... who are you?! Who are you?!”","He screamed as his body tumbled to the ground, yet the flames clung to him like a living entity, burning relentlessly. The acrid scent of scorched flesh mingled with the night breeze, spreading through the air.","“What good would it do a dying man to know?” Feng Jiu remarked indifferently, watching the black-robed man writhing and screaming on the ground, reduced to a burning husk. Her hand moved, gripping the Blue Edge as a faint azure glow surged from its blade.","“No one I intend to kill has ever escaped!”","As her cold voice fell, her sword-wielding hand struck downward in an instant, carrying a fierce sword qi. The slash cut through the air like a mountain river, sharp and terrifying!","“Whoosh!”","“Arghhh!”","As the fierce sword qi erupted, a shrill, wretched scream filled with unwillingness pierced the air. Yet, the barrier surrounding the courtyard contained the sound, preventing it from escaping.","The only witnesses to this scene, their faces drained of color and hearts pounding in terror, were the figures piled up in the corner...","Blood spattered. The body split cleanly in two, the halves scattering across the ground. Flames consumed it, burning until not even a speck of ash remained, all scattered into the night air by the wind.","The elderly man who had arrived with the cloaked figure was utterly petrified by the spectacle. He dared not even entertain thoughts of escape. The overwhelming pressure was too intimidating, the woman’s power too terrifying. His legs gave way beneath him, and he collapsed trembling against the wall.","Cold sweat beaded on his forehead, his face as pale as paper. Dazed by sheer terror, his eyes lost their usual sparkle, sitting there as if his soul had been stolen.","Feng Jiu shot him a glance. With a flick of her Blue Edge, a flash of cold steel whistled through the air, sealing his throat in an instant!","Even in death, the old man’s eyes remained wide open, his face frozen in terror as he stared straight ahead, unable to utter even a scream.","Those in the corner desperately tried to make themselves invisible. What kind of being was the Specter Lord of the Specter Palace? Not only were the people of Blazing Sun City aware of his name, but even nearby powerful figures had heard of his extraordinary strength. Now, they had witnessed him crushed and killed without any chance to fight back by this azure-robed woman. How could they not be terrified?","After disposing of those two, Feng Jiu felt somewhat satisfied. After all, eliminating the man who sought to turn her daughter into a medicinal pill had settled an unfinished matter.","At least, she no longer had to worry about her child being targeted again when she wasn’t there to protect her.","Her fingers lightly traced the blade of the Blue Edge Sword before she swiftly sheathed it. She turned to face the figures huddled in the corner. With a flick of her wrist, a surge of spirit energy rippled through the air. The next moment, muffled groans escaped their lips.","Feng Jiu stood in the courtyard, her clear gaze fixed on the corner. Her voice was unhurried, tinged with a hint of languid indifference: “You all saw that, didn’t you?”"]},{"number":4980,"title":"Chapter 4980: Thoughts","paragraphs":["Capítulo 4980: Thoughts","Those who had been lying face down on the ground, piled atop one another, all felt the spirit energy within them return. Their bodies regained movement, and the flow of qi within them circulated normally once more.","Relief washed over them. They thought, since she hadn’t killed them, surely she wouldn’t kill them now?","Without hesitation, they scrambled to their feet and stepped forward. Though puzzled by her question, they exchanged glances and answered in unison, “To answer your question, we all witnessed it.”","Not only had they witnessed it, but they had seen it clearly. They believed that no matter how many years passed, they would never forget the events of this night.","“Oh? Then tell me, what exactly happened tonight?” Feng Jiu curved her lips slightly, fixing her gaze on one of the elders.","The elder, meeting Feng Jiu’s stare, felt a chill run down his spine. He cautiously stepped forward, clasped his hands in a respectful bow, then hesitated before speaking: ” The news of the thousand-year-old Wu Ling Ginseng circulating in the Huangfu family was a ruse, primarily to lure the Specter Palace Specter Lord into a trap. Now that the matter is concluded, what would you require of us? Any command you give, we dare not refuse.","At that moment, her formidable aura surged forth. Had they not witnessed her power earlier, none would have imagined that this very woman had slain the Specter Palace’s Specter Lord—leaving not even a corpse behind. Likely, even the soul had been consumed by the heavenly fire, vanishing into the void.","“Very well.”","Feng Jiu spoke as she strolled leisurely through the courtyard. “I had Huangfu Xiao spread the rumor to lure that person here. Now that he’s dead and the matter settled, there’s nothing more to it. However, you witnessed tonight’s events and know the truth. But outsiders remain unaware. They believe the Huangfu family possesses that thousand-year-old Wu Ling Ginseng, and as long as that rumor persists, the Huangfu family will never have a day of peace.”","Hearing this, the others’ hearts stirred. They immediately replied, “Rest assured, Your Excellency. We will spread the word that the Huangfu family possesses no thousand-year-old Wu Ling Ginseng.”","Having lived for hundreds of years, they instantly grasped her meaning upon hearing her words. They agreed with a silent sigh of relief, marveling at the Huangfu family’s extraordinary fortune in befriending such a formidable powerhouse.","The only question was: did the Huangfu family know her true identity?","No—even if others remained unaware, the Huangfu family surely knew. Otherwise, they would never have risked spreading rumors about the thousand-year-old Wu Ling Ginseng, inviting disaster upon themselves.","For a moment, thoughts stirred among them. It seemed the Huangfu family was worth cultivating a relationship with!","Feng Jiu glanced at them and said indifferently, “Beyond that, go and root out every last remnant of the Specter Palace’s scattered forces! I want this faction wiped from existence!”","Hearing this, they didn’t hesitate, immediately responding, “Yes!”","Several Specter Palace strongholds had been destroyed, many powerful members slain, and tonight their Specter Lord had also perished here. Only the lower-ranking members remained. With their strength, cultivation, and influence, wiping out this faction would be quite easy.","“Go,” Feng Jiu signaled, dismissing them.","Hearing they could depart, the group felt a surge of relief. They bowed in unison, then swiftly gathered their energy and leapt away from the Huangfu residence."]},{"number":4981,"title":"Chapter 4981: All Settled","paragraphs":["After they departed, Feng Jiu cast a faint glance around the courtyard. With a wave of her hand, she removed the protective barrier surrounding the residence and returned to the courtyard to rest.","For reasons unknown, no one infiltrated the Huangfu residence that night.","The next morning, Huangfu Xiao arrived at the front courtyard with several trusted aides before the others had even left their rooms. Noticing that the barrier had been removed and finding only a corpse and some bloodstains on the ground, he felt a flicker of unease. He immediately ordered his men to begin cleaning up.","\"Send someone out to gather intelligence on the outside. Use unfamiliar faces for the reconnaissance. Report back immediately with any news.\" Huangfu Xiao whispered to one of his men.","\"Yes, Master.\" The man responded before withdrawing to make arrangements.","Huangfu Xiao headed toward the rear courtyard, intending to visit Lady Xuanyuan to inquire about the previous night. Yet halfway there, he halted and instead turned toward his daughter's quarters.","Since she still needed to treat Old Master Huangfu again today, Feng Jiu hadn't stayed up too late. When she finished washing up and stepped out of her room, Huangfu Yunxue was already bustling about.","After breakfast, the Old Patriarch Huangfu and Huangfu Xiao arrived at the courtyard. Spotting the woman seated there, they approached.","\"Grandfather, Father,\" Huangfu Yunxue greeted them, stepping forward to offer a curtsy.","\"Yunxue, you may withdraw,\" Huangfu Xiao instructed, motioning for her to leave.","Huángfu Yunxue glanced at Feng Jiu, who was seated there drinking tea, before responding, \"Yes.\"","\"Lady Xuanyuan,\" the two bowed to her.","\"Have a seat,\" Feng Jiu invited.","The two men approached and sat down. After a moment, the Old Patriarch spoke: \"Seeing that my health has improved considerably, I came to Lady Xuanyuan for treatment today. I wonder if Lady Xuanyuan received the visitor she was expecting last night?\"","Truthfully, upon seeing the barrier lifted, he had already begun to suspect something. Asking her directly was merely to hear it from her own lips.","\"The Specter Lord of the Specter Palace is dead. That faction should vanish soon enough.\" Feng Jiu toyed with her teacup as she looked at him. \"Your condition requires only one more treatment today. After that, proper recuperation will see you fully restored. With matters settled, I shall depart today.\"","Hearing this, both of them paused slightly. Huangfu Xiao said, \"Lady Xuanyuan, won't you stay a few more days? It's rare for you to visit Blazing Sun City. You probably haven't seen much of it yet. Now that matters are settled, why not stay a few more days? I'll have Yunxue accompany you to explore the city?\"","\"It's unnecessary. I have matters to attend to,\" she replied, shaking her head.","Hearing she had other commitments, they felt it inappropriate to insist further and relented.","In the courtyard, Feng Jiu administered another treatment. After a while, withdrawing her hands, she said, \"After I depart, you needn't worry. No one will trouble your Huangfu family. The matter should be resolved today.\"","Huangfu Xiao rose to his feet and bowed deeply to her. \"Thank you, Lady Xuanyuan.\"","The two did not linger long in her courtyard. After a brief stay, they departed. Huangfu Yunxue, who had been waiting outside, entered after they left. Watching the lady stroll leisurely through the garden, she hesitated before asking, \"Are you leaving, My lady?\"","Outside earlier, she had overheard their conversation—she was leaving today.","\"Mhm.\" Feng Jiu responded softly, pausing beside the flowers and plants at the corner of the courtyard."]},{"number":4982,"title":"Chapter 4982: Travel","paragraphs":["Chapter 4982: Travel","Huangfu Yunxue listened to her soft voice and couldn’t help asking, “After My lady leaves, will she ever come back? Yunxue, will I ever see My lady again?”","Feng Jiu smiled, casually plucking a flower to play with in her hand. Turning to face the strikingly beautiful young girl, she said with a smile, “Whether she’ll return, I cannot say. But you and I share a certain karmic connection. Perhaps we shall meet again someday.”","She walked slowly forward, pinning the flower she’d been holding to Yunxue’s hair. Seeing the delicate blossom nestled in the simple-dressed girl’s hair, she instantly looked even more radiant and captivating.","She smiled. “If we should meet again in the future, I shall grant you an opportunity.”","Huangfu Yunxue paused, her hand gently brushing the blossom. She looked at My lady before her—her expression serene, yet a faint smile playing at her lips—and her own lips parted, though no words came.","“I’ll be going now. Just inform your father and the others later,” Feng Jiu said softly, her steps already carrying her toward the exit.","Seeing this, Huangfu Yunxue hurried after her. “Yunxue will see you out, My lady.” She walked alongside her, accompanying her all the way to the gates of the Huangfu residence. Only when the woman’s figure vanished from sight did she turn toward the main courtyard.","She wanted to know—who exactly was this My lady?","In the main courtyard, upon seeing Yunxue enter, the Old Patriarch and Huangfu Xiao exchanged glances and asked in unison, “Did My lady Xuanyuan have any instructions?”","“No,” Yunxue shook her head and stepped forward. “Grandfather, Father, Lady Xuanyuan has left.”","“Left...” The Old Patriarch murmured softly, his voice tinged with a hint of sigh.","Huangfu Xiao remained silent. She had said she would leave today, but he hadn’t expected it to happen so quickly. Recalling the news he’d received earlier from the servants below, his heart was filled with a thousand emotions.","Everything had unfolded exactly as she had foreseen. All was calm once more, as if the Huangfu family had never drawn the attention of powerful figures due to that thousand-year-old Wu Ling Ginseng.","She had departed after completing her task, leaving behind a shock they would never forget.","“Grandfather, Father.” Huangfu Yunxue knelt, her gaze fixed on them.","“What are you doing?” Huangfu Xiao inquired.","“Please tell Yunxue, Grandfather and Father, who exactly is this Lady Xuanyuan?” She looked at them and said, “Because of her, Yunxue has gained sudden enlightenment. To have received such a blessing without knowing the identity of the benefactor... my heart cannot rest easy.”","Hearing this, the old patriarch sighed softly and said, “What good would knowing do?” Such a supreme and exalted benefactor—our Huangfu family is fortunate merely to have laid eyes upon her.”","“Please tell Yunxue, Grandfather.” She bowed her head to him.","The old man looked at her, paused to consider, then said, “She is the Phoenix Sovereign.” He added, “You alone must know this. Do not speak of it to others.”","Huangfu Yunxue’s heart jolted. She had surmised that My lady’s status must be exceedingly noble, but never imagined it would be such a supremely exalted being...","Empress Phoenix Sovereign!","Even though she rarely left Blazing Sun City, she had heard many tales about this Empress Phoenix Sovereign. Never did she expect to have the fortune of serving by her side for these past few days.","Recalling the Empress’s words, a thought surfaced in her mind. Without hesitation, she spoke: “Grandfather, Father, I wish to travel.”","“Why do you wish to travel?” Huangfu Xiao asked, his brow slightly furrowed."]},{"number":4983,"title":"Chapter 4983: Idea","paragraphs":["Chapter 4983: Idea","So she relayed Lady Xuanyuan’s words to the two of them, saying, “Yunxue thinks that if I stay at home forever, the chance of meeting Lady Xuanyuan again in this lifetime is practically zero. It would be better to go out and travel. First, it broadens my horizons; second, I can witness the myriad aspects of the world; and third, who knows—perhaps one day I’ll encounter Lady Xuanyuan out there.”","At this point, she smiled and added, “It’s not that Yunxue is fixated on Lady Xuanyuan’s promise of a future opportunity. Rather, when I saw her stride away so carefree and unrestrained, I couldn’t help but feel a pang of envy.”","She looked at the two of them and said, ” Yunxue doesn’t wish to remain forever within the family’s protection, confined to this small world for her entire life.”","With that, she prostrated herself before them, striking three loud knocks with her forehead: “I implore Grandfather and Father to grant me this wish.”","Hearing this, the old master and Huangfu Xiao fell silent. Neither spoke, merely watching Huangfu Yunxue kneeling before them, her forehead striking the ground in supplication.","After a long pause, Huangfu Xiao spoke in a measured tone, “You’ve never traveled far, nor do you understand the dangers of the world. Moreover, your current strength is insufficient for venturing out. If you truly left, you would likely perish within three months.”","“Yunxue isn’t afraid, Father. Yunxue isn’t afraid of death.” She looked at him, her gaze unwavering.","Seeing her such determination, Huangfu Xiao was at a loss for words. Just as he was about to rebuke her, his father spoke up beside him.","“Since you wish to go, I shall grant your request! However, you have only recently attained enlightenment. Now is not the time to leave. You must wait until you successfully break through to the next stage.”","“Agreed!” Huangfu Yunxue responded, a smile lighting up her face.","With her current state of mind and the benefits gained from her enlightenment, she could achieve advancement within three months.","“Patriarch, a guest has arrived at the gates!” The steward hurried in to report, his expression brimming with excitement.","Noticing the steward’s expression, the Old Patriarch gestured. “Go see who it is.”","“Yes, sir.” Huangfu Xiao responded before heading toward the front courtyard.","“Grandfather, I’ll return to seclude myself for cultivation now.” Huangfu Yunxue said, then followed him out.","Meanwhile, after leaving the Huangfu residence, Feng Jiu wandered through the city streets. She sat for a while in an inn, confirming that the entire Specter Palace faction had vanished overnight. Only then did she depart from Blazing Sun City, heading toward the Song family’s location...","At the Song residence, Song Mi’er and her brothers had been taking Hao’er and the others sightseeing around the city these past few days. After exploring all the city’s attractions, they stayed home, though lingering in the same place grew tedious—especially for the children.","That day, Yue’er trotted over to her two brothers, her voice brimming with excitement. “Big Brother, Brother, I heard Brother Song and the others talking about going to some forest to gather ingredients. Can we tag along and see what it’s like?”","Hearing this, the two brothers practicing martial arts in the courtyard paused. Hao’er wiped the sweat from his forehead and asked, “Will they agree to take us? And how long will they be gone?” Mother told us to wait here for her. If we go with them, won’t Mother come back and not find us?”","“No, no, no. If Mother comes, we’ll just have her wait here for us to return,” Yue’er said with a beaming smile. “I only heard them talking and ran to tell you guys. I haven’t even asked them if they’ll take us along yet.”"]},{"number":4984,"title":"Chapter 4984: Go Ahead","paragraphs":["Chapter 4984: Go Ahead","“Where’s Sister Mi’er?” Muchen asked, glancing at his younger sister. “Doesn’t she know Brother Song and the others are going?”","“Her Mother called her away. She probably doesn’t know. I just heard them mention it—they said they’re going to see if there are any new ingredients.” She stepped forward, grabbing both brothers’ hands and shaking them. “Big Brother, Brother, let’s go too! Please, please!” Staying here every day is so boring, and I can’t keep eating like this. Look, my tummy’s getting round.”","She patted her plump little belly and sighed with the air of a little adult: “If I get any fatter, Master won’t recognize me anymore.”","Hao’er and Muchen glanced at her, their lips curving into faint smiles. These past days here, they’d eaten all sorts of delicious and exotic foods daily. The two older brothers were fine—they knew moderation and burned calories through martial arts training, so their bodies hadn’t gained weight. But Yue’er couldn’t control her appetite or get herself moving. After just a few days, while her face remained slim, her little belly had noticeably rounded out. To them, she looked utterly adorable like this.","“Big Brother, how about we tag along? It’d be good training and a chance to stretch our legs,” Mu Chen suggested, turning to his elder brother.","“Sounds good,” Hao’er nodded. “Let’s find Sister Mi’er first. We need to discuss this with her.”","“I’ll go find Sister Mi. Big Brother, Brother, you two head to Brother Song’s courtyard first. I’ll bring Sister Mi over shortly.” Yue’er said cheerfully, springing to her feet and dashing out the door, waving excitedly at them like a bird released from its cage.","Seeing her such joy, the two brothers’ eyes softened, a hint of warmth flickering within. After tidying up, they stepped out of the courtyard.","The three Song brothers were in the midst of final discussions. As matters reached their conclusion, Song Er and Song San rose to their feet. “We’ll head back to prepare,” they said. “Once everything’s arranged, we’ll depart shortly.”","“Alright,” the eldest Song brother replied. As he rose, he spotted two figures approaching and greeted them with a smile, “What brings you here?”","“Big Brother Song, Second Brother Song, Third Brother Song.” The two bowed and addressed them by their birth order. It must be said, calling them by their birth order made them easier to remember.","“We’ve decided to take a trip. We probably won’t be able to keep you company for a while. If you want to go anywhere or try some good food, just ask Mi’er, okay?” Song Er said with a smile, looking at the two.","Hearing this, Hao’er spoke up: “Actually, we came to ask if we could go with Big Brother Song?”","“You want to come with us?” The three brothers exchanged surprised glances before replying, “That’s not advisable. This isn’t a leisure trip. The forest we’re heading to is quite dangerous, and if we need to search for food, we’ll likely venture deeper. Taking you along wouldn’t be safe.”","“Big Brother Song, rest assured. We won’t slow you down. Our master trained us early on to survive alone in dangerous forests. We can absolutely protect ourselves.” Regardless of their actual strength, the contract beasts they carried alone were enough to keep them safe in the forest.","“But...” Third Brother Song hesitated, his gaze lingering on the two. For a moment, he couldn’t make up his mind.","“Go then!” The voice of the Song Patriarch echoed through the courtyard, causing everyone present to turn their heads."]},{"number":4985,"title":"Chapter 4985: Go Together","paragraphs":["Chapter 4985: Go Together","“Father.”","The three Song brothers bowed to him upon his arrival, their eyes glancing toward their younger sister and Yun Qi standing beside him.","Song Lingbo entered with his hands clasped behind his back. “Come to think of it, I haven’t ventured outside in quite some time. I’ll accompany you this time—and bring them along too! It’ll broaden their horizons.”","Hearing this, the three brothers exchanged glances before replying, “Alright, we’ll go together. But won’t that leave only Mother behind at the estate?”","“Hmm. With your Mother overseeing the household, there’s no need to worry. Even if she encounters something she can’t resolve, she’ll consult with the elders.” Song Lingbo glanced at Hao’er and the others, smiling as he added, “You three should go back with Mi’er to pack. There’s no need to leave today—we’ll set out first thing tomorrow morning!”","“Yes, thank you, Uncle Song,” Hao’er and the others bowed in response.","“Come on, come on. I’ll take you back to pack and see what you need to bring,” Mi’er said cheerfully, beckoning Hao’er and Muchen. She led the three of them back to prepare.","In the courtyard, Song Lingbo instructed his three sons to prepare thoroughly and select a few servants from the estate to form an escort party.","Meanwhile, Mi’er, who had brought the three back to the courtyard, explained, “Since we’ll be traveling with my father and brother the entire journey, we won’t have to worry about food along the way. We don’t need to carry too many provisions; we can just gather whatever we need locally whenever we’re hungry.”","The three nodded in agreement without objection. Then Hao’er asked, “Sister Mi’er, how long will this trip take? I’m a bit worried that if we leave, Mother might come by just when we’re gone and not see us.”","Hearing this, Mi’er smiled brightly and said, “Don’t worry about that. I’ll go tell my mother right now. I’ll let her know a friend might be visiting. If she comes, I’ll ask her to stay at the mansion and be well taken care of until we return.”","“Can we leave a message for Mother too?” Hao’er asked.","“Of course you can. You can also leave her a letter. Go to your rooms to write whatever you wish. Once you’re done, I’ll gather them all together and give them to my Mother. When your Mother arrives, she can hand them to her. How does that sound?” Mi’er inquired.","“Mm, great!” The three children’s eyes lit up, and they immediately agreed.","“Alright, then go write your letters first. I’ll go get some spirit rice. I’ll come back later to collect your letters before meeting my Mother.” Song Mi’er said, waving to them before turning to leave.","The three had someone prepare ink and paper. After writing their letters in their room, they waited for Mi’er to return and handed her the finished letters.","Song Mi’er took the letters to her Mother’s courtyard. As soon as she entered, she saw her father there too. She trotted in, calling out cheerfully, “Father, Mother.”","“You’re a grown young lady now, yet you still skip about like this,” Lady Song shook her head, looking at her with a mix of indulgence and resignation.","“Mother, I’m leaving tomorrow with Father and my brothers. Don’t miss me too much!” Song Mi’er giggled, wrapping her arm around her mother’s and nuzzling her shoulder.","“When you go out with your father, learn as much as you can,” Lady Song gently tapped her nose, her tone tinged with resignation. “Your brothers mostly stay home, but you’re always running off somewhere. And when you do leave, you’re gone for so long. It keeps Mother constantly worried.”"]},{"number":4986,"title":"Chapter 4986: Leave a Message","paragraphs":["Chapter 4986: Leave a Message","“Don’t worry, Mother! I’m doing just fine out here! No one dares bully me.” She said with a smile, lifting her chin slightly in pride. She was someone’s Master—her Master was none other than the Empress Phoenix Sovereign. Who would dare cross her?","But these words, she couldn’t share with her parents now.","“Rest assured! Taking her with us won’t cause any trouble. It’s actually you staying home that worries me a bit.” Song Lingbo frowned as he spoke, looking at her. “Our journey will likely take about a month. If anything comes up at home that you can’t handle, remember to consult the clan elders. With all of us sons away, if anyone sends calling cards, don’t accept them. And definitely don’t attend any banquets.”","“Yes, I understand,” Lady Song replied with a smile.","“Mother, I expect a friend will visit after we leave. Please welcome her and let her stay in the mansion until we return,” Mi’er hurriedly added.","“Your friend? Male or female?” Lady Song asked in surprise.","Song Mi’er beamed. “A woman. She’s someone very important. Mother, you must instruct the servants to treat her well.”","Seeing her daughter’s earnestness, she shook her head and chuckled. “What is this friend’s name? You must tell your mother clearly, lest we mistake someone else for her.”","What was her name?","Song Mi’er’s mind raced. She recalled that Master often referred to herself as Lady Xuanyuan when outside. She then told her Mother, “My friend’s husband’s family name is Xuanyuan. She is commonly addressed as Lady Xuanyuan.”","“Lady Xuanyuan? Very well, I’ll remember that. I’ll instruct the gatekeeper accordingly.” She nodded in agreement, silently committing the name to memory.","“And this—this is the letter I left for Lady Xuanyuan. Mother, please remember to hand it to her personally.” Mi’er took out the letters written by Hao’er and the others and handed them to her.","Mi’er stayed and chatted with her parents in the room for a while before rising to return and prepare for tomorrow’s journey.","Early the next morning, a group of lightly-equipped travelers set out from the Song residence.","This time, with Song Lingbo and his three sons traveling together, they selected twelve men from the household to form an escort. For their purposes, this dozen was more than sufficient.","After all, these twelve would likely focus more on protecting the three children. As for the Song family members themselves, they were quite confident in their own abilities.","Once outside the city gates, the group immediately took to flying on their magical artifacts, heading straight for their destination.","After half a day’s flight, they reached the forest by mid-afternoon. Since their goal was to gather ingredients, they naturally skipped the outer regions. Only the deeper parts of the forest held what they sought.","They flew directly to the inner edge of the forest before venturing in. Mi’er and Hao’er, who were nearby, remarked: Look, this forest has distinct zones. It’s quite obvious—this patch of red trees marks the inner perimeter.”","Hao’er and the others looked down and indeed saw a conspicuous expanse of red trees within the forest below. It formed a clear boundary, encircling the area like a border, creating a distinct demarcation.","“Squeak!”","Suddenly, a series of sharp, urgent cries pierced the air. Hao’er and the others looked toward the source to see a dark mass of giant birds approaching. Simultaneously, they heard Song Lingbo’s deep voice command, “Vittle Spirit Birds! Quickly, speed up our descent!”"]},{"number":4987,"title":"Chapter 4987: Show One’s Hand","paragraphs":["\"Hold on tight!\"","Hearing the voice, Hao’er and the others gripped the flying artifact beneath them as it accelerated downward. A fierce wind lashed their faces, blowing so hard they could barely keep their eyes open.","Behind them came the screeching cries and the flapping of wings from the flock of giant birds. Their vision darkened, and simultaneously, the air grew noticeably colder.","Looking forward, they realized the flying artifact had passed through the canopy of towering trees, entering the forest and landing on the ground.","\"Squeak!\"","A sound echoed, revealing a giant bird, unwilling to let its prey escape. It folded its wings and dove straight down, its sharp, hooked red beak letting out a shrill cry as its two clawed feet lunged toward the nearest child, Muchen.","Perhaps the giant bird deemed this human child too small and harmless. Seizing him would make it easier to carry off its prey for a satisfying meal.","\"Watch out!\"","Not only Song Lingbo and his two sons, but all twelve members of the Song family traveling together cried out in alarm. Seeing the giant bird swoop for the child, they instinctively raised their swords and knives to strike, yet feared injuring the boy. They swiftly gathered their qi and lunged forward. But when they witnessed what happened next, everyone froze in place.","Muchen didn’t even flinch when he saw the giant bird’s talons, as sharp as an eagle’s, reaching for him.","Truth be told, though young, he’d slain countless beasts—let alone a mere giant bird.","Had this giant bird, like others of its kind, dared not descend, the matter might have ended there. As a child, he certainly wouldn’t chase after a flock of so-called Vittle Spirit Birds to pluck their feathers or slay them. But this particular bird mistook him for someone incapable of lifting a finger, even attempting to seize him as prey. Faced with such an insult, he could not stand idly by and let it have its way.","Besides, coming to this forest with the Song family was meant to be a training exercise to broaden his horizons. Yet the Song family seemed to think that as children, they had no means of self-defense. Under these circumstances, he felt it necessary to show off his skills.","Thus, as the giant bird swooped toward him, he crouched low, drew the dagger from his boot, and leaped forward. Seizing the bird’s feathers with one hand, he flipped onto its back. With a swift swing of his blade, he severed the Vittle Spirit Bird’s head clean off.","Blood spattered down from midair, splattering the ground. A sharp, piercing scream erupted—abrupt and terrified. The moment the sound rang out, the head of the Vittle Spirit Bird was severed cleanly, tumbling to the earth. The giant bird, poised to flap its wings and flee, plummeted downward in response to this sudden change.","\"Thud!\"","The bird’s body, as large as an adult human, crashed heavily to the ground. It twitched faintly a few times before finally stiffening completely, its life extinguished.","The three Song family members and the twelve Song family guards were all stunned. They stared dumbly at the scene before them, unable to recover for a long moment.","This... this is insane! Was that kid’s skill just too good? And his reflexes—were they too fast?","He took down a giant Vittle Spirit Bird like that? And with a single stroke, he severed the entire head—a head as big as an adult’s arm..."]},{"number":4988,"title":"Chapter 4988: In The End","paragraphs":["The stunned gazes of the crowd shifted from the child, whose small face remained utterly calm, not even a flicker of surprise crossing his brow, to the dagger in his hand.","This dagger was undoubtedly a fine blade!","Compared to their bewilderment and shock, Mi’er, Hao’er, and Yue’er appeared utterly accustomed to it, showing not the slightest surprise.","They knew Muchen well. If he couldn’t handle even such a giant bird, that would be truly strange.","Mi’er stepped forward, patting her three brothers on the shoulder. Her face beamed with pride and satisfaction as she declared, \"Big Brother, Second Brother, Third Brother, what do you think? Didn’t I tell you? All three of them possess the ability to protect themselves. There’s no need to worry about them.\"","\"Indeed, he’s formidable.\"","The three brothers nodded in unison. After exchanging a glance with Mi’er, they turned their gaze back to Muchen, who was wiping the blade of his dagger. \" \"Who would’ve thought his adaptability and combat skills were this strong?\"","As they spoke, their gazes drifted involuntarily to the two figures standing nearby, their eyes flickering. All three were disciples of the Azure Emperor. If this Yun Yuan was this formidable, Yun Chen and Yun Qi couldn’t be too shabby either.","It seemed their claim of self-sufficiency wasn’t mere bravado.","At that moment, Song Lingbo stepped forward and addressed Muchen: \"This is a Vittle Spirit Bird. It dominates the skies above this forest with its speed and formidable, hardened plumage, preying specifically on cultivators. It consumes their spirit energy and flesh, converting them into its own strength.\"","As he spoke, he crouched beside the Vittle Spirit Bird, pressing his fingers against its corpse. Pointing to a specific spot, he explained, \"This is an elder bird. It has already formed a Golden Core here.\"","Muchen watched as Song Lingbo, whose palm now held a sharp, small knife, precisely stabbed it into the corpse of the Vittle Spirit Bird. Moments later, he extracted a red, thumb-sized, spherical bead.","\"Take it. This is valuable,\" Song Lingbo said, handing the red bead to Muchen.","Muchen glanced at him before reaching out to take it. Examining it, he asked, \"Uncle Song, what use is this bead?\"","Song Lingbo smiled. \"Only Vittle Spirit Birds that live a hundred years become ’old birds.’ And among a hundred old birds, only a few will form Golden Cores. These cores store the bird’s accumulated energy and spirit energy. They can be used for cultivation or swallowed directly—they greatly aid in advancing one’s cultivation.\"","Upon hearing this, Muchen nodded as if understanding. He walked over to Yue’er, handed her the red bead, and said, \"Here, play with it. But don’t eat it—it’s too dirty.\"","\"Hehe, thank you, Second Senior Brother,\" Yue’er said, her eyes crinkling with laughter as she took the red bead and began to play with it.","The Song family members, seeing him give that rare Golden Core to Yun Qi, couldn’t help but smile. They thought to themselves, their bond is truly strong.","\"Alright, let’s head forward and take a look! This forest holds countless treasures, but also unimaginable dangers. So, we must remain cautious. Safety comes first above all else.\" Song Lingbo said, looking at everyone, especially the three children and his daughter, Mi’er.","\"Yes, we understand.\" The group responded in unison before setting off together.","After they departed, the scent of blood on the ground drew the flock of Vittle Spirit Birds circling overhead. With shrill cries, they descended, circling the forest several times before diving in to tear at the corpse..."]},{"number":4989,"title":"Chapter 4989: Plans","paragraphs":["\"Let’s rest here for a bit! See if there are any ingredients nearby—we can just gather some local produce to cook.\" Song Lingbo surveyed the area, deciding to pause their journey here.","\"Alright, you guys rest up. We’ll scout the surroundings,\" Song Yihong said, gathering his two brothers and leading a couple of Jingwei guards to investigate nearby.","\"Find a place to sit and rest. Drink water if you’re thirsty, but don’t wander off.\" Song Mi’er instructed Hao’er and the others before approaching her father. With a bright smile, she asked, \"Father, I heard there’s Black Awn Lingzhi in this forest. Is that true?\"","Sitting beneath a tree, Song Lingbo glanced at her and replied, \"I’ve never encountered one myself, but I’ve heard that the cultivator finds them here. Why do you ask?\"","\"I heard that these Black Awn Lingzhi gain sentience and can move on their own, so I’m curious! I wonder what they look like? Do they taste good?\" She rested her chin in her hand, picturing ordinary lingzhi while imagining the black awn variety.","They say it’s a precious treasure with countless benefits. It’s just a pity she’d never seen one in her entire life.","Song Lingbo didn’t respond to her question. Instead, his gaze drifted toward the three children sitting in a circle. A complex expression flashed across his eyes as he asked, \"Are all three of them that skilled?\"","Caught off guard by the sudden shift in topic, Song Mi’er paused, following his gaze to see Hao’er and the others deep in conversation.","Seeing this, she smiled. \"Yes! All three of them are quite skilled. Yun Chen stands out the most, but the other two aren’t half bad either. Father, don’t underestimate them!\"","\"Of course I won’t underestimate them. After all, their master...\" His voice trailed off, leaving the sentence unfinished.","Over there, Hao’er and the others sat in a circle, deep in conversation.","\"This place is a rare training ground. We haven’t had much chance to spar lately. Here, we can really let loose. How about this? Let’s have a contest. We’ll see who has the most fierce beast crystal cores when we leave.\"","Hao’er spoke, glancing at his younger siblings and casting a sideways look toward Song Lingbo. \"Unless absolutely necessary, do not summon your life-bound contract beasts.\"","\"Yes, we understand.\" Muchen and Muyue nodded.","\"And you,\" Hao’er addressed Yue’er, \"though you’re studying medicine, don’t let your combat skills grow rusty. This time, you’re forbidden from using potions against the fierce beast. Try to defeat it with your own strength.\"","His sister’s interest in medicine was commendable, but he worried she might become overly reliant on potions. If she ever faced real combat, her fighting prowess might fall short.","\"Mm-hmm, Yun Qi understands.\" She responded with a cheerful smile.","Not long after, Song Yihong and the others returned. Some had gathered branches, others carried wild game, and a few had collected mushrooms.","\"Big Brother, Second Brother, Third Brother, you’re back!\" Song Mi’er smiled as she stepped forward to help carry their belongings. Spotting the abundance of mushrooms, she exclaimed, \" \"So many mushrooms!\"","\"Probably because it rained recently. That area has a lot of mushrooms growing.\"","Song Yifan said, turning to Song Lingbo, \"Father, we caught some wild game. After separating the meat from the bones, we’ll use the bones to make a broth. Then we’ll use that broth to poach the meat and mushrooms. It should be quite delicious.\""]},{"number":4990,"title":"Chapter 4990: Arrives","paragraphs":["\"Alright, let’s do as you suggest! When traveling, there’s no need for elaborate meals—the main thing is to make sure everyone eats their fill. See if you can find any wild greens around here to pick and add to the soup later.\" Song Lingbo spoke as he crossed his legs beneath the tree, closing his eyes to rest. With several sons handling the task, he naturally didn’t need to lift a finger, simply waiting for their return.","\"We’ll help too,\" Hao’er and the others said as they approached.","Seeing this, Mi’er said, \"Then come with me to gather some wild greens! Pick plenty of mushrooms too, just in case we don’t have enough.\"","\"I’ll go with you,\" Song Yiming said, setting down his things before accompanying them to the nearby area.","The others began their tasks methodically: some prepared the game, others fetched pots and bowls, while some readied the fire...","Several days later, as Hao’er and the others were training in the forest with the Song family, Feng Jiu arrived in the city. After inquiring about the Song residence, she approached their gate.","Facing the large door, she stepped forward and knocked.","The door swung open. A middle-aged man studied the woman in green robes outside, then asked, \"May I ask if you are Lady Xuanyuan?\"","Before leaving, Miss Mi’er had instructed him that a friend of hers would visit—a woman in green robes, matching her description in age and appearance. He assumed this must be her.","Hearing the gatekeeper’s words, Feng Jiu raised an eyebrow. She had been about to ask, but unexpectedly, he had addressed her first.","So she replied, \"Indeed. I’m here to see Mi’er.\"","\"Please come inside, honored guest.\" The middle-aged man dared not delay, hastily opening the gate to invite her in. \" Mi’er instructed before leaving that Lady Xuanyuan is our Song family’s honored guest. We must not neglect her.","As he escorted her into the mansion, he beckoned another servant to take his place at the gate and personally guided her toward the front hall. Slowing his pace slightly, he added, \"Lady Xuanyuan, please take a seat in the hall. I will fetch My lady.\"","After Feng Jiu sat down, a maid brought tea and pastries before withdrawing to wait outside.","Sitting alone in the hall, Feng Jiu was unrestrained. She picked up the tea, sipped it, then tasted a pastry. Soon after, a beautiful woman walked in at a leisurely pace.","She observed the woman, noting a faint resemblance between her brow and Song Mi’er’s. Yet unlike Song Mi’er’s coquettish features, this woman possessed a different kind of beauty.","Her beauty wasn’t dazzling, nor was it coquettish or delicate. Instead, it radiated an air of dignified elegance—not startlingly striking, yet growing more captivating the longer one looked, revealing deeper layers of grace.","\"Lady Xuanyuan.\"","Lady Song entered alone, her face adorned with a composed smile. She was somewhat surprised by Lady Xuanyuan’s youth and the calm, serene aura she carried.","She gave a slight nod, her voice gentle and warm as a spring breeze: \"I am the wife of the Song P and Mi’er’s Mother. Mi’er has spoken of Lady Xuanyuan, though I never imagined you would be so young.\"","As she spoke, she took her seat at the head of the table, her gentle gaze resting appreciatively on the figure in blue seated to her left.","At that moment, Feng Jiu also rose, gave a slight bow, and sat down. She smiled, \"I too have often heard Mi’er speak of you, My lady. You are indeed as gentle and beautiful as she described.\""]},{"number":4991,"title":"Chapter 4991: Company","paragraphs":["Hearing this, Lady Song couldn’t help but smile, her expression filled with indulgent resignation: \" Mi’er has caused me quite a bit of worry. After she left home not long ago, she didn’t even send a single letter back. I was so anxious at home. Thankfully, she managed to make friends like Lady Xuanyuan while away. She told me that Lady Xuanyuan took great care of her during her travels. Now that she’s come home, she must stay for a while longer so we can properly fulfill our duties as hosts.\"","\"Actually, she was the one who took care of me more while we were out, especially with her exceptional culinary skills,\" Feng Jiu said with a smile.","\"Our family has a long tradition of culinary arts. All the children in our household are quite skilled in the kitchen. When Mi’er returned recently, she brought three friends she’d met out there. They stayed here for a few days and all gained quite a bit of weight.\"","Lady Song thought of Yun Qi, one of those three children—plump and adorable with her round little frame—and her smile deepened involuntarily.","Hearing this, Feng Jiu’s eyes flickered slightly. \"You mean Yun Chen and the others, right? We came here together, but I had to leave early for some business. We agreed I’d come back to pick them up once I was done.\"","\"Lady Xuanyuan knows them too?\" Lady Song asked in surprise. \"Mi’er never mentioned it to me. But then, she probably didn’t expect Lady Xuanyuan to finish her business so quickly. Just a few days ago, Mi’er and Yun Qi, along with her father and three brothers, left to explore the forest for new ingredients. They’ll likely be gone about a month.\"","As she spoke, she retrieved a thick bundle of letters and handed it over. \"Mi’er asked me to give this to you. Lady Xuanyuan, please stay at the estate for now. It will be nice to have company.\"","Feng Jiu accepted the letter, opened it, and discovered it wasn’t written by Mi’er but by the three children. They mainly recounted their experiences at the Song family’s residence these past days. They also mentioned that their journey out was intended to gain some experience, urging her to wait for their return at the Song residence and not to leave them behind.","A smile touched Feng Jiu’s lips. She folded the letter carefully, tucked it away into her cosmos sack, then turned to Lady Song with a smile. \"Then I shall be staying for the time being.\"","\"Not at all!\"","Lady Song smiled. \"After Mi’er mentioned you were coming, I had a courtyard prepared for you. Let me show you around! I’ll also take you on a tour of the estate. The flowers in my garden are in full bloom right now—perfect for admiring.\"","Feng Jiu agreed cheerfully, following her out of the hall toward the rear courtyard, taking the opportunity to familiarize herself with the Song residence...","After touring the Song residence, they visited the guest quarters. Yet in the end, Feng Jiu didn’t choose to stay in the courtyard prepared by Lady Song. Instead, she settled into the courtyard where Yue’er lived.","That day, Lady Song accompanied her until dusk before departing. After Lady Song left, Feng Jiu had servants prepare a bath, soaked in the warm water, changed into fresh clothes, and then entered her spatial pocket.","Since the three children had gone off to train, she would wait here for their return. She might as well use this free time to see if any medicinal herbs or medicinal pills needed refining and prepare them while she had the chance.","The next morning, Lady Song arrived at Feng Jiu’s courtyard. After having breakfast served, she learned from the maidservant that Lady Xuanyuan hadn’t risen yet, so she waited in the courtyard."]},{"number":4992,"title":"Chapter 4992: Observe","paragraphs":["It wasn’t until the tail end of the third hour that the door finally opened, and that figure clad in azure emerged.","\"Lady Xuanyuan, I thought dining alone might be too quiet for you. Since I’m also by myself, I had the servants bring breakfast over and set it up in your courtyard. Let’s eat together!\" She said with a smile, glancing at Feng Jiu, whose brow still held traces of sleepiness. \" If you find the mansion too dull, I’ll have someone take you into town for a stroll later!\"","\"Alright.\" Feng Jiu replied, though it was unclear whether she was agreeing to the first or second part of the invitation. Nevertheless, after her voice faded, she saw Feng Jiu stride over and sit down at the table.","\"These are just ordinary breakfast dishes. I wonder if they suit your taste.\" \" Lady Song said, motioning for a maid to serve her a bowl of clear congee.","\"It’s fine.\" Feng Jiu smiled, sampling each dish in turn. After a while, a bowl of congee and several dishes left her quite full.","After eating her fill, she chatted with Lady Song for a while longer before leaving the mansion with one of the Song household’s attendants to wander around the city.","In stark contrast to Feng Jiu’s leisurely pace, the Song family group deep within the forest—including Hao’er and the others—were far from relaxed.","The reason was simple: as they ventured deeper into the heart of the woods, they encountered not only fierce beasts but also rare edible treasures. At that moment, the Song family’s father and sons were racing against golden snub-nosed monkeys.","Golden little monkeys darted and leaped among the branches, plucking fist-sized red berries from the twigs while emitting occasional squeaks.","After gathering the fruit, the monkeys didn’t leave. Instead, they snapped branches to pelt the Song family members, then let out a shrill cry and swiftly retreated.","\"There are too many monkeys! We should retreat!\"","Song Lingbo declared. Seeing the berries nearly depleted by the monkeys, his anger flared. He flipped his palm, unleashing a burst of flame that coalesced into a blade, slashing toward the monkeys.","\"Hiss!\"","The monkeys bared their teeth in a snarling hiss, as if issuing a warning. Yet to the Song family’s surprise, the monkeys dared not approach the three children, not even hurling objects in their direction.","\"Perhaps there are more sour berries ahead. We can pick some then to make jam. The monkeys have picked most of these, leaving only a few behind,\" Song Yiming said, motioning for everyone to follow him out.","The group pressed deeper into the forest, the twelve elite Song family guards forming a protective perimeter. Suddenly, a furious roar echoed through the air, and a vicious figure shot out from the shadows.","\"Roooooar!\"","\"Watch out!\"","As the beast’s roar reverberated, Song Lingbo bellowed a warning. Instantly, the group scattered in all directions, dodging the sudden charge. His eyes widened as he focused on the creature.","He raised a hand, signaling the others to retreat. \"This is a full-grown Scarlet Earth Tiger. You all step back. I’ll handle this.\"","Seeing him prepare to act, Hao’er, Muchen, and Yue’er all turned to watch him. Throughout their journey, they’d seen him dispatch fierce beasts with a single strike. But what about this one?","Over these days of training, they had also observed the Song family’s techniques and attacks. However, since those differed from what they had learned, their interest gradually waned. But if it was Song Lingbo... perhaps they could learn something from watching him engage in battle against the Scarlet Earth Tiger."]},{"number":4993,"title":"Chapter 4993: Tiger Pelt","paragraphs":["Mi’er shielded the three of them as they retreated. Seeing their eyes fixed on her father ahead, she smiled and said, \"My father is incredibly powerful. His blade technique alone puts my brothers to shame.\"","Just as she spoke, Hao’er and the others watched as Song Lingbo, facing the Scarlet Earth Tiger, swung a blade in a spinning arc straight at the beast. The blade in his hand was about three fingers wide, gleaming with a sharp, black luster. As he swung, the aura of the blade’s energy burst forth, striking directly at the tiger’s vital points.","The Scarlet Earth Tiger was robust and powerful, a peak-tier fierce beast with formidable combat prowess. As their one-on-one battle commenced, the scent of blood quickly filled the air.","\"Roooooar!\"","\"Whoosh! Whoosh!\"","The roar of the blade’s aura and the Scarlet Earth Tiger’s bellow echoed intermittently. The onlookers stepped back, watching as trees around them snapped—whether from the tiger’s charge or the blade’s force—crashing down in a chaotic tangle that partially obscured the figure of man and beast.","\"Thud!\"","After about half an incense stick’s worth of time, a thunderous crash echoed, followed by a return to silence.","Everyone watched as Song Lingbo emerged, one hand gripping his blade and the other dragging the slain Scarlet Earth Tiger. With effortless ease, he hauled the beast, weighing hundreds of pounds, before the crowd.","\"Mi’er, how about I skin this Scarlet Earth Tiger and make you a rug?\" Song Lingbo asked with a smile, looking at his youngest daughter.","\"No need, no need! I don’t need it now. Father, give it to my brothers!\" Song Mi’er waved her hands hurriedly.","\"Fine, if you don’t want it, I’ll skin it and send it to your Mother.\"","Song Lingbo glanced at his three sons. \"If you want to hunt one yourselves, go ahead. It’s just a Scarlet Earth Tiger—you’re perfectly capable.\"","The three Song brothers twitched their lips at their father’s blatant favoritism. They were used to it—since childhood, they’d had to fight for what they wanted, while their sister got whatever she desired effortlessly. That was the difference between sons and daughters!","\"Don’t just stand around. Stay in this area for the next couple days. You can explore around.\" Song Lingbo looked at Hao’er and the others. \"You three come along too! Don’t wander too far. Stay safe.\"","These past days had truly made him reevaluate these three youngsters. Though young, they were no pushovers. Their skills were more than sufficient to handle fierce beasts. Back when his own children were their age, they’d still be trailing after him, whining and crying!","Truly, comparing people to people is like comparing the living to the dead. One wonders, whose children are these three? How could they be so accomplished at such a young age?","\"Father, I’ll take them to explore nearby. I won’t follow Brother and the others.\" Song Mi’er said cheerfully, waving at them before swiftly leading Hao’er and the other two away.","\"You two follow and protect them. Don’t let anything happen to them,\" Song Lingbo instructed the two Jingwei.","\"Yes, Master.\" The two guards responded. Though they doubted the children needed their protection, they swiftly followed.","\"Father, we’ll explore nearby too,\" the three Song brothers declared, each taking a child and departing.","After they left, Song Lingbo personally began stripping the tiger’s pelt, preparing to bring it home as a gift for his lady..."]},{"number":4994,"title":"Chapter 4994: Golden Silk Monkey","paragraphs":["Song Mi’er led Hao’er and the other two around the area but saw no other beasts. She suggested to them, \"Why don’t we look for some ingredients or supplies nearby? There shouldn’t be any fierce beasts around here.\"","Hao’er glanced around and said, \"Sister Mi’er, don’t worry about us. We can protect ourselves. You go gather ingredients! The three of us want to explore a bit further.\"","\"But...\" Song Mi’er hesitated. After all, the danger here was lurking—who knew what might suddenly appear?","\"Sister Mi’er, don’t worry! We’ll protect ourselves,\" Yue’er said with a bright smile.","\"We came out to test how much our skills have improved. We can’t always rely on you to protect us,\" Muchen added.","Seeing this, Mi’er glanced at the three of them before finally saying, \"Alright then! But you must be careful. If you encounter a fierce beast you can’t handle, run back immediately. Safety comes first.\"","\"Got it.\" The three responded, exchanging glances as a hint of amusement flashed in their eyes.","\"We’ll follow you!\" the two Jingwei birds told Hao’er and the others. \"Our Master ordered us to protect you.\"","Hao’er and the others exchanged a glance with the two Jingwei before nodding. They continued forward. After traveling a considerable distance, Hao’er turned to Muchen and Muyue. \"Should we stay together or split up?\"","Muchen and Muyue looked at each other, considered for a moment, then said, \"Let’s stick together for now. We’ll see if any fierce beasts appear.\"","\"Alright.\" Hao’er nodded and continued forward.","Truthfully, given their current skills and strength, he felt quite confident even if they split up. Moreover, Yue’er now had an exceptionally powerful contract beast, so there was no need to worry about her.","\"Did you hear something?\" Muchen stopped and looked toward a certain spot in the forest.","Hearing this, Hao’er and Yue’er also stopped and listened intently. Faint, faint sounds drifted out from the dense foliage.","\"Sounds like monkeys,\" Yue’er remarked, glancing at them. \"Could it be that group of Golden Silk Monkeys from earlier?\"","\"Let’s go check.\" \" Hao’er said, leading them toward the source of the sound.","The two Jingwei following behind overheard their conversation and immediately stepped forward to block their path. They addressed Hao’er: \"Young Master Chen, those Golden Silk Spirit Monkeys are not gentle creatures. On the contrary, they are combative and live in large groups. If we pursue them, it would be unwise.\"","Hearing this, Hao’er replied, \"There were roughly thirty to fifty monkeys earlier. Even if we find their main nest, there couldn’t be more than fifty or sixty. These Golden Silk Monkeys are gregarious creatures, but their groups never exceed a hundred. They’re combative—perfect for us to hone our skills.\"","\"But...\" They tried to protest, only to see the three already striding ahead. Reluctantly, they followed.","Within the dense forest, towering trees formed a natural canopy of green leaves. Even at midday, only faint sunlight filtered through the thick foliage, casting slanted patches of light.","A damp air hung heavy, carrying the faint scent of decaying leaves mingled with earthiness, carried by the gentle breeze.","Around a tree so massive three men couldn’t encircle it, a troop of Golden Silk Monkeys leaped and darted through the branches..."]},{"number":4995,"title":"Chapter 4995: React","paragraphs":["After Hao’er and the others drew near, they didn’t reveal themselves immediately. Instead, they hid partially behind the trees, observing the scene ahead. The large tree was incredibly lush, its branches and leaves spreading like a giant umbrella. Vines grew and twisted around the trunk, with some monkeys clinging to the vines, swinging and leaping between the trees, emitting squeaking sounds.","\"Probably less than seventy,\" Muchen estimated the monkeys. It was indeed a group, but not an overwhelming number.","\"Huh? That larger monkey sitting up there actually has others grooming it.\" Yue’er watched with curiosity as the big monkey sat atop the tree, flanked by two smaller ones crouching beside it.","Hao’er glanced over and whispered, \"That one is probably the monkey king. Groups like this usually have a leader.\"","\"Oh.\"","Yue’er blinked, watching as the king monkey wiped a fruit on its body before popping it into its mouth. It glanced left and right, then suddenly fixed its gaze on them. Instantly, it leaped up, baring its teeth in a snarl as it hurled the half-eaten fruit toward them.","\"Oh no, we’re spotted!\" Yue’er cried, leaping out.","Hao’er and Muchen also sprang forward, positioning themselves beside Yue’er. Noticing the two Jingwei behind them about to follow, Hao’er said, \"You two stay back. The three of us can handle this.\"","\"That monkey’s reflexes are lightning-fast. The three of you might not stand a chance,\" one Jingwei said, looking at them with concern. Though their skills were indeed impressive, three people with six hands against that group of monkeys—they feared they might be overwhelmed.","\"It’s alright. If we can’t handle it, you can come out and help us then,\" Yue’er said with a smile, already gripping a dagger in her hand. She fixed her gaze on the monkey swinging toward them on a vine, then leaped forward. Instead of dodging, she charged straight at it.","Seeing this, the two Jingwei felt their breath catch in their throats, hearts racing.","The next moment, the other two also leapt forward. Their agile movements were no less nimble than those of the Golden Silk Monkeys. Watching their swift, decisive strikes, the two Jingwei took a deep breath and slowly exhaled.","It seemed their worries were unfounded. The three of them should be more than capable of handling this group of monkeys.","So, they held back, retreating to watch from behind a tree. They reasoned that if their intervention was truly needed, they could always step in later.","The trio darted forward, using vines to evade the monkeys’ strikes or leap onto branches. They had chosen to confront this troop of Golden Silk Monkeys specifically to hone their reflexes in the chaos of battle. Outnumbered and facing agile opponents, this scenario should push their reaction times to the limit.","Hao’er leapt from a branch, his dagger flashing toward the monkey king. The ape, who had been watching and calling from the treetops, saw the blade coming and instantly bared its claws. With a shrill cry, it lunged at Hao’er, swift as the wind yet carrying a fierce, cutting momentum.","\"Rip!\"","The monkey’s claws tore through Hao’er’s clothing, but her skin remained unharmed. Hao’er counterattacked swiftly, forcing the monkey king to retreat. Having missed its strike, the monkey king showed no desire to linger in battle. It turned and leaped to the other side of the tree. Seeing this, Hao’er followed immediately."]},{"number":4996,"title":"Chapter 4996: No Wonder","paragraphs":["\"I didn’t expect their reflexes to be this sharp.\" One of the guards watched the scene unfold ahead and couldn’t help but sigh softly.","\"Their courage is extraordinary too.\"","Another chimed in, observing how the two youngsters struck with ruthless precision and not a moment’s hesitation. Around the great tree, monkey corpses lay scattered haphazardly on the ground, blood splattered and thick in the air.","\"That fierce beast we ate yesterday—I heard from Miss Mi’er that they hunted it down.\"","\"Wow, impressive, truly impressive! No wonder the Master agreed to bring them into the forest. Though, I doubt even he knew they possessed such skills beforehand?\"","\"Indeed, he didn’t. They originally followed Miss Mi’er back.\"","\"Huh? Look!\" As they spoke, one of them suddenly widened his eyes upon seeing Yun Qi ahead sheathe his dagger and switch to a whip.","\"What is it?\" The other guard ollowed his gaze, landing on the whip Yun Qi was cracking. With a single lash, the monkey let out a shriek and bolted, head in its paws, clearly terrified of the whip.","\"Her whip handling is quite nimble. These monkeys probably fear whips the most,\" one guard remarked, a hint of amusement flickering across his face.","The other rolled his eyes at this. \"Who asked you to watch her technique? I told you to look at the whip itself—look at that whip...\"","\"The whip?\"","The nearby guard glanced at the whip in Yun Qi’s hand. \"Looks like a decent magical artifact. But I don’t use whips myself, so I’m not too familiar with them. What’s up with this whip? Is there something wrong with it?\"","\"If I’m not mistaken, this whip is the Ancient Divine Whip. I’ve heard it was bestowed by the Azure Emperor upon his young disciple, Yun Qi, as a means of self-defense. He even issued a decree of death, declaring that anyone who dares covet this Divine Whip shall face the annihilation of their entire clan!\" The guard spoke, his eyes flickering with a hint of excitement.","He never imagined he’d see the Ancient Divine Whip. He’d only ever encountered it in the Weapon Compendium, never expecting to behold the real thing. If this whip was genuine, then their identities...","Suddenly, it all clicked into place. Why would their master personally lead them into the forest? Could it be he already knew their true identities? No wonder—how could Miss Mi’er bring back people without informing her parents?","\"Ah? Then... then they’re the Azur...\" The guard beside him gasped, his words cut off as a hand clamped over his mouth.","\"Good. Keep it to yourself,\" he hurriedly added, scanning the surroundings. Seeing no one nearby, he exhaled softly.","\"Master knew too?\" the guard asked.","\"Of course he knew. But since Master didn’t speak of it, we must keep it sealed tight—never utter a word.\" The other man spoke, glancing ahead and pausing in surprise.","In just that brief moment, only a dozen Golden Silk Monkeys remained.","\"Squeak! Squeak!\"","The remaining dozen Golden Silk Monkeys shrieked in panic, abandoning the fight altogether. They fled swiftly, vanishing into the forest within mere breaths.","\"Senior Brother, what about the monkey king?\" Yue’er asked Hao’er as he returned.","\"I killed him.\"","He opened his palm, revealing a crystal core: \"This is for you. Let’s look around—these monkeys must have hidden something here.\""]},{"number":4997,"title":"Chapter 4997: You Know Me","paragraphs":["\"Alright.\"","Yue’er took the crystal core, examined it briefly, then tucked it away. She followed him to the great tree to investigate. Finally, they spotted a tiny hole in one side of the trunk. A pile of leaves covered something inside. When they parted the leaves, they found a collection of strange and peculiar objects.","\"Senior Brother, where did that monkey get these things? Are these shiny things beads?\" Yue’er pulled out a fist-sized bead radiating a layer of spiritual energy glow, unsure what it was.","Hao’er stepped forward to look. Seeing mostly glowing or colorful stones and similar items, he said, \"Pack these things up and take them with us.\"","\"Alright.\" Yue’er, being small, climbed inside and gathered everything up.","The two guard then hurried forward. \"Young Master Chen, perhaps we should head back first! They might already be preparing food over there.\" Both secretly wiped away sweat, deeply worried about venturing further in.","Hearing this, Hao’er looked at Muchen and Muyue and asked, \"Are you hungry?\"","\"Not hungry.\" They shook their heads. They had food with them, so they genuinely hadn’t felt hungry.","\"Well then, perhaps we should go see if Miss Mi’er has gathered any ingredients?\" another Jingwei suggested. He felt it best to lead them back. Firstly, their combat prowess was somewhat intimidating. Secondly, he feared they might venture deeper and encounter something they couldn’t handle. If anything happened, ten of them wouldn’t be enough to make up for it.","\"Then let’s head back first!\" Muchen spoke up, saying, \"The monkey carcasses here might attract other fierce beasts soon. To spare them worry, we should return first!\"","\"Mhm.\" Hao’er nodded before following the two guard members toward Mi’er, intending to help her search for ingredients.","Song Lingbo gazed at the entire tiger pelt he’d stripped off, a smile spreading across his face. He was about to pack it away, planning to process it at home before presenting it to his wife, when a voice suddenly reached his ears.","\"Sir, this tiger pelt is exceptionally well-skinned. Might I inquire if you would consider selling it to me?\"","Recognizing the voice, Song Lingbo looked up to see a group of about forty or fifty people approaching from the distance. The middle-aged man leading them was staring intently at the tiger pelt in his hands.","\"Sorry, I need this pelt myself,\" Song Lingbo replied, tucking it away. He then instructed the nearby Jingwei guards, \"Prepare the tiger meat. Simmer the bones for soup. We’ll have this Scarlet Earth Tiger for lunch.\"","\"Yes, sir.\" The guards responded respectfully. After glancing at the approaching group, they got to work.","The Song family members, clad in plain, unremarkable travel robes—their sole advantage being their dirt-resistant nature—carried no distinctive insignia. After a brief appraisal, the group exchanged puzzled glances.","\"Hey! Who are you lot? Pretty bold, aren’t you? Just a handful of people daring to venture into this forest?\" a man in his thirties called out from behind.","Song Lingbo watched the guard birds at work, needing no further prompting. He turned his gaze to the group standing not far away, fixing his eyes on the middle-aged man leading them. \"With Captain Chai’s abilities, surely he doesn’t lack for meat? What’s the point of staring at us like that?\"","Hearing this, the middle-aged leader—who had been about to order his men forward—flinched slightly. He stared at the enigmatic middle-aged man before him, pondered for a moment, then asked, \"You know me?\""]},{"number":4998,"title":"Chapter 4998: Sit Down and Talk","paragraphs":["Chapter 4998: Sit Down and Talk","“I’ve heard of you, though I never imagined I’d have the honor of meeting you today.” Song Lingbo spoke, adjusting his robes as he spoke.","Hearing this, the Captain surnamed Chai narrowed his eyes, his mind racing. Someone who could identify his status at a glance—no ordinary person! But who could this individual be? Knowing about their mercenary group yet showing no fear—was it sheer courage, or was he putting on a brave front?","“May I ask your name?” Captain Chai, the leader, inquired, his gaze fixed on him.","“Song Lingbo.” He raised his hand in a fist salute.","“Culinary God Song!” The captain’s voice rose slightly, his surprise unmistakable.","“Father! We’re back!” Mi’er returned with the three children, carrying several unidentified items. Hao’er and the others helped carry some things, while the two guard birds behind them clutched branches they’d gathered.","Seeing them, Song Lingbo smiled. ” Stop running around. The fire’s already lit. Sit tight a bit longer, and you can have some soup first.”","Mi’er and the others approached, sizing up the group. They noticed that the forty or fifty members all carried a distinct scent of blood, and each bore a hint of savagery and bloodlust in their brows. The group couldn’t help but frown slightly, keeping their distance as they walked.","“Heh heh, Captain, word is Chef God Song Lingbo’s culinary skills are extraordinary. His dishes can replenish lost spirit energy and even enhance one’s strength to aid breakthroughs—practically like medicinal pills. Now that we’ve stumbled upon this, surely we wouldn’t pass up such a golden opportunity?”","A man approached, his voice hushed, eyes gleaming with excitement. His gaze swept over Song Mi’er and the three children with a hint of ruthlessness, deepening the smile on his face.","“Captain, look—they have a woman and three children. And there are only a handful of them...”","The implication was clear.","The captain, a man surnamed Chai, felt a stir within upon hearing this. Truth be told, the moment he learned that this person was the Culinary God Song Lingbo, the thought had crossed his mind. However, the Culinary God Song’s formidable strength had kept him from acting rashly. But if they captured the woman and the three children first, wouldn’t he have no choice but to comply?","“Culinary God Song, I’ve long admired your reputation.”","The Captain spoke, raising his hand in a bow as he stepped forward. Yet, the moment his words fell, he suddenly flung a net toward Song Mi’er and the three children standing nearby. The net closed in on them instantly, tightening so swiftly that the group, each holding something in their hands, couldn’t dodge in time.","“Ah!”","Song Mi’er gasped, dropping her belongings as she let go. She braced against the net with both hands, trying to pull it off, but it only tightened further.","Hao’er, Muchen, and Yue’er froze for a moment before their own items also fell to the ground. Trapped within the net, they were dragged toward the group, who swiftly surrounded them, trapping them in the center.","Seeing this, the three exchanged glances. They didn’t cry out, remaining silent.","Song Lingbo, enraged that he dared attack them even after knowing his identity, his expression darkening further, barked furiously, “Chai San! Release them!”","“Culinary God Song, no need for anger. Since we’ve met here by chance, why not sit down and talk?”"]},{"number":4999,"title":"Chapter 4999: Difficult Little Brats","paragraphs":["Chapter 4999: Difficult Little Brats","Chai San glanced at the ensnared figures, a smile spreading across his face.","“Chai San, if you release them now and get out of my sight, I’ll pretend this never happened. Otherwise, don’t blame me for being impolite!” Song Lingbo’s voice was calm yet firm.","“Heh, Culinary God Song, don’t you want them to be safe?” He laughed with confidence, his gaze shifting from the trapped figures to Song Lingbo. “I know Culinary God Song’s skills are formidable, and his knife work is nothing short of divine. If we faced you directly, even with our numbers, we’d struggle to match you. But with these people in my hands, unless Culinary God Song doesn’t want them to live, it’s best we talk.”","“Negotiate? Hmph! What exactly do you want to negotiate?” Song Lingbo snorted coldly. Lost in thought, he glanced toward the three children, their faces serene. The urgency between his brows gradually faded.","We’ve heard that what Culinary God Song creates is akin to an alchemist’s medicinal pills. Our request is simple: we want Culinary God Song to concoct something that can enhance our abilities. If Culinary God Song agrees, I, Chai, will naturally spare these children. If not... well...”","As the dagger sliced through the net, Hao’er and the other two, along with the two Jingwei and Mi’er, leapt free. Simultaneously, a cold voice emerged from Hao’er’s mouth.","“And if not, then what?”","The words barely left his lips when he lunged at Chai San with the dagger in his hand. His speed was like a shadow streaking past, leaving no time to react.","Whoosh!","A sharp blade of air sliced through the air, a bone-chilling aura carrying a cold, murderous intent. Chai San whipped his head around just in time to see a flash of cold steel streaking toward his throat. The overwhelming killing intent made him dodge without hesitation, narrowly avoiding the fatal strike. The blade, having missed his throat, twisted mid-air and slammed down into his shoulder.","“Gah! Aah!”","Agony surged through him as blood spurted forth. His instinctive cry of pain erupted as he raised his palm to strike. Nearby, Song Lingbo immediately stepped forward, grabbing Hao’er by the collar and pulling him behind her. Simultaneously, she gathered spirit energy in one hand to meet Chai San’s palm strike.","“Boom!”","The palms collided, unleashing a powerful blast of air that rippled outward from their contact points. Wind blades surged through the air. In that split second, both sides snapped out of their shock and swiftly launched attacks at each other, igniting a chaotic melee!","“Damn it! That brat!”","One mercenary had initially dismissed him as just a child, planning to deal with him first. But now he found the brat’s moves sharp and deadly, striking with lethal intent from the start. The mercenary was forced into a panicked retreat, step by step.","“Brat? I’m more than capable of killing you!” Muchen snorted coldly. Holding his dagger, he lunged forward at Du Qing’s side, aiming for the man’s vital points.","Meanwhile, Yue’er’s agile form leapt, evading several mercenaries’ attacks. She then swept her dagger horizontally at their lower bodies. Her small figure darted swiftly past them, and as she flashed by, the dagger in her hand would inevitably slash at their legs.","“Sss!”","“Ah!”","“My leg!”","“Damn it! If I catch you, brat!”","The mercenaries gasped in pain, trying to grab the tiny figure. But instead of catching her, each one ended up with wounded legs."]},{"number":5000,"title":"Chapter 5000: Melee","paragraphs":["Chapter 5000: Melee","Though the Song family’s forces were few, each fighter was capable of holding their own against ten opponents. Even the three younger members, Hao’er and the others, possessed combat prowess that could not be underestimated.","At that moment, a flying knife flashed through the air in Song Lingbo’s hand, slicing cleanly across Chai San’s throat. As he watched the man grunt and collapse, he looked up ahead. His gaze flickered uncontrollably. The words he’d intended to shout—a command for everyone to stop—got stuck in his throat, never forming.","Up ahead, guard and the others, along with Mi’er and the three children, were locked in fierce combat with the mercenaries. Setting guard aside for now, his gaze fell upon Mi’er and the children. Witnessing their astonishing combat prowess, his expression grew somewhat peculiar.","He knew his daughter well. While she was capable in combat, she certainly couldn’t take on three mercenaries alone. Yet here she was, moving with effortless ease, which surprised him.","As for the three children...","He knew they were disciples of the Azure Emperor, so their skills couldn’t be too shabby. Plus, they’d shown their hand a few times in the forest these past days, so he had some idea of their capabilities. But now, seeing them take on mercenaries with such decisive, clean strikes—that ruthless intensity was truly eye-opening!","The Song brothers had rushed back upon hearing the commotion, expecting trouble. Yet upon witnessing the scene, they froze. Turning to their father, they asked, “Father, what happened?”","“Wow! Who knew they were this strong!”","“That’s Chai San’s mercenary team. Just now...” He briefly explained the situation, paused, then added, “Though I’m not sure how it escalated to this.”","The scene before them had devolved into a one-sided massacre. As corpses piled up on the ground, the remaining dozen or so survivors fled frantically into the woods. They assumed the escapees would simply vanish, but the next moment...","“Lion! Drive them back to that monkey territory!” ”","Yue’er shouted. The moment her voice fell, a flash of light leapt forward. Perhaps to avoid startling the forest’s fierce beasts with its roar, the lion didn’t bellow upon emerging. Instead, it let out a low growl and gave chase after the fleeing dozen, driving them toward the area where the monkey corpses lay.","In this forest, the scent of blood was the surest lure for fierce beasts. With so many monkey corpses and the lingering stench of blood in that area, driving those people there meant they would meet a gruesome end without a single blow being struck!","Perhaps the shock they had already endured was too great. When the divine-tier lion appeared, the Song family members merely flashed their eyes briefly, saying nothing more, nor did they cry out in alarm.","As disciples of the Azure Emperor, possessing a divine-tier contract beast was hardly unusual. Without proper safeguards, the Azure Emperor likely wouldn’t have allowed them to travel unprotected.","“Arghhhh!”","Soon after, piercing screams echoed through the forest, mingled with beastly roars and desperate cries for help. The sounds grew fainter and fainter until they faded away entirely.","The lion watched from the thicket as the pack of fierce beasts tore the men apart. devouring their corpses in mere moments. After licking their lips, they glanced toward the Song family’s direction, seemingly detecting the scent of blood there. Just as they growled lowly and began striding forward to hunt, they suddenly retreated with alertness, their eyes fixed on the thicket with fear."]}]);
